const verses = [{"ref":"1.1","s":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच ।\nधर्मक्षेत्रे कुरुक्षेत्रे समवेता युयुत्सवः ।\nमामकाः पाण्डवाश्चैव किमकुर्वत सञ्जय ॥ १ ॥","t":"Dhritarashtra asked: Sanjaya, what did my sons and the sons of Pandu do after they gathered at the holy field of Kurukshetra, ready for battle?"},{"ref":"1.2","s":"सञ्जय उवाच ।\nदृष्ट्वा तु पाण्डवानीकं व्यूढं दुर्योधनस्तदा ।\nआचार्यमुपसङ्गम्य राजा वचनमब्रवीत् ॥ २ ॥","t":"Sanjaya said: After seeing the Pandava army in their battle formation, King Duryodhana went to his teacher Drona and said the following:"},{"ref":"1.3","s":"पश्यैतां पाण्डुपुत्राणामाचार्य महतीं चमूम् ।\nव्यूढां द्रुपदपुत्रेण तव शिष्येण धीमता ॥ ३ ॥","t":"Look, master, at this great army of Pandu's sons, arranged by your own talented student, the son of Drupada."},{"ref":"1.4","s":"अत्र शूरा महेष्वासा भीमार्जुनसमा युधि ।\nयुयुधानो विराटश्च द्रुपदश्च महारथः ॥ ४ ॥","t":"Here are heroes and great archers who are just as skilled in battle as Bhima and Arjuna — specifically Yuyudhana, Virata, and the great warrior Drupada;"},{"ref":"1.5","s":"धृष्टकेतुश्चेकितानः काशिराजश्च वीर्यवान् ।\nपुरुजित्कुन्तिभोजश्च शैब्यश्च नरपुङ्गवः ॥ ५ ॥","t":"Dhristaketu, Cekitana, and the brave king of Kashi; Purujit, Kuntibhoja, and Shaibya, who is a leader among men;"},{"ref":"1.6","s":"युधामन्युश्च विक्रान्त उत्तमौजाश्च वीर्यवान् ।\nसौभद्रो द्रौपदेयाश्च सर्व एव महारथाः ॥ ६ ॥","t":"The brave Yudhamanyu and the strong Uttamauja; the son of Subhadra and the sons of Draupadi — all of these are elite warriors."},{"ref":"1.7","s":"अस्माकं तु विशिष्टा ये तान्निबोध द्विजोत्तम ।\nनायका मम सैन्यस्य संज्ञार्थं तान्ब्रवीमि ते ॥ ७ ॥","t":"But also know the most distinguished leaders on our side, master. I will name them for you now, just for your information:"},{"ref":"1.8","s":"भवान्भीष्मश्च कर्णश्च कृपश्च समितिञ्जयः ।\nअश्वत्थामा विकर्णश्च सौमदत्तिस्तथैव च ॥ ८ ॥","t":"You yourself, and Bhishma, Karna, and the victorious Kripa; Ashvatthama, Vikarna, and also the son of Somadatta;"},{"ref":"1.9","s":"अन्ये च बहवः शूरा मदर्थे त्यक्तजीविताः ।\nनानाशस्त्रप्रहरणाः सर्वे युद्धविशारदाः ॥ ९ ॥","t":"And many other heroes have risked their lives for me, using many different types of weapons and being highly skilled in combat."},{"ref":"1.10","s":"अपर्याप्तं तदस्माकं बलं भीष्माभिरक्षितम् ।\nपर्याप्तं त्विदमेतेषां बलं भीमाभिरक्षितम् ॥ १० ॥","t":"Our army, protected by Bhishma, is unlimited and superior; their army, protected by Bhima, is limited and inferior."},{"ref":"1.11","s":"अयनेषु च सर्वेषु यथाभागमवस्थिताः ।\nभीष्ममेवाभिरक्षन्तु भवन्तः सर्व एव हि ॥ ११ ॥","t":"So, everyone should stay at their assigned posts in the various battle formations and make sure to protect Bhishma above everything else."},{"ref":"1.12","s":"तस्य सञ्जनयन्हर्षं कुरुवृद्धः पितामहः ।\nसिंहनादं विनद्योच्चैः शङ्खं दध्मौ प्रतापवान् ॥ १२ ॥","t":"Then the elderly grandfather of the Kurus, the powerful Bhishma, let out a roar like a lion and blew his conch shell loudly to cheer up Duryodhana."},{"ref":"1.13","s":"ततः शङ्खाश्च भेर्यश्च पणवानकगोमुखाः ।\nसहसैवाभ्यहन्यन्त स शब्दस्तुमुलोऽभवत् ॥ १३ ॥","t":"Immediately, conch shells, drums, and horns were all sounded at the same time, creating a massive, deafening noise."},{"ref":"1.14","s":"ततः श्वेतैर्हयैर्युक्ते महति स्यन्दने स्थितौ ।\nमाधवः पाण्डवश्चैव दिव्यौ शङ्खौ प्रदध्मतुः ॥ १४ ॥","t":"Then, Krishna and Arjuna, standing in their magnificent chariot pulled by white horses, also blew their divine conch shells."},{"ref":"1.15","s":"पाञ्चजन्यं हृषीकेशो देवदत्तं धनञ्जयः ।\nपौण्ड्रं दध्मौ महाशङ्खं भीमकर्मा वृकोदरः ॥ १५ ॥","t":"Krishna blew his conch named Panchajanya; Arjuna blew his, called Devadatta; and the mighty Bhima blew his enormous conch, Paundra."},{"ref":"1.16","s":"अनन्तविजयं राजा कुन्तीपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nनकुलः सहदेवश्च सुघोषमणिपुष्पकौ ॥ १६ ॥","t":"King Yudhishthira blew Anantavijaya; Nakula and Sahadeva blew the conches Sughosha and Manipushpaka."},{"ref":"1.17","s":"काश्यश्च परमेष्वासः शिखण्डी च महारथः ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नो विराटश्च सात्यकिश्चापराजितः ॥ १७ ॥","t":"The king of Kashi, a master archer; Shikhandi, the great warrior; Dhristadyumna, Virata, and the undefeated Satyaki;"},{"ref":"1.18","s":"द्रुपदो द्रौपदेयाश्च सर्वशः पृथिवीपते ।\nसौभद्रश्च महाबाहुः शङ्खान्दध्मुः पृथक्पृथक् ॥ १८ ॥","t":"Drupada, the sons of Draupadi, and the strong son of Subhadra all blew their conches from every side, O King."},{"ref":"1.19","s":"स घोषो धार्तराष्ट्राणां हृदयानि व्यदारयत् ।\nनभश्च पृथिवीं चैव तुमुलो व्यनुनादयन् ॥ १९ ॥","t":"That massive noise echoed through the sky and earth, and it shook the hearts of Dhritarashtra's sons."},{"ref":"1.20","s":"अथ व्यवस्थितान्दृष्ट्वा धार्तराष्ट्रान्कपिध्वजः ।\nप्रवृत्ते शस्त्रसम्पाते धनुरुद्यम्य पाण्डवः ।\nहृषीकेशं तदा वाक्यमिदमाह महीपते ॥ २० ॥","t":"Then, as the battle was just about to start, Arjuna (whose flag had a monkey on it) saw Dhritarashtra's sons ready for war. He picked up his bow and said these words to Krishna:"},{"ref":"1.21","s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nसेनयोरुभयोर्मध्ये रथं स्थापय मेऽच्युत ॥ २१ ॥","t":"Arjuna said: O Krishna (the immovable one), please stop my chariot right in the middle, between the two armies."},{"ref":"1.22","s":"यावदेतान्निरीक्षेऽहं योद्धुकामानवस्थितान् ।\nकैर्मया सह योद्धव्यमस्मिन्रणसमुद्यमे ॥ २२ ॥","t":"So that I can see all these people who have come here eager to fight, and know exactly who I must battle in this great conflict."},{"ref":"1.23","s":"योत्स्यमानानवेक्षेऽहं य एतेऽत्र समागताः ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रस्य दुर्बुद्धेर्युद्धे प्रियचिकीर्षवः ॥ २३ ॥","t":"I want to look at those who are ready to fight, who have gathered here to please the evil-minded son of Dhritarashtra."},{"ref":"1.24","s":"सञ्जय उवाच ।\nएवमुक्तो हृषीकेशो गुडाकेशेन भारत ।\nसेनयोरुभयोर्मध्ये स्थापयित्वा रथोत्तमम् ॥ २४ ॥","t":"Sanjaya said: After Arjuna spoke, Krishna drove that magnificent chariot and stopped it right in the middle, between the two armies."},{"ref":"1.25","s":"भीष्मद्रोणप्रमुखतः सर्वेषां च महीक्षिताम् ।\nउवाच पार्थ पश्यैतान्समवेतान्कुरूनिति ॥ २५ ॥","t":"Right in front of Bhishma, Drona, and all the kings, Krishna said: \"Arjuna, look at all these Kurus gathered here.\""},{"ref":"1.26","s":"तत्रापश्यत्स्थितान्पार्थः पितॄनथ पितामहान् ।\nआचार्यान्मातुलान्भ्रातॄन्पुत्रान्पौत्रान्सखींस्तथा ॥ २६ ॥","t":"There Arjuna saw his fathers, grandfathers, teachers, uncles, brothers, sons, grandsons, and friends all standing in the battle lines."},{"ref":"1.27","s":"श्वशुरान्सुहृदश्चैव सेनयोरुभयोरपि ।\nतान्समीक्ष्य स कौन्तेयः सर्वान्बन्धूनवस्थितान् ॥ २७ ॥","t":"He also saw fathers-in-law and well-wishers in both armies. Seeing all these relatives standing there together..."},{"ref":"1.28","s":"कृपया परयाविष्टो विषीदन्निदमब्रवीत् ।\nअर्जुन उवाच ।\nदृष्ट्वेमं स्वजनं कृष्ण युयुत्सुं समुपस्थितम् ॥ २८ ॥","t":"...Arjuna was filled with deep pity and sadness. He said: \"O Krishna, seeing my own people here, so eager to fight each other,\""},{"ref":"1.29","s":"सीदन्ति मम गात्राणि मुखं च परिशुष्यति ।\nवेपथुश्च शरीरे मे रोमहर्षश्च जायते ॥ २९ ॥","t":"\"My limbs are weak, my mouth is dry, my body is shaking, and my hair is standing on end.\""},{"ref":"1.30","s":"गाण्डीवं स्रंसते हस्तात्त्वक्चैव परिदह्यते ।\nन च शक्नोम्यवस्थातुं भ्रमतीव च मे मनः ॥ ३० ॥","t":"\"My bow Gandiva is slipping from my hand, my skin feels like it's burning, I can't stay still, and my mind is spinning.\""},{"ref":"1.31","s":"निमित्तानि च पश्यामि विपरीतानि केशव ।\nन च श्रेयोऽनुपश्यामि हत्वा स्वजनमाहवे ॥ ३१ ॥","t":"\"I see bad signs, Krishna, and I don't see any good coming from killing my own people in this battle.\""},{"ref":"1.32","s":"न काङ्क्षे विजयं कृष्ण न च राज्यं सुखानि च ।\nकिं नो राज्येन गोविन्द किं भोगैर्जीवितेन वा ॥ ३२ ॥","t":"\"I don't want victory, Krishna, nor a kingdom, nor any pleasures. What is the point of a kingdom, or enjoyments, or even life itself, if we have to do this?\""},{"ref":"1.33","s":"येषामर्थे काङ्क्षितं नो राज्यं भोगाः सुखानि च ।\nत इमेऽवस्थिता युद्धे प्राणांस्त्यक्त्वा धनानि च ॥ ३३ ॥","t":"\"The very people for whom we wanted a kingdom and wealth are now standing here in battle, ready to lose their lives and everything they own.\""},{"ref":"1.34","s":"आचार्याः पितरः पुत्रास्तथैव च पितामहः ।\nमातुलाः श्वशुराः पौत्राः स्यालाः सम्बन्धिनस्तथा ॥ ३४ ॥","t":"\"Teachers, fathers, sons, grandfathers, uncles, fathers-in-law, grandsons, brothers-in-law, and other relatives.\""},{"ref":"1.35","s":"एतान्न हन्तुमिच्छामि घ्नतोऽपि मधुसूदन ।\nअपि त्रैलोक्यराज्यस्य हेतोः किं नु महीकृते ॥ ३५ ॥","t":"\"I do not want to kill them, even if they kill me, not even for control over the entire universe, let alone for just this earth.\""},{"ref":"1.36","s":"निहत्य धार्तराष्ट्रान्नः का प्रीतिः स्याज्जनार्दन ।\nपापमेवाश्रयेदस्मान्हत्वैतानाततायिनः ॥ ३६ ॥","t":"\"What happiness would we find in killing Dhritarashtra's sons? Even if they are aggressors, only bad things would come to us from killing them.\""},{"ref":"1.37","s":"तस्मान्नार्हा वयं हन्तुं धार्तराष्ट्रान्स्वबान्धवान् ।\nस्वजनं हि कथं हत्वा सुखिनः स्याम माधव ॥ ३७ ॥","t":"\"Therefore, we should not kill Dhritarashtra's sons, our own relatives. How can we ever be happy after killing our own people, Krishna?\""},{"ref":"1.38","s":"यद्यप्येते न पश्यन्ति लोभोपहतचेतसः ।\nकुलक्षयकृतं दोषं मित्रद्रोहे च पातकम् ॥ ३८ ॥","t":"\"Even if they don't see anything wrong with destroying a family or betraying friends because they are blinded by greed—\""},{"ref":"1.39","s":"कथं न ज्ञेयमस्माभिः पापादस्मान्निवर्तितुम् ।\nकुलक्षयकृतं दोषं प्रपश्यद्भिर्जनार्दन ॥ ३९ ॥","t":"\"—why shouldn't we, who actually see the wrong in destroying a family, be wise enough to walk away from this evil?\""},{"ref":"1.40","s":"कुलक्षये प्रणश्यन्ति कुलधर्माः सनातनाः ।\nधर्मे नष्टे कुलं कृत्स्नमधर्मोऽभिभवत्युत ॥ ४० ॥","t":"\"When a family is destroyed, its ancient traditions and duties also disappear. Without these duties, the whole family falls into lawlessness.\""},{"ref":"1.41","s":"अधर्माभिभवात्कृष्ण प्रदुष्यन्ति कुलस्त्रियः ।\nस्त्रीषु दुष्टासु वार्ष्णेय जायते वर्णसङ्करः ॥ ४१ ॥","t":"\"When lawlessness takes over, Krishna, the women of the family are harmed. When this happens, there is a mixing of social classes and values.\""},{"ref":"1.42","s":"सङ्करो नरकायैव कुलघ्नानां कुलस्य च ।\nपतन्ति पितरो ह्येषां लुप्तपिण्डोदकक्रियाः ॥ ४२ ॥","t":"\"This confusion leads to ruin for everyone. Even the ancestors are forgotten because no one is left to honor them.\""},{"ref":"1.43","s":"दोषैरेतैः कुलघ्नानां वर्णसङ्करकारकैः ।\nउत्साद्यन्ते जातिधर्माः कुलधर्माश्च शाश्वताः ॥ ४३ ॥","t":"\"Because of these wrongs, the lasting duties of our community and family are completely destroyed.\""},{"ref":"1.44","s":"उत्सन्नकुलधर्माणां मनुष्याणां जनार्दन ।\nनरकेऽनियतं वासो भवतीत्यनुशुश्रुम ॥ ४४ ॥","t":"\"We have heard that for those who destroy their family duties, Krishna, a long stay in a state of suffering (hell) is certain.\""},{"ref":"1.45","s":"अहो बत महत्पापं कर्तुं व्यवसिता वयम् ।\nयद्राज्यसुखलोभेन हन्तुं स्वजनमुद्यताः ॥ ४५ ॥","t":"\"Alas! We are about to commit a huge crime. Because of our greed for power and pleasure, we are ready to kill our own family.\""},{"ref":"1.46","s":"यदि मामप्रतीकारमशस्त्रं शस्त्रपाणयः ।\nधार्तराष्ट्र रणे हन्युस्तन्मे क्षेमतरं भवेत् ॥ ४६ ॥","t":"\"It would be better for me if Dhritarashtra's sons killed me in battle while I was unarmed and didn't fight back.\""},{"ref":"1.47","s":"सञ्जय उवाच ।\nएवमुक्त्वार्जुनः सङ्ख्ये रथोपस्थ उपाविशत् ।\nविसृज्य सशरं चापं शोकसंविग्नमानसः ॥ ४७ ॥","t":"Sanjaya said: Having said this on the battlefield, Arjuna sat down in his chariot and threw down his bow and arrows, his heart filled with grief."},{"ref":"2.1","s":"सञ्जय उवाच ।\nतं तथा कृपयाविष्टमश्रुपूर्णाकुलेक्षणम् ।\nविषीदन्तमिदं वाक्यमुवाच मधुसूदनः ॥ १ ॥","t":"Sanjaya said: To Arjuna, who was overwhelmed with pity and whose eyes were filled with tears of despair, Krishna spoke these words:"},{"ref":"2.2","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nकुतस्त्वा कश्मलमिदं विषमे समुपस्थितम् ।\nअनार्यजुष्टमस्वर्ग्यमकीर्तिकरमर्जुन ॥ २ ॥","t":"The Blessed One said: Arjuna, where did this weakness come from at such a critical moment? It is not worthy of a noble person; it does not lead to a higher state and only brings disgrace."},{"ref":"2.3","s":"क्लैब्यं मा स्म गमः पार्थ नैतत्त्वय्युपपद्यते ।\nक्षुद्रं हृदयदौर्बल्यं त्यक्त्वोत्तिष्ठ परन्तप ॥ ३ ॥","t":"Do not give in to this weakness, Arjuna; it doesn't suit you. Cast off this small-heartedness and stand up, you conqueror of obstacles."},{"ref":"2.4","s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nकथं भीष्ममहं सङ्ख्ये द्रोणं च मधुसूदन ।\nइषुभिः प्रतियोत्स्यामि पूजार्हावरिसूदन ॥ ४ ॥","t":"Arjuna asked: Krishna, how can I attack Bhishma and Drona with arrows in this battle? They are both worthy of my deepest respect."},{"ref":"2.5","s":"गुरूनहत्वा हि महानुभावान्\nश्रेयो भोक्तुं भैक्ष्यमपीह लोके ।\nहत्वार्थकामांस्तु गुरूनिहैव\nभुञ्जीय भोगान् रुधिरप्रदिग्धान् ॥ ५ ॥","t":"It would be better to live on charity in this world than to kill these noble teachers. If I kill them, any wealth or pleasure I gain will be stained with their blood."},{"ref":"2.6","s":"न चैतद्विद्मः कतरन्नो गरीयो\nयद्वा जयेम यदि वा नो जयेयुः ।\nयानेव हत्वा न जिजीविषामस्\nतेऽवस्थिताः प्रमुखे धार्तराष्ट्राः ॥ ६ ॥","t":"We don't even know which is better: for us to win or for them to win. The very people we don't want to live without are now standing before us as enemies."},{"ref":"2.7","s":"कार्पण्यदोषोपहतस्वभावः\nपृच्छामि त्वां धर्मसम्मूढचेताः ।\nयच्छ्रेयः स्यान्निश्चितं ब्रूहि तन्मे\nशिष्यस्तेऽहं शाधि मां त्वां प्रपन्नम् ॥ ७ ॥","t":"I am confused about my duty and paralyzed by this feeling of pity. I ask you: tell me for certain what is best for me. I am your student; please guide me, as I have come to you for help."},{"ref":"2.8","s":"न हि प्रपश्यामि ममापनुद्याद्\nयच्छोकमुच्छोषणमिन्द्रियाणाम् ।\nअवाप्य भूमावसपत्नमृद्धं\nराज्यं सुराणामपि चाधिपत्यम् ॥ ८ ॥","t":"I don't see anything that could remove this grief that is draining me—even if I gained complete and wealthy control over the whole world, or even over the gods."},{"ref":"2.9","s":"सञ्जय उवाच ।\nएवमुक्त्वा हृषीकेशं गुडाकेशः परन्तपः ।\nन योत्स्य इति गोविन्दमुक्त्वा तूष्णीं बभूव ह ॥ ९ ॥","t":"Sanjaya said: After saying this to Krishna, Arjuna (the conqueror of obstacles) said \"I will not fight,\" and then he became silent."},{"ref":"2.10","s":"तमुवाच हृषीकेशः प्रहसन्निव भारत ।\nसेनयोरुभयोर्मध्ये विषीदन्तमिदं वचः ॥ १० ॥","t":"Krishna, as if smiling, spoke these words to the despondent Arjuna right there in the middle of the two armies:"},{"ref":"2.11","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nअशोच्यानन्वशोचस्त्वं प्रज्ञावादांश्च भाषसे ।\nगतासूनगतासूंश्च नानुशोचन्ति पण्डिताः ॥ ११ ॥","t":"The Blessed One said: You are grieving for people who don't need your grief, even though you sound like you are speaking wisely. Those who truly understand reality do not grieve for the dead or the living."},{"ref":"2.12","s":"न त्वेवाहं जातु नासं न त्वं नेमे जनाधिपाः ।\nन चैव न भविष्यामः सर्वे वयमतः परम् ॥ १२ ॥","t":"There was never a time when I, or you, or all these kings didn't exist. And none of us will ever stop existing in the future."},{"ref":"2.13","s":"देहिनोऽस्मिन्यथा देहे कौमारं यौवनं जरा ।\nतथा देहान्तरप्राप्तिर्धीरस्तत्र न मुह्यति ॥ १३ ॥","t":"Just as the soul in this body goes through childhood, youth, and old age, it also moves into another body after death. A steady person is not confused by this natural process."},{"ref":"2.14","s":"मात्रास्पर्शास्तु कौन्तेय शीतोष्णसुखदुःखदाः ।\nआगमापायिनोऽनित्यास्तांस्तितिक्षस्व भारत ॥ १४ ॥","t":"The interaction of your senses with the world creates feelings like heat and cold, or pleasure and pain. These feelings come and go and are only temporary. You must learn to endure them, Arjuna."},{"ref":"2.15","s":"यं हि न व्यथयन्त्येते पुरुषं पुरुषर्षभ ।\nसमदुःखसुखं धीरं सोऽमृतत्वाय कल्पते ॥ १५ ॥","t":"The person who is not disturbed by these changes, who remains steady in both pain and pleasure, is ready for a state of eternal peace."},{"ref":"2.16","s":"नासतो विद्यते भावो नाभावो विद्यते सतः ।\nउभयोरपि दृष्टोऽन्तस्त्वनयोस्तत्त्वदर्शिभिः ॥ १६ ॥","t":"What is not real has no lasting existence, and what is real can never stop existing. Those who see the truth have understood the difference between these two."},{"ref":"2.17","s":"अविनाशि तु तद्विद्धि येन सर्वमिदं ततम् ।\nविनाशमव्ययस्यास्य न कश्चित्कर्तुमर्हति ॥ १७ ॥","t":"Understand that the essence which spreads through everything is indestructible. No one can destroy this unchanging reality."},{"ref":"2.18","s":"अन्तवन्त इमे देहा नित्यस्योक्ताः शरीरिणः ।\nअनाशिनोऽप्रमेयस्य तस्माद्युध्यस्व भारत ॥ १८ ॥","t":"Only these bodies have an end; the soul within them is eternal, indestructible, and beyond measure. Therefore, do your duty and fight, Arjuna."},{"ref":"2.19","s":"य एनं वेत्ति हन्तारं यश्चैनं मन्यते हतम् ।\nउभौ तौ न विजानीतो नायं हन्ति न हन्यते ॥ १९ ॥","t":"Anyone who thinks the soul can kill or be killed is mistaken. It neither kills nor is it ever killed."},{"ref":"2.20","s":"न जायते म्रियते वा कदाचिन्\nनायं भूत्वा भविता वा न भूयः ।\nअजो नित्यः शाश्वतोऽयं पुराणो\nन हन्यते हन्यमाने शरीरे ॥ २० ॥","t":"The soul is never born and never dies. It didn't come into being at some point, nor will it ever stop being. It is unborn, eternal, and ancient; it is not destroyed even when the body is destroyed."},{"ref":"2.21","s":"वेदाविनाशिनं नित्यं य एनमजमव्ययम् ।\nकथं स पुरुषः पार्थ कं घातयति हन्ति कम् ॥ २१ ॥","t":"Pārtha, anyone who knows the soul to be indestructible, eternal, unborn, and unchanging—how can that person kill anyone, or cause anyone to be killed?"},{"ref":"2.22","s":"वासांसि जीर्णानि यथा विहाय\nनवानि गृह्णाति नरोऽपराणि ।\nतथा शरीराणि विहाय जीर्णान्य्\nअन्यानि संयाति नवानि देही ॥ २२ ॥","t":"Just as a person throws away old, worn-out clothes and puts on new ones, the soul casts off old, useless bodies and enters new ones."},{"ref":"2.23","s":"नैनं छिन्दन्ति शस्त्राणि नैनं दहति पावकः ।\nन चैनं क्लेदयन्त्यापो न शोषयति मारुतः ॥ २३ ॥","t":"Weapons cannot cut the soul, fire cannot burn it, water cannot wet it, and wind cannot dry it out."},{"ref":"2.24","s":"अच्छेद्योऽयमदाह्योऽयमक्लेद्योऽशोष्य एव च ।\nनित्यः सर्वगतः स्थाणुरचलोऽयं सनातनः ॥ २४ ॥","t":"The soul is impossible to cut, burn, wet, or dry. It is eternal, present everywhere, stable, unmoving, and ever-lasting."},{"ref":"2.25","s":"अव्यक्तोऽयमचिन्त्योऽयमविकार्योऽयमुच्यते ।\nतस्मादेवं विदित्वैनं नानुशोचितुमर्हसि ॥ २५ ॥","t":"The soul is said to be invisible, beyond human thought, and unchangeable. Therefore, knowing it to be this way, you should not grieve."},{"ref":"2.26","s":"अथ चैनं नित्यजातं नित्यं वा मन्यसे मृतम् ।\nतथापि त्वं महाबाहो नैवं शोचितुमर्हसि ॥ २६ ॥","t":"And even if you think the soul is born and dies over and over again, even then, O mighty warrior, you have no reason to grieve."},{"ref":"2.27","s":"जातस्य हि ध्रुवो मृत्युर्ध्रुवं जन्म मृतस्य च ।\nतस्मादपरिहार्येऽर्थे न त्वं शोचितुमर्हसि ॥ २७ ॥","t":"For anyone who is born, death is certain; and for anyone who dies, birth is certain. Therefore, you should not grieve over what is unavoidable."},{"ref":"2.28","s":"अव्यक्तादीनि भूतानि व्यक्तमध्यानि भारत ।\nअव्यक्तनिधनान्येव तत्र का परिदेवना ॥ २८ ॥","t":"Beings are invisible before birth, visible during their lives, and invisible again after death, Arjuna. So what is there to cry about in this?"},{"ref":"2.29","s":"आश्चर्यवत्पश्यति कश्चिदेनम्\nआश्चर्यवद्वदति तथैव चान्यः ।\nआश्चर्यवच्चैनमन्यः शृणोति\nश्रुत्वाप्येनं वेद न चैव कश्चित् ॥ २९ ॥","t":"Someone sees this soul as a wonder, another speaks of it as a wonder, and another hears of it as a wonder. Yet, even after hearing about it, no one truly understands it."},{"ref":"2.30","s":"देही नित्यमवध्योऽयं देहे सर्वस्य भारत ।\nतस्मात्सर्वाणि भूतानि न त्वं शोचितुमर्हसि ॥ ३० ॥","t":"The soul that lives in the body of every being is eternally safe from harm, Arjuna. Therefore, you should not grieve for any living thing."},{"ref":"2.31","s":"स्वधर्ममपि चावेक्ष्य न विकम्पितुमर्हसि ।\nधर्म्याद्धि युद्धाच्छ्रेयोऽन्यत्क्षत्रियस्य न विद्यते ॥ ३१ ॥","t":"Looking at your own duty (dharma), you should not hesitate. For a person of your position (a kṣatriya), there is nothing better than a righteous fight for a just cause."},{"ref":"2.32","s":"यदृच्छया चोपपन्नं स्वर्गद्वारमपावृतम् ।\nसुखिनः क्षत्रियाः पार्थ लभन्ते युद्धमीदृशम् ॥ ३२ ॥","t":"Pārtha, fortunate are those who find themselves facing such a battle that comes of its own accord—it is like an open door to a higher state of existence."},{"ref":"2.33","s":"अथ चेत्त्वमिमं धर्म्यं सङ्ग्रामं न करिष्यसि ।\nततः स्वधर्मं कीर्तिं च हित्वा पापमवाप्स्यसि ॥ ३३ ॥","t":"But if you do not fight this righteous battle, you will be abandoning your duty and your honor, and you will incur the consequences of that failure."},{"ref":"2.34","s":"अकीर्तिं चापि भूतानि कथयिष्यन्ति तेऽव्ययाम् ।\nसम्भावितस्य चाकीर्तिर्मरणादतिरिच्यते ॥ ३४ ॥","t":"People will speak of your disgrace for a long time. For someone who has been respected, dishonor is actually worse than death."},{"ref":"2.35","s":"भयाद्रणादुपरतं मंस्यन्ते त्वां महारथाः ।\nयेषां च त्वं बहुमतो भूत्वा यास्यसि लाघवम् ॥ ३५ ॥","t":"The great warriors will think you left the battle because you were afraid. Those who used to respect you will now look down on you."},{"ref":"2.36","s":"अवाच्यवादांश्च बहून्वदिष्यन्ति तवाहिताः ।\nनिन्दन्तस्तव सामर्थ्यं ततो दुःखतरं नु किम् ॥ ३६ ॥","t":"Your enemies will say many hurtful things and mock your skills. What could be more painful than having your competence and courage insulted?"},{"ref":"2.37","s":"हतो वा प्राप्स्यसि स्वर्गं जित्वा वा भोक्ष्यसे महीम् ।\nतस्मादुत्तिष्ठ कौन्तेय युद्धाय कृतनिश्चयः ॥ ३७ ॥","t":"If you are killed, you will reach a higher state; if you win, you will enjoy success in this world. Therefore, stand up, Arjuna, and be resolved to do your duty."},{"ref":"2.38","s":"सुखदुःखे समे कृत्वा लाभालाभौ जयाजयौ ।\nततो युद्धाय युज्यस्व नैवं पापमवाप्स्यसि ॥ ३८ ॥","t":"Treat pleasure and pain, gain and loss, victory and defeat as the same. Then prepare for battle. If you act this way, you will not incur any wrong."},{"ref":"2.39","s":"एषा तेऽभिहिता साङ्ख्ये बुद्धिर्योगे त्विमां शृणु ।\nबुद्ध्या युक्तो यया पार्थ कर्मबन्धं प्रहास्यसि ॥ ३९ ॥","t":"This is the analytical understanding (Sāṅkhya) I have given you. Now, listen to the practical discipline (Yoga). When you act with this understanding, you will be free from the burden of your actions."},{"ref":"2.40","s":"नेहाभिक्रमनाशोऽस्ति प्रत्यवायो न विद्यते ।\nस्वल्पमप्यस्य धर्मस्य त्रायते महतो भयात् ॥ ४० ॥","t":"In this path, no effort is ever wasted, and there are no negative side-effects. Even a small amount of this practice protects you from great fear."},{"ref":"2.41","s":"व्यवसायात्मिका बुद्धिरेकेह कुरुनन्दन ।\nबहुशाखा ह्यनन्ताश्च बुद्धयोऽव्यवसायिनाम् ॥ ४१ ॥","t":"A resolute mind is focused on a single point, Arjuna. But the minds of those who lack resolve are scattered in many directions and endless thoughts."},{"ref":"2.42","s":"यामिमां पुष्पितां वाचं प्रवदन्त्यविपश्चितः ।\nवेदवादरताः पार्थ नान्यदस्तीति वादिनः ॥ ४२ ॥","t":"People who lack deep understanding are carried away by flowery words and literal interpretations of scriptures, claiming there is nothing more to reality than these rules."},{"ref":"2.43","s":"कामात्मानः स्वर्गपरा जन्मकर्मफलप्रदाम् ।\nक्रियाविशेषबहुलां भोगैश्वर्यगतिं प्रति ॥ ४३ ॥","t":"Driven by desire and seeking only pleasure and power, they perform complex rituals hoping for rewards in this life or the next."},{"ref":"2.44","s":"भोगैश्वर्यप्रसक्तानां तयापहृतचेतसाम् ।\nव्यवसायात्मिका बुद्धिः समाधौ न विधीयते ॥ ४४ ॥","t":"Those who are attached to enjoyment and power, and whose minds are stolen by such flowery words, can never achieve a steady, resolute mind in deep focus."},{"ref":"2.45","s":"त्रैगुण्यविषया वेदा निस्त्रैगुण्यो भवार्जुन ।\nनिर्द्वन्द्वो नित्यसत्त्वस्थो निर्योगक्षेम आत्मवान् ॥ ४५ ॥","t":"The scriptures deal with the three qualities of nature. Rise above these qualities, Arjuna. Be free from dualities, stay established in purity, let go of the need to acquire or protect things, and stay focused on your true self."},{"ref":"2.46","s":"यावानर्थ उदपाने सर्वतः सम्प्लुतोदके ।\nतावान्सर्वेषु वेदेषु ब्राह्मणस्य विजानतः ॥ ४६ ॥","t":"To someone who has realized the ultimate truth, the formal rules of scripture are as useful as a small well is when there is a flood of water everywhere."},{"ref":"2.47","s":"कर्मण्येवाधिकारस्ते मा फलेषु कदाचन ।\nमा कर्मफलहेतुर्भूर्मा ते सङ्गोऽस्त्वकर्मणि ॥ ४७ ॥","t":"You have a right to your work, but never to the results of your work. Do not let the reward be your motivation, but also do not be attached to doing nothing."},{"ref":"2.48","s":"योगस्थः कुरु कर्माणि सङ्गं त्यक्त्वा धनञ्जय ।\nसिद्ध्यसिद्ध्योः समो भूत्वा समत्वं योग उच्यते ॥ ४८ ॥","t":"Do your work while being established in a state of balance (Yoga), letting go of attachment. Remain the same in both success and failure. This state of mental evenness is called Yoga."},{"ref":"2.49","s":"दूरेण ह्यवरं कर्म बुद्धियोगाद्धनञ्जय ।\nबुद्धौ शरणमन्विच्छ कृपणाः फलहेतवः ॥ ४९ ॥","t":"Mere action is far inferior to the action performed with clear understanding. Seek refuge in wisdom. Those who act only for rewards are narrow-minded and pitiable."},{"ref":"2.50","s":"बुद्धियुक्तो जहातीह उभे सुकृतदुष्कृते ।\nतस्माद्योगाय युज्यस्व योगः कर्मसु कौशलम् ॥ ५० ॥","t":"A person with a clear understanding rises above the concepts of 'good' and 'evil' deeds in this world. Therefore, commit yourself to Yoga. Yoga is defined as skill in action."},{"ref":"2.51","s":"कर्मजं बुद्धियुक्ता हि फलं त्यक्त्वा मनीषिणः ।\nजन्मबन्धविनिर्मुक्ताः पदं गच्छन्त्यनामयम् ॥ ५१ ॥","t":"Wise people, who are focused on clear understanding and have let go of the rewards of their actions, are freed from the cycle of birth and death and reach a state that is completely free from suffering."},{"ref":"2.52","s":"यदा ते मोहकलिलं बुद्धिर्व्यतितरिष्यति ।\nतदा गन्तासि निर्वेदं श्रोतव्यस्य श्रुतस्य च ॥ ५2 ॥","t":"When your understanding moves beyond the confusion of delusion, you will become indifferent to all the conflicting opinions and theories you have ever heard or will ever hear."},{"ref":"2.53","s":"श्रुतिविप्रतिपन्ना ते यदा स्थास्यति निश्चला ।\nसमाधावचला बुद्धिस्तदा योगमवाप्स्यसि ॥ ५३ ॥","t":"When your mind, which has been confused by various conflicting teachings, becomes steady and unmoving in deep focus, then you will have achieved true Yoga."},{"ref":"2.54","s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nस्थितप्रज्ञस्य का भाषा समाधिस्थस्य केशव ।\nस्थितधीः किं प्रभाषेत किमासीत व्रजेत किम् ॥ ५४ ॥","t":"Arjuna asked: Krishna, what are the characteristics of a person whose wisdom is steady and who is established in deep focus? How does such a person speak, sit, and move in the world?"},{"ref":"2.55","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nप्रजहाति यदा कामान्सर्वान्पार्थ मनोगतान् ।\nआत्मन्येवात्मना तुष्टः स्थितप्रज्ञस्तदोच्यते ॥ ५५ ॥","t":"The Blessed One said: When a person lets go of all the selfish desires in their mind and finds complete satisfaction within themselves, then that person is said to have steady wisdom."},{"ref":"2.56","s":"दुःखेष्वनुद्विग्नमनाः सुखेषु विगतस्पृहः ।\nवीतरागभयक्रोधः स्थितधीर्मुनिरुच्यते ॥ ५६ ॥","t":"One who is not disturbed by sorrow, who doesn't crave pleasure, and who is free from attachment, fear, and anger—such a person is called a sage of steady mind."},{"ref":"2.57","s":"यः सर्वत्रानभिस्नेहस्तत्तत्प्राप्य शुभाशुभम् ।\nनाभिनन्दति न द्वेष्टि तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता ॥ ५७ ॥","t":"Anyone who is not attached to anything, who meets both good and bad things without getting over-excited or becoming hateful, has truly steady wisdom."},{"ref":"2.58","s":"यदा संहरते चायं कूर्मोऽङ्गानीव सर्वशः ।\nइन्द्रियाणीन्द्रियार्थेभ्यस्तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता ॥ ५८ ॥","t":"Just as a tortoise pulls its limbs into its shell, a person of steady wisdom can withdraw their senses from the distractions of the world at will."},{"ref":"2.59","s":"विषया विनिवर्तन्ते निराहारस्य देहिनः ।\nरसवर्जं रसोऽप्यस्य परं दृष्ट्वा निवर्तते ॥ ५९ ॥","t":"If you stop indulging your senses, the objects of desire may go away, but the 'craving' for them remains. This craving only disappears when you experience a higher, more fulfilling reality."},{"ref":"2.60","s":"यततो ह्यपि कौन्तेय पुरुषस्य विपश्चितः ।\nइन्द्रियाणि प्रमाथीनि हरन्ति प्रसभं मनः ॥ ६० ॥","t":"Arjuna, the senses are so powerful and turbulent that they can forcibly carry away the mind of even a wise person who is trying their best to control them."},{"ref":"2.61","s":"तानि सर्वाणि संयम्य युक्त आसीत मत्परः ।\nवशे हि यस्येन्द्रियाणि तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता ॥ ६१ ॥","t":"A person should control all their senses and stay focused on the highest reality. One who has their senses under control truly has steady wisdom."},{"ref":"2.62","s":"ध्यायतो विषयान्पुंसः सङ्गस्तेषूपजायते ।\nसङ्गात्सञ्जायते कामः कामात्क्रोधोऽभिजायते ॥ ६२ ॥","t":"When you keep thinking about things you want, you become attached to them. This attachment turns into a strong craving, and when that craving is blocked, it turns into anger."},{"ref":"2.63","s":"क्रोधाद्भवति सम्मोहः सम्मोहात्स्मृतिविभ्रमः ।\nस्मृतिभ्रंशाद्बुद्धिनाशो बुद्धिनाशात्प्रणश्यति ॥ ६३ ॥","t":"Anger leads to delusion, and delusion makes you forget what you have learned. When your memory is confused, your ability to reason is destroyed. And when you lose your reason, you are completely lost."},{"ref":"2.64","s":"रागद्वेषवियुक्तैस्तु विषयानिन्द्रियैश्चरन् ।\nआत्मवश्यैर्विधेयात्मा प्रसादमधिगच्छति ॥ ६४ ॥","t":"But a self-controlled person, who moves through the world with senses free from both attraction and dislike, reaches a state of internal clarity and peace."},{"ref":"2.65","s":"प्रसादे सर्वदुःखानां हानिरस्योपजायते ।\nप्रसन्नचेतसो ह्याशु बुद्धिः पर्यवतिष्ठते ॥ ६५ ॥","t":"In this state of internal clarity, all sorrows disappear. For someone with a clear mind, wisdom quickly becomes stable and permanent."},{"ref":"2.66","s":"नास्ति बुद्धिरयुक्तस्य न चायुक्तस्य भावना ।\nन चाभावयतः शान्तिरशान्तस्य कुतः सुखम् ॥ ६६ ॥","t":"An undisciplined person has no real understanding and no ability to focus. Without focus, there is no peace; and without peace, how can there be any happiness?"},{"ref":"2.67","s":"इन्द्रियाणं हि चरतां यन्मनोऽनुविधीयते ।\nतदस्य हरति प्रज्ञां वायुर्नावमिवाम्भसि ॥ ६७ ॥","t":"If your mind constantly follows your wandering senses, it will sweep away your wisdom just as a strong wind blows a boat off its course on the water."},{"ref":"2.68","s":"तस्माद्यस्य महाबाहो निगृहीतानि सर्वशः ।\nइन्द्रियाणीन्द्रियार्थेभ्यस्तस्य प्रज्ञा प्रतिष्ठिता ॥ ६८ ॥","t":"Therefore, Arjuna, one who has completely pulled back their senses from the distractions of the world has truly steady wisdom."},{"ref":"2.69","s":"या निशा सर्वभूतानां तस्यां जागर्ति संयमी ।\nयस्यां जाग्रति भूतानि सा निशा पश्यतो मुनेः ॥ ६९ ॥","t":"What most people see as 'darkness' (internal growth, self-control), the wise person sees as 'light.' And what most people see as 'light' (material chasing, sensory pleasure), the wise person sees as 'darkness.'"},{"ref":"2.70","s":"आपूर्यमाणमचलप्रतिष्ठं\nसमुद्रमापः प्रविशन्ति यद्वत् ।\nतद्वत्कामा यं प्रविशन्ति सर्वे\nस शान्तिमाप्नोति न कामकामी ॥ ७० ॥","t":"Just as the ocean stays still even though many rivers flow into it, a wise person remains peaceful even though many desires and thoughts enter their mind. Peace is for such a person, not for someone who chases after every desire."},{"ref":"2.71","s":"विहाय कामान्यः सर्वान्पुमांश्चरति निःस्पृहः ।\nनिर्ममो निरहङ्कारः स शान्तिमधिगच्छति ॥ ७१ ॥","t":"The person who lives without selfish desires, without craving, without 'mine and yours,' and without ego—that person reaches true peace."},{"ref":"2.72","s":"एषा ब्राह्मी स्थितिः पार्थ नैनां प्राप्य विमुह्यति ।\nस्थित्वास्यामन्तकालेऽपि ब्रह्मनिर्वाणमृच्छति ॥ ७२ ॥","t":"This is the state of ultimate reality, Arjuna. Once you reach it, you are never confused again. If you stay in this state, even at the moment of death, you reach eternal freedom."},{"ref":"3.1","s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nज्यायसी चेत्कर्मणस्ते मता बुद्धिर्जनार्दन ।\nतत्किं कर्मणि घोरे मां नियोजयसि केशव ॥ १ ॥","t":"Arjuna asked: Krishna, if you think that clear understanding is better than action, then why are you pushing me to do this violent and terrible work?"},{"ref":"3.2","s":"व्यामिश्रेणेव वाक्येन बुद्धिं मोहयसीव मे ।\nतदेकं वद निश्चित्य येन श्रेयोऽहमाप्नुयाम् ॥ २ ॥","t":"Your words are confusing me. Please tell me clearly and specifically the one path I should follow to reach the highest good."},{"ref":"3.3","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nलोकेऽस्मिन्द्विविधा निष्ठा पुरा प्रोक्ता मयानघ ।\nज्ञानयोगेन सांख्यानां कर्मयोगेन योगिनाम् ॥ ३ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: Arjuna, I have previously described two paths for finding balance in this world: the path of analytical knowledge for those who are contemplative, and the path of selfless action for those who are active."},{"ref":"3.4","s":"न कर्मणामनारम्भान्नैष्कर्म्यं पुरुषोऽश्नुते ।\nन च संन्यसनादेव सिद्धिं समधिगच्छति ॥ ४ ॥","t":"You don't achieve 'freedom from work' just by refusing to start any tasks. And you don't reach perfection simply by quitting your job or responsibilities."},{"ref":"3.5","s":"न हि कश्चित्क्षणमपि जातु तिष्ठत्यकर्मकृत् ।\nकार्यते ह्यवशः कर्म सर्वः प्रकृतिजैर्गुणैः ॥ ५ ॥","t":"No one can stay completely inactive for even a single second. Everyone is forced to act by the natural forces and traits they were born with."},{"ref":"3.6","s":"कर्मेन्द्रियाणि संयम्य य आस्ते मनसा स्मरन् ।\nइन्द्रियार्थान्विमूढात्मा मिथ्याचारः स उच्यते ॥ ६ ॥","t":"Someone who stops their physical body from acting, but keeps obsessing about desires in their mind, is a confused hypocrite."},{"ref":"3.7","s":"यस्त्विन्द्रियाणि मनसा नियम्यारभतेऽर्जुन ।\nकर्मेन्द्रियैः कर्मयोगमसक्तः स विशिष्यते ॥ ७ ॥","t":"But the person who uses their mind to control their senses and performs their work with their body without being attached to the outcome—that person is truly outstanding."},{"ref":"3.8","s":"नियतं कुरु कर्म त्वं कर्म ज्यायो ह्यकर्मणः ।\nशरीरयात्रापि च ते न प्रसिद्धयेदकर्मणः ॥ ८ ॥","t":"Do the work you are supposed to do, because acting is better than not acting. You couldn't even keep your own body alive if you stopped all action."},{"ref":"3.9","s":"यज्ञार्थात्कर्मणोऽन्यत्र लोकोऽयं कर्मबन्धनः ।\nतदर्थं कर्म कौन्तेय मुक्तसङ्गः समाचर ॥ ९ ॥","t":"Any work done for a selfish reason creates a burden (bondage). But work done as a contribution or sacrifice (Yajña) is free. Therefore, Arjuna, do your work as a contribution, without being attached to what you get from it."},{"ref":"3.10","s":"सहयज्ञाः प्रजाः सृष्ट्वा पुरोवाच प्रजापतिः ।\nअनेन प्रसविष्यध्वमेष वोऽस्त्विष्टकामधुक् ॥ १० ॥","t":"In the beginning, the Creator created humanity along with the principle of sacrifice and said: 'Grow and prosper through this spirit of contribution; let this be the source of everything you need.'"},{"ref":"3.11","s":"देवान्भावयतानेन ते देवा भावयन्तु वः ।\nपरस्परं भावयन्तः श्रेयः परमवाप्स्यथ ॥ ११ ॥","t":"Support the cosmic forces (gods) with your contribution, and let those forces support you in return. By mutually supporting each other, you will reach the highest good."},{"ref":"3.12","s":"इष्टान्भोगान्हि वो देवा दास्यन्ते यज्ञभाविताः ।\nतैर्दत्तानप्रदायैभ्यो यो भुङ्क्ते स्तेन एव सः ॥ १२ ॥","t":"The cosmic forces, strengthened by your contributions, will provide the things you need. Anyone who enjoys these gifts without giving anything back is a thief."},{"ref":"3.13","s":"यज्ञशिष्टाशिनः सन्तो मुच्यन्ते सर्वकिल्बिषैः ।\nभुञ्जते ते त्वघं पापा ये पचन्त्यात्मकारणात् ॥ १३ ॥","t":"Those who eat what is left over after making a contribution are freed from negativity. But those who cook only for themselves are essentially 'eating' their own selfishness."},{"ref":"3.14","s":"अन्नाद्भवन्ति भूतानि पर्जन्यादन्नसंभवः ।\nयज्ञाद्भवति पर्जन्यो यज्ञः कर्मसमुद्भवः ॥ १४ ॥","t":"Living beings come from food; food comes from rain; rain comes from the balance of nature (sacrifice); and that balance is maintained by our actions."},{"ref":"3.15","s":"कर्म ब्रह्मोद्भवं विद्धि ब्रह्माक्षरसमुद्भवम् ।\nतस्मात्सर्वगतं ब्रह्म नित्यं यज्ञे प्रतिष्ठितम् ॥ १५ ॥","t":"Understand that purposeful action comes from the creative principle (Brahman), and that principle comes from the eternal reality. Therefore, the highest reality is always present in every act of selfless contribution."},{"ref":"3.16","s":"एवं प्रवर्तितं चक्रं नानुवर्तयतीह यः ।\nअघायुरिन्द्रियारामो मोघं पार्थ स जीवति ॥ १६ ॥","t":"Anyone who does not participate in this natural cycle of contribution, but only lives for their own sensory pleasure and selfish gain, lives a useless life."},{"ref":"3.17","s":"यस्त्वात्मरतिरेव स्यादात्मतृप्तश्च मानवः ।\nआत्मन्येव च संतुष्टस्तस्य कार्यं न विद्यते ॥ १७ ॥","t":"However, for the person who finds total joy within themselves, who is satisfied with their own inner nature, and who is content in the Self alone—for such a person, there is no 'forced' duty to be done."},{"ref":"3.18","s":"नैव तस्य कृतेनार्थो नाकृतेनेह कश्चन ।\nन चास्य सर्वभूतेषु कश्चिदर्थव्यपाश्रयः ॥ १८ ॥","t":"Such a person has nothing to gain by doing things and nothing to lose by not doing them. They do not depend on anyone or anything outside themselves for their sense of worth."},{"ref":"3.19","s":"तस्मादसक्तः सततं कार्यं कर्म समाचर ।\nअसक्तो ह्याचरन्कर्म परमाप्नोति पूरुषः ॥ १९ ॥","t":"Therefore, always do the work that needs to be done without being attached to the results. By working this way, a person reaches the highest state of being."},{"ref":"3.20","s":"कर्मणैव हि संसिद्धिमास्थिता जनकादयः ।\nलोकसंग्रहमेवापि संपश्यन्कर्तुमर्हसि ॥ २० ॥","t":"Great leaders like Janaka reached perfection through action alone. You should also do your work, if only to set an example and help maintain the order of the world (lokasaṃgraha)."},{"ref":"3.21","s":"यद्यदाचरति श्रेष्ठस्तत्तदेवेतरो जनः ।\nस यत्प्रमाणं कुरुते लोकस्तदनुवर्तते ॥ २१ ॥","t":"Whatever a leader does, others will copy. Whatever standards a leader sets, the rest of the world will follow."},{"ref":"3.22","s":"न मे पार्थास्ति कर्तव्यं त्रिषु लोकेषु किञ्चन ।\nनानवाप्तमवाप्तव्यं वर्त एव च कर्मणि ॥ २२ ॥","t":"Arjuna, there is nothing in the entire universe that I *must* do, and there is nothing I don't already have. Yet, I am constantly engaged in action."},{"ref":"3.23","s":"यदि ह्यहं न वर्तेयं जातु कर्मण्यतन्द्रितः ।\nमम वर्त्मानुवर्तन्ते मनुष्याः पार्थ सर्वशः ॥ २३ ॥","t":"If I ever stopped working tirelessly, people everywhere would follow my example and stop doing their work as well."},{"ref":"3.24","s":"उत्सीदेयुर्इमे लोका न कुर्यां कर्म चेदहम् ।\nसङ्करस्य च कर्ता स्यामुपहन्यामिमाः प्रजाः ॥ २४ ॥","t":"These worlds would fall into ruin if I stopped acting. I would be responsible for creating chaos and destroying the very people I am meant to support."},{"ref":"3.25","s":"सक्ताः कर्मण्यविद्वांसो यथा कुर्वन्ति भारत ।\nकुर्याद्विद्वांस्तथासक्तश्चिकीर्षुर्लोकसङ्ग्रहम् ॥ २५ ॥","t":"Just as ignorant people work hard because they are attached to rewards, wise people should work just as hard—but without attachment—for the welfare of the world."},{"ref":"3.26","s":"न बुद्धिभेदं जनयेदज्ञानां कर्मसङ्गिनाम् ।\nजोषयेत्सर्वकर्माणि विद्वान् युक्तः समाचरन् ॥ २६ ॥","t":"A wise person should not confuse those who are attached to their work by telling them to stop. Instead, the wise should perform all actions beautifully and with discipline, encouraging others to do the same."},{"ref":"3.27","s":"प्रकृतेः क्रियमाणानि गुणैः कर्माणि सर्वशः ।\nअहङ्कारविमूढात्मा कर्ताहमिति मन्यते ॥ २७ ॥","t":"All actions are actually done by the natural forces of the universe. But a person who is confused by their ego thinks: 'I am the one doing this.'"},{"ref":"3.28","s":"तत्त्ववित्तु महाबाहो गुणकर्मविभागयोः ।\nगुणा गुणेषु वर्तन्त इति मत्वा न सज्जते ॥ २८ ॥","t":"But someone who knows the truth understands that it's just 'natural qualities interacting with other natural qualities.' Knowing this, they don't get caught up in attachment."},{"ref":"3.29","s":"प्रकृतेर्गुणसम्मूढाः सज्जन्ते गुणकर्मसु ।\nतानकृत्स्नविदो मन्दान् कृत्स्नविन्न विचालयेत् ॥ २९ ॥","t":"People who are confused by nature become attached to their actions and roles. Those who know the full truth should not try to force this understanding on those who aren't ready for it."},{"ref":"3.30","s":"मयि सर्वाणि कर्माणि सन्न्यस्याध्यात्मचेतसा ।\nनिराशीर्निर्ममो भूत्वा युध्यस्व विगतज्वरः ॥ ३० ॥","t":"Offer all your actions to the highest reality with a clear focus on your inner Self. Be free from selfish hope and possessiveness, and do your work (fight) without any mental agitation (fever)."},{"ref":"3.31","s":"ये मे मतमिदं नित्यमनुतिष्ठन्ति मानवाः ।\nश्रद्धावन्तोऽनसूयन्तो मुच्यन्ते तेऽपि कर्मभिः ॥ ३१ ॥","t":"People who constantly practice this teaching with trust and without complaining will also be freed from the burden of their actions."},{"ref":"3.32","s":"ये त्वेतदभ्यसूयन्तो नानुतिष्ठन्ति मे मतम् ।\nसर्वज्ञानविमूढांस्तान्विद्धि नष्टानचेतसः ॥ ३२ ॥","t":"But those who reject and complain about this teaching, and do not practice it—know that they are completely confused and have lost their ability to reason and succeed."},{"ref":"3.33","s":"सदृशं चेष्टते स्वस्याः प्रकृतेर्ज्ञानवानपि ।\nप्रकृतिं यान्ति भूतानि निग्रहः किं करिष्यति ॥ ३३ ॥","t":"Even a wise person acts according to their own natural tendencies. All living things follow their nature; what is the point of trying to forcefully suppress it?"},{"ref":"3.34","s":"इन्द्रियस्येन्द्रियस्यार्थे रागद्वेषौ व्यवस्थितौ ।\nतयोर्न वशमागच्छेत्तौ ह्यस्य परिपन्थिनौ ॥ ३४ ॥","t":"Every sense naturally feels attraction or dislike for certain objects. You should not let yourself be controlled by these feelings, as they are obstacles on your path."},{"ref":"3.35","s":"श्रेयान्स्वधर्मो विगुणः परधर्मात्स्वनुष्ठितात् ।\nस्वधर्मे निधनं श्रेयः परधर्मो भयावहः ॥ ३५ ॥","t":"It is better to do your own duty, even if you do it imperfectly, than to do someone else's duty perfectly. It is better to fail at your own path than to succeed at a path that doesn't belong to you."},{"ref":"3.36","s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nअथ केन प्रयुक्तोऽयं पापं चरति पूरुषः ।\nअनिच्छन्नपि वार्ष्णेय बलादिव नियोजितः ॥ ३६ ॥","t":"Arjuna asked: Krishna, what is it that forces a person to do wrong things, even when they don't want to? It feels like they are being pushed by some invisible power."},{"ref":"3.37","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nकाम एष क्रोध एष रजोगुणसमुद्भवः ।\nमहाशनो महापाप्मा विद्ध्येनमिह वैरिणम् ॥ ३७ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: It is selfish desire and anger, which come from the quality of passion. This is the 'all-devouring enemy' that causes all the trouble in the world."},{"ref":"3.38","s":"धूमेनाव्रियते वह्निर्यथादर्शो मलेन च ।\nयथोल्बेनावृतो गर्भस्तथा तेनेदमावृतम् ॥ ३८ ॥","t":"Just as smoke covers fire, dust covers a mirror, and a membrane covers a baby in the womb, our true knowledge is covered and hidden by selfish desire."},{"ref":"3.39","s":"आवृतं ज्ञानमेतेन ज्ञानिनो नित्यवैरिणा ।\nकामरूपेण कौन्तेय दुष्पूरेणानलेन च ॥ ३९ ॥","t":"Arjuna, this insatiable fire of desire is the constant enemy of the wise. It covers up their wisdom and is never satisfied."},{"ref":"3.40","s":"इन्द्रियाणि मनो बुद्धिरस्याधिष्ठानमुच्यते ।\nएतैर्विमोहयत्येष ज्ञानमावृत्य देहिनम् ॥ ४० ॥","t":"Desire lives in the senses, the mind, and the intellect. Using these as its base, it confuses the soul and hides its true knowledge."},{"ref":"3.41","s":"तस्मात्त्वमिन्द्रियाण्यादौ नियम्य भरतर्षभ ।\nपाप्मानं प्रजहि ह्येनं ज्ञानविज्ञाननाशनम् ॥ ४१ ॥","t":"Therefore, Arjuna, first control your senses and destroy this evil desire, which is the destroyer of both theoretical knowledge and practical experience."},{"ref":"3.42","s":"इन्द्रियाणि पराण्याहुरिन्द्रियेभ्यः परं मनः ।\nमनसस्तु परा बुद्धिर्यो बुद्धेः परतस्तु सः ॥ ४२ ॥","t":"The senses are powerful, but the mind is more powerful than the senses. The intellect is more powerful than the mind, and the Soul (the Self) is even more powerful than the intellect."},{"ref":"3.43","s":"एवं बुद्धेः परं बुद्ध्वा संस्तभ्यात्मानमात्मना ।\nजहि शत्रुं महाबाहो कामरूपं दुरासदम् ॥ ४३ ॥","t":"Knowing that which is even higher than the intellect, and using your highest Self to steady your lower self, destroy this difficult enemy that takes the form of desire."},{"ref":"4.1","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nइमं विवस्वते योगं प्रोक्तवानहमव्ययम् ।\nविवस्वान्मनवे प्राह मनुरिक्ष्वाकवेऽब्रवीत् ॥ १ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: I taught this eternal science of Yoga to the Sun-god (Vivasvan); the Sun-god taught it to the first human (Manu), and Manu passed it on to the first king (Ikshvaku)."},{"ref":"4.2","s":"एवं परम्पराप्राप्तमिमं राजर्षयो विदुः ।\nस कालेनेह महता योगो नष्टः परन्तप ॥ २ ॥","t":"This knowledge was handed down in a continuous chain and understood by the wise kings. But over a long period of time, this science of Yoga was lost to the world, Arjuna."},{"ref":"4.3","s":"स एवायं मया तेऽद्य योगः प्रोक्तः पुरातनः ।\nभक्तोऽसि मे सखा चेति रहस्यं ह्येतदुत्तमम् ॥ ३ ॥","t":"I am telling you that same ancient Yoga today because you are my partner and my friend. This is a profound and supreme secret."},{"ref":"4.4","s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nअपरं भवतो जन्म परं जन्म विवस्वतः ।\nकथमेतद्विजानीयां त्वमादौ प्रोक्तवानिति ॥ ४ ॥","t":"Arjuna asked: You were born recently, but the Sun-god was born in the ancient past. How can I understand that you taught this science to him in the beginning?"},{"ref":"4.5","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nबहूनी मे व्यतीतानि जन्मानि तव चार्जुन ।\nतान्यहं वेद सर्वाणि न त्वं वेत्थ परन्तप ॥ ५ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: Arjuna, both you and I have had many previous lives. I remember all of them, but you do not."},{"ref":"4.6","s":"अजोऽपि सन्नव्ययात्मा भूतानामीश्वरोऽपि सन् ।\nप्रकृतिं स्वामधिष्ठाय सम्भवाम्यात्ममायया ॥ ६ ॥","t":"Although I am unborn, eternal, and the Lord of all living beings, I still appear in the world by controlling my own natural energy through my own power."},{"ref":"4.7","s":"यदा यदा हि धर्मस्य ग्लानिर्भवति भारत ।\nअभ्युत्थानमधर्मस्य तदात्मानं सृजाम्यहम् ॥ ७ ॥","t":"Whenever there is a decline in order and justice (Dharma) and a rise in chaos and injustice, then I manifest myself."},{"ref":"4.8","s":"परित्राणाय साधूनां विनाशाय च दुष्कृताम् ।\nधर्मसंस्थापनार्थाय सम्भवामि युगे युगे ॥ ८ ॥","t":"To protect the good, to stop the wrongdoers, and to firmly re-establish the principles of justice, I appear again and again throughout history."},{"ref":"4.9","s":"जन्म कर्म च मे दिव्यमेवं यो वेत्ति तत्त्वतः ।\nत्यक्त्वा देहं पुनर्जन्म नैति मामेति सोऽर्जुन ॥ ९ ॥","t":"Arjuna, anyone who truly understands the nature of my divine appearance and work will not be trapped in the cycle of birth and death after they leave their body; they will reach the highest state."},{"ref":"4.10","s":"वीतरागभयक्रोधा मन्मया मामुपाश्रिताः ।\nबहवो ज्ञानतपसा पूता मद्भावमागताः ॥ १० ॥","t":"Being free from attachment, fear, and anger, and being fully absorbed in Me, many people in the past have been purified by the fire of knowledge and have reached my state of being."},{"ref":"4.11","s":"ये यथा मां प्रपद्यन्ते तांस्तथैव भजाम्यहम् ।\nमम वर्त्मानुवर्तन्ते मनुष्याः पार्थ सर्वशः ॥ ११ ॥","t":"In whatever way people approach Me, I respond to them in that same way. People everywhere are actually following my path, Arjuna, in all their different ways."},{"ref":"4.12","s":"काङ्क्षन्तः कर्मणां सिद्धिं यजन्त इह देवताः ।\nक्षिप्रं हि मानुषे लोके सिद्धिर्भवति कर्मजा ॥ १२ ॥","t":"People who want quick results from their actions often look for external help (gods); in this human world, results from material actions come very quickly."},{"ref":"4.13","s":"चातुर्वर्ण्यं मया सृष्टं गुणकर्मविभागशः ।\nतस्य कर्तारमपि मां विद्ध्यकर्तारमव्ययम् ॥ १३ ॥","t":"I created the four social categories based on people's natural qualities and the work they do. Although I am the source of this system, understand that I am not its 'doer' and I am unchanging."},{"ref":"4.14","s":"न मां कर्माणि लिम्पन्ति न मे कर्मफले स्पृहा ।\nइति मां योऽभिजानाति कर्मभिर्न स बध्यते ॥ १४ ॥","t":"Actions do not stain me, and I have no desire for the results of action. Anyone who understands this about me will also not be trapped by the results of their own actions."},{"ref":"4.15","s":"एवं ज्ञात्वा कृतं कर्म पूर्वैरपि मुमुक्षुभिः ।\nकुरु कर्मैव तस्मात्त्वं पूर्वैः पूर्वतरं कृतम् ॥ १५ ॥","t":"Understanding this truth, the seekers of freedom in the past performed their duties. Therefore, you should also do your work, following the example of those who came before you."},{"ref":"4.16","s":"किं कर्म किमकर्मेति कवयोऽप्यत्र मोहिताः ।\nतत्ते कर्म प्रवक्ष्यामि यज्ज्ञात्वा मोक्ष्यसेऽशुभात् ॥ १६ ॥","t":"What is true action and what is true inaction? Even very intelligent people are confused about this. I will explain it to you so that you can be freed from all negativity."},{"ref":"4.17","s":"कर्मणो ह्यपि बोद्धव्यं बोद्धव्यं च विकर्मणः ।\nअकर्मणश्च बोद्धव्यं गहना कर्मणो गतिः ॥ १७ ॥","t":"You must understand the nature of purposeful work, the nature of wrong work, and the nature of 'non-work.' The logic of how action affects us is very deep and complex."},{"ref":"4.18","s":"कर्मण्यकर्म यः पश्येदकर्मणि च कर्म यः ।\nस बुद्धिमान्मनुष्येषु स युक्तः कृत्स्नकर्मकृत् ॥ १८ ॥","t":"One who can see 'stillness' while they are busy working, and 'action' while they are sitting still—that person is truly wise and successful in everything they do."},{"ref":"4.19","s":"यस्य सर्वे समारम्भाः कामसङ्कल्पवर्जिताः ।\nज्ञानाग्निदग्धकर्माणं तमाहुः पण्डितं बुधाः ॥ १९ ॥","t":"A person whose every action is free from selfish desire and motivated only by wisdom is called a sage. Their actions are 'burnt away' (neutralized) by the fire of their knowledge."},{"ref":"4.20","s":"त्यक्त्वा कर्मफलासङ्गं नित्यतृप्तो निराश्रयः ।\nकर्मण्यभिप्रवृत्तोऽपि नैव किञ्चित्करोति सः ॥ २० ॥","t":"Having let go of attachment to results, always content and not dependent on anything external—such a person is 'doing nothing' even while they are fully busy with work."},{"ref":"4.21","s":"निराशीर्यतचित्तात्मा त्यक्तसर्वपरिग्रहः ।\nशारीरं केवलं कर्म कुर्वन्नाप्नोति किल्बिषम् ॥ २१ ॥","t":"Free from selfish expectations, with a controlled mind and self, having let go of the need to 'own' things, and doing only what is necessary for survival—such a person incurs no negative consequences (stain)."},{"ref":"4.22","s":"यदृच्छालाभसन्तुष्टो द्वन्द्वातीतो विमत्सरः ।\nसमः सिद्धावसिद्धौ च कृत्वापि न निबध्यते ॥ २२ ॥","t":"Content with whatever comes naturally, rising above opposites (like/dislike), free from jealousy, and remaining the same in both success and failure—such a person is not trapped by their actions."},{"ref":"4.23","s":"गतसङ्गस्य मुक्तस्य ज्ञानावस्थितचेतसः ।\nयज्ञायाचरतः कर्म समग्रं प्रविलीयते ॥ २३ ॥","t":"For a person who has no attachment, who is free, whose mind is grounded in wisdom, and who works only as a contribution (sacrifice)—all the consequences of their actions completely dissolve."},{"ref":"4.24","s":"ब्रह्मार्पणं ब्रह्म हविर्ब्रह्माग्नौ ब्रह्मणा हुतम् ।\nब्रह्मैव तेन गन्तव्यं ब्रह्मकर्मसमाधिना ॥ २४ ॥","t":"The act of offering is the Absolute (Brahman); the gift is the Absolute; the person offering is the Absolute; and the goal is the Absolute. One who sees every action as an expression of the Absolute reaches that Absolute state."},{"ref":"4.25","s":"दैवमेवापरे यज्ञं योगिनः पर्युपासते ।\nब्रह्माग्नावपरे यज्ञं यज्ञेनैवोपजुह्वति ॥ २५ ॥","t":"Some people offer their sacrifices to external powers (gods); others offer their very sense of 'self' as a sacrifice into the fire of the Absolute."},{"ref":"4.26","s":"श्रोत्रादीनीन्द्रियाण्यन्ये संयमाग्निषु जुह्वति ।\nशब्दादीन्विषयानन्य इन्द्रियाग्निषु जुह्वति ॥ २६ ॥","t":"Some people 'sacrifice' their senses by practicing strict self-control; others 'sacrifice' the objects of their senses by using them with total discipline."},{"ref":"4.27","s":"सर्वाणीन्द्रियकर्माणि प्राणकर्माणि चापरे ।\nआत्मसंयमयोगाग्नौ जुह्वति ज्ञानदीपिते ॥ २७ ॥","t":"Others offer all the activities of their senses and even their very life-force into the fire of self-mastery, which is lit by the light of knowledge."},{"ref":"4.28","s":"द्रव्ययज्ञास्तपोयज्ञा योगयज्ञास्तथापरे ।\nस्वाध्यायज्ञानयज्ञाश्च यतयः संशितव्रताः ॥ २८ ॥","t":"People contribute in different ways: some give away possessions, some practice difficult self-discipline, some practice Yoga, and some dedicate themselves to study and the sharing of knowledge."},{"ref":"4.29","s":"अपाने जुह्वति प्राणं प्राणेऽपानं तथापरे ।\nप्रणापानगती रुद्ध्वा प्राणायामपरायणाः ॥ २९ ॥","t":"Others practice controlling their breath, offering the incoming breath to the outgoing and vice versa, aiming to master the flow of their life-energy."},{"ref":"4.30","s":"अपरे नियताहाराः प्राणान्प्राणेषु जुह्वति ।\nसर्वेऽप्येते यज्ञविदो यज्ञक्षपितकल्मषाः ॥ ३० ॥","t":"Others practice disciplined eating as a form of sacrifice. All these people understand the principle of contribution, and their internal impurities are destroyed by this practice."},{"ref":"4.31","s":"यज्ञशिष्टामृतभुजो यान्ति ब्रह्म सनातनम् ।\nनायं लोकोऽस्त्ययज्ञस्य कुतोऽन्यः कुरुसत्तम ॥ ३१ ॥","t":"Those who enjoy the 'nectar' (results) that remains after a sacrifice reach the eternal reality. This world is not for someone who refuses to contribute; how then could any higher world be for them?"},{"ref":"4.32","s":"एवं बहुविधा यज्ञा वितता ब्रह्मणो मुखे ।\nकर्मजान्विद्धि तान्सर्वान्वेवं ज्ञात्वा विमोक्ष्यसे ॥ ३२ ॥","t":"Many such forms of sacrifice are described in the ancient teachings. Understand that all of them are expressed through action. Knowing this deeply, you will be freed."},{"ref":"4.33","s":"श्रेयान्द्रव्यमयाद्यज्ञाज्ज्ञानयज्ञः परन्तप ।\nसर्वं कर्माखिलं पार्थ ज्ञाने परिसमाप्यते ॥ ३३ ॥","t":"The sacrifice of knowledge is superior to the sacrifice of material possessions, Arjuna. All actions, in their entirety, find their ultimate fulfillment in wisdom."},{"ref":"4.34","s":"तद्विद्धि प्रणिपातेन परिप्रश्नेन सेवया ।\nउपदेक्ष्यन्ति ते ज्ञानं ज्ञानिनस्तत्त्वदर्शिनः ॥ ३४ ॥","t":"Learn this knowledge by being humble (prostrating), by asking deep questions (inquiry), and by being of service. Those who have seen the truth will then teach you."},{"ref":"4.35","s":"यज्ज्ञात्वा न पुनर्मोहमेवं यास्यसि पाण्डव ।\nयेन भूतान्यशेषेण द्रक्ष्यस्यात्मन्यथो मयि ॥ ३५ ॥","t":"Once you have this knowledge, you will never fall into confusion again. You will see all living beings as part of your own self, and then as part of Me (the Absolute)."},{"ref":"4.36","s":"अपि चेदसि पापेभ्यः सर्वेभ्यः पापकृत्तमः ।\nसर्वं ज्ञानप्लवेनैव वृजिनं सन्तरिष्यसि ॥ ३६ ॥","t":"Even if you were the worst of all wrongdoers, you can cross over the ocean of negativity using the boat of knowledge alone."},{"ref":"4.37","s":"यथैधांसि समिद्धोऽग्निर्भस्मसात्कुरुतेऽर्जुन ।\nज्ञानाग्निः सर्वकर्माणि भस्मसात्कुरुते तथा ॥ ३७ ॥","t":"Just as a blazing fire turns wood into ashes, the fire of knowledge turns all the 'residue' of your past actions into ashes."},{"ref":"4.38","s":"न हि ज्ञानेन सदृशं पवित्रमिह विद्यते ।\nतत्स्वयं योगसंसिद्धः कालेनात्मनि विन्दति ॥ ३८ ॥","t":"There is nothing in this world as purifying as knowledge. A person who is perfected in Yoga eventually finds this knowledge arising naturally within themselves."},{"ref":"4.39","s":"श्रद्धावाँल्लभते ज्ञानं तत्परः संयतेन्द्रियः ।\nज्ञानं लब्ध्वा परां शान्तिमचिरेणाधिगच्छति ॥ ३९ ॥","t":"A person who has trust (faith), who is dedicated, and who has controlled their senses, attains this knowledge. And once they have knowledge, they reach supreme peace immediately."},{"ref":"4.40","s":"अज्ञश्चाश्रद्दधानश्च संशयात्मा विनश्यति ।\nनायं लोकोऽस्ति न परो न सुखं संशयात्मनः ॥ ४० ॥","t":"The person who is ignorant, who has no trust, and who is always doubting, is ruined. For someone who is always doubting, there is no happiness in this world or any other."},{"ref":"4.41","s":"योगसंन्यस्तकर्माणं ज्ञानसंछिन्नसंशयम् ।\nआत्मवन्तं न कर्माणि निबध्नन्ति धनञ्जय ॥ ४१ ॥","t":"Arjuna, actions do not trap a person who has surrendered their work through Yoga, whose doubts have been cut away by knowledge, and who is truly self-possessed."},{"ref":"4.42","s":"तस्मादज्ञानसंभूतं हृत्स्थं ज्ञानासिनात्मनः ।\nछित्त्वैनं संशयं योगमातिष्ठोत्तिष्ठ भारत ॥ ४२ ॥","t":"Therefore, Arjuna, take up the sword of knowledge and cut away this doubt born of ignorance that sits in your heart. Stand up, take your place in Yoga, and rise to the battle."},{"ref":"5.1","s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nसंन्यासं कर्मणां कृष्ण पुनर्योगं च शंससि ।\nयच्छ्रेय एतयोरेकं तन्मे ब्रूहि सुनिश्चितम् ॥ १ ॥","t":"Arjuna asked: Krishna, you speak highly of quitting all actions (renunciation), but you also praise the disciplined performance of action (Yoga). Please tell me clearly: which of these two is actually better for me?"},{"ref":"5.2","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nसंन्यासः कर्मयोगश्च निःश्रेयसकरावुभौ ।\nतयोस्तु कर्मसंन्यासात्कर्मयोगो विशिष्यते ॥ २ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: Both quitting action and performing disciplined action lead to the highest good. But of the two, the Yoga of action is superior to the renunciation of action."},{"ref":"5.3","s":"ज्ञेयः स नित्यसंन्यासी यो न द्वेष्टि न काङ्क्षति ।\nनिर्द्वन्द्वो हि महाबाहो सुखं बन्धात्प्रमुच्यते ॥ ३ ॥","t":"A person who neither hates anything nor craves anything is a true renouncer, even if they are busy working. Being free from these opposites, they are easily freed from all burdens."},{"ref":"5.4","s":"साङ्ख्ययोगौ पृथग्बालाः प्रवदन्ति न पण्डिताः ।\nएकमप्यास्थितः सम्यगुभयोर्विन्दते फलम् ॥ ४ ॥","t":"Only the immature think that analytical knowledge and disciplined action are different; the wise know they are the same. If you truly master even one, you get the results of both."},{"ref":"5.5","s":"यत्साङ्ख्यैः प्राप्यते स्थानं तद्योगैरपि गम्यते ।\nएकं साङ्ख्यं च योगं च यः पश्यति स पश्यति ॥ ५ ॥","t":"The ultimate destination reached through deep study is the same as the one reached through dedicated work. One who sees study and work as one truly understands reality."},{"ref":"5.6","s":"संन्यासस्तु महाबाहो दुःखमाप्तुमयोगतः ।\nयोगयुक्तो मुनिर्ब्रह्म नचिरेणाधिगच्छति ॥ ६ ॥","t":"Arjuna, it is very difficult to achieve true renunciation without first practicing the Yoga of action. A wise person who practices Yoga reaches the ultimate reality very quickly."},{"ref":"5.7","s":"योगयुक्तो विशुद्धात्मा विजितात्मा जितेन्द्रियः ।\nसर्वभूतात्मभूतात्मा कुर्वन्नपि न लिप्यते ॥ ७ ॥","t":"One who is disciplined in Yoga, whose heart is pure, who has mastered their self and their senses, and who sees themselves in everyone—such a person is never stained by their actions, even when they are busy."},{"ref":"5.8","s":"नैव किञ्चित्करोमीति युक्तो मन्येत तत्त्ववित् ।\nपश्यञ्शृण्वन्स्पृशञ्जिघ्रन्नश्नन्गच्छन्स्वपञ्श्वसन् ॥ ८ ॥","t":"A person who knows the truth thinks 'I am not the one doing anything,' even while they are seeing, hearing, touching, smelling, eating, walking, sleeping, and breathing."},{"ref":"5.9","s":"प्रलपन्विसृजन्गृह्णन्नुन्मिषन्निमिषन्नपि ।\nइन्द्रियाणीन्द्रियार्थेषु वर्तन्त इति धारयन् ॥ ९ ॥","t":"Even while speaking, giving, holding, or just blinking their eyes, they maintain the understanding that 'it is just the senses interacting with the world.'"},{"ref":"5.10","s":"ब्रह्मण्याधाय कर्माणि सङ्गं त्यक्त्वा करोति यः ।\nलिप्यते न स पापेन पद्मपत्रमिवाम्भसा ॥ १० ॥","t":"One who does their work as an offering to the Absolute and lets go of all attachment, is never affected by negativity, just as a lotus leaf is never made wet by the water it lives in."},{"ref":"5.11","s":"कायेन मनसा बुद्ध्या केवलैरिन्द्रियैरपि ।\nयोगिनः कर्म कुर्वन्ति सङ्गं त्यक्त्वात्मशुद्धये ॥ ११ ॥","t":"Using their body, mind, intellect, and even just their senses, those who practice Yoga perform their work without attachment, simply to purify their inner self."},{"ref":"5.12","s":"युक्तः कर्मफलं त्यक्त्वा शान्तिमाप्नोति नैष्ठिकीम् ।\nअयुक्तः कामकारेण फले सक्तो निबध्यते ॥ १२ ॥","t":"A disciplined person, by letting go of the results of their work, reaches ultimate peace. But an undisciplined person, driven by desire and attached to rewards, is trapped in constant stress."},{"ref":"5.13","s":"सर्वकर्माणि मनसा संन्यस्यास्ते सुखं वशी ।\nनवद्वारे पुरे देही नैव कुर्वन्न कारयन् ॥ १३ ॥","t":"A self-controlled person, having mentally let go of the ownership of their actions, lives happily in this 'nine-gated city' (the body), knowing that they are not the ones truly acting or causing action."},{"ref":"5.14","s":"न कर्तृत्वं न कर्माणि लोकस्य सृजति प्रभुः ।\nन कर्मफलसंयोगं स्वभावस्तु प्रवर्तते ॥ १४ ॥","t":"The ultimate power (the Lord) does not create the feeling of being a 'doer,' nor the actions themselves, nor the link between work and reward. It is simply the inherent nature of everything that makes things happen."},{"ref":"5.15","s":"नादत्ते कस्यचित्पापं न चैव सुकृतं विभुः ।\nअज्ञानेनावृतं ज्ञानं तेन मुह्यन्ति जन्तवः ॥ १५ ॥","t":"The Absolute reality does not 'take sides' or judge anyone's good or bad deeds. True knowledge is simply hidden by ignorance, and that is why people are confused."},{"ref":"5.16","s":"ज्ञानेन तु तदज्ञानं येषां नाशितमात्मनः ।\nतेषामादित्यवज्ज्ञानं प्रकाशयति तत्परम् ॥ १६ ॥","t":"But for those whose ignorance has been destroyed by knowledge, that knowledge shines like the sun, revealing the highest truth."},{"ref":"5.17","s":"तद्बुद्धयस्तदात्मानस्तन्निष्ठास्तत्परायणाः ।\nगच्छन्त्यपुनरावृत्तिं ज्ञाननिर्धूतकल्मषाः ॥ १७ ॥","t":"Those whose minds are focused on the Truth, who identify with the Truth, who are established in the Truth, and who seek only the Truth, reach a state of permanent freedom, their negativity washed away by wisdom."},{"ref":"5.18","s":"विद्याविनयसम्पन्ने ब्राह्मणे गवि हस्तिनि ।\nशुनि चैव श्वपाके च पण्डिताः समदर्शिनः ॥ १८ ॥","t":"Those who are truly wise see the same life-force in a learned person, a cow, an elephant, a dog, and even an outcast. They look at all beings with an equal eye."},{"ref":"5.19","s":"इहैव तैर्जितः सर्गो येषां साम्ये स्थितं मनः ।\nनिर्दोषं हि समं ब्रह्म तस्माद्ब्रह्मणि ते स्थिताः ॥ १९ ॥","t":"Those whose minds are established in equality have 'conquered' the world right here on earth. Since the Absolute is flawless and equal, they are established in that Absolute."},{"ref":"5.20","s":"न प्रहृष्येत्प्रियं प्राप्य नोद्विजेत्प्राप्य चाप्रियम् ।\nस्थिरबुद्धिरसम्मूढो ब्रह्मविद्ब्रह्मणि स्थितः ॥ २० ॥","t":"A person should not get over-excited when something good happens, nor should they tremble when something bad happens. With a steady, clear mind, one who knows the Truth stays grounded in the Truth."},{"ref":"5.21","s":"बाह्यस्पर्शेष्वसक्तात्मा विन्दत्यात्मनि यत्सुखम् ।\nस ब्रह्मयोगयुक्तात्मा सुखमक्षयमश्नुते ॥ २१ ॥","t":"One who is not attached to external sensory experiences finds happiness within their own self. By uniting their self with the Absolute through Yoga, they enjoy a happiness that never ends."},{"ref":"5.22","s":"ये हि संस्पर्शजा भोगा दुःखयोनय एव ते ।\nआद्यन्तवन्तः कौन्तेय न तेषु रमते बुधः ॥ २२ ॥","t":"Pleasures that come from sensory contact are actually the birthplaces of sorrow. They have a beginning and an end, Arjuna; a wise person does not find lasting satisfaction in them."},{"ref":"5.23","s":"शक्नोतीहैव यः सोढुं प्राक्शरीरविमोक्षणात् ।\nकामक्रोधोद्भवं वेगं स युक्तः स सुखी नरः ॥ २३ ॥","t":"One who is able to withstand the powerful waves of desire and anger while still living in this body, is a truly disciplined and happy person."},{"ref":"5.24","s":"योऽन्तःसुखोऽन्तरारामस्तथान्तर्ज्योतिरेव यः ।\nस योगी ब्रह्मनिर्वाणं ब्रह्मभूतोऽधिगच्छति ॥ २४ ॥","t":"One who finds joy within, who is satisfied within, and who has their own internal light—that person has already reached the Absolute and finds ultimate freedom."},{"ref":"5.25","s":"लभन्ते ब्रह्मनिर्वाणमृषयः क्षीणकल्मषाः ।\nछिन्नद्वैधा यतात्मानः सर्वभूतहिते रताः ॥ २५ ॥","t":"Wise thinkers reaching this ultimate freedom are those whose impurities are gone, whose doubts are cut away, who have mastered themselves, and who are dedicated to the well-being of all living beings."},{"ref":"5.26","s":"कामक्रोधवियुक्तानां यतीनां यतचेतसाम् ।\nअभितो ब्रह्मनिर्वाणं वर्तते विदितात्मनाम् ॥ २६ ॥","t":"For those who are free from desire and anger, whose minds are controlled, and who have realized their true self, ultimate freedom exists in every direction."},{"ref":"5.27","s":"स्पर्शान्कृत्वा बहिर्बाह्यांश्चक्षुश्चैवान्तरे भ्रुवोः ।\nप्राणापानौ समौ कृत्वा नासाभ्यन्तरचारिणौ ॥ २७ ॥","t":"Shutting out all external distractions, focusing the attention, and regulating the breath into a steady, equal rhythm..."},{"ref":"5.28","s":"यतेन्द्रियमनोबुद्धिर्मुनिर्मोक्षपरायणः ।\nविगतेच्छाभयक्रोधो यः सदा मुक्त एव सः ॥ २८ ॥","t":"...the wise person who has mastered their senses, mind, and intellect, and who has let go of selfish desire, fear, and anger, is truly free forever."},{"ref":"5.29","s":"भोक्तारं यज्ञतपसां सर्वलोकमहेश्वरम् ।\nसुहृदं सर्वभूतानां ज्ञात्वा मां शान्तिमृच्छति ॥ २९ ॥","t":"Understanding that the Absolute is the ultimate goal of all efforts, the sovereign of all worlds, and the true friend of every living being, one finds ultimate peace."},{"ref":"6.1","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nअनाश्रितः कर्मफलं कार्यं कर्म करोति यः ।\nस संन्यासी च योगी च न निरग्निर्न चाक्रियः ॥ १ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: One who does the work they are supposed to do, without being dependent on the results, is a true renouncer and a true Yogi. It’s not just about giving up external rituals or stopping all activities."},{"ref":"6.2","s":"यं संन्यासमिति प्राहुर्योगं तं विद्धि पाण्डव ।\nन ह्यसंन्यस्तसङ्कल्पो योगी भवति कश्चन ॥ २ ॥","t":"Arjuna, understand that what is called 'renunciation' is actually the same as 'Yoga.' No one can be a Yogi unless they have let go of their selfish motivations and hidden agendas."},{"ref":"6.3","s":"आरुरुक्षोर्मुनेर्योगं कर्म कारणमुच्यते ।\nयोगारूढस्य तस्यैव शमः कारणमुच्यते ॥ ३ ॥","t":"For someone who wants to reach the state of Yoga, work is the path. But for someone who has already reached that state, calmness and peace are the way to stay there."},{"ref":"6.4","s":"यदा हि नेन्द्रियार्थेषु न कर्मस्वनुषज्जते ।\nसर्वसङ्कल्पसंन्यासी योगारूढस्तदोच्यते ॥ ४ ॥","t":"A person is said to have reached Yoga when they no longer cling to sensory pleasures or their own actions, and have let go of all selfish plans."},{"ref":"6.5","s":"उद्धरेदात्मनात्मानं नात्मानमवसादयेत् ।\nआत्मैव ह्यात्मनो बन्धुरात्मैव रिपुरात्मनः ॥ ५ ॥","t":"You must lift yourself up with your own mind; do not let yourself down. Your own mind can be your best friend, or it can be your worst enemy."},{"ref":"6.6","s":"बन्धुरात्मात्मनस्तस्य येनात्मैवात्मना जितः ।\nअनात्मनस्तु शत्रुत्वे वर्तेतात्मैव शत्रुवत् ॥ ६ ॥","t":"For someone who has mastered their mind, the mind is a helpful friend. But for someone whose mind is out of control, that same mind acts like an enemy, working against them."},{"ref":"6.7","s":"जितात्मनः प्रशान्तस्य परमात्मा समाहितः ।\nशीतोष्णसुखदुःखेषु तथा मानापमानयोः ॥ ७ ॥","t":"For a person who is calm and has mastered themselves, their inner self remains steady in heat and cold, pleasure and pain, and even in praise and insult."},{"ref":"6.8","s":"ज्ञानविज्ञानतृप्तात्मा कूटस्थो विजितेन्द्रियः ।\nयुक्त इत्युच्यते योगी समलोष्टाश्मकाञ्चनः ॥ ८ ॥","t":"A person is truly disciplined when they are satisfied with wisdom and experience, remain unshaken, have mastered their senses, and see no fundamental difference between a piece of dirt, a stone, and a piece of gold."},{"ref":"6.9","s":"सुहृन्मित्रार्युदासीनमध्यस्थद्वेष्यबन्धुषु ।\nसाधुष्वपि च पापेषु समबुद्धिर्विशिष्यते ॥ ९ ॥","t":"A person is truly outstanding when they maintain the same balanced perspective toward everyone—friends, enemies, strangers, relatives, and even good or bad people."},{"ref":"6.10","s":"योगी युञ्जीत सततमात्मानं रहसि स्थितः ।\nएकाकी यतचित्तात्मा निराशीरपरिग्रहः ॥ १० ॥","t":"A practitioner of Yoga should regularly spend time alone in a quiet place, with a controlled mind, free from selfish expectations and the need to 'own' things."},{"ref":"6.11","s":"शुचौ देशे प्रतिष्ठाप्य स्थिरमासनमात्मनः ।\nनात्युच्छ्रितं नातिनीचं चैलाजिनकुशोत्तरम् ॥ ११ ॥","t":"Set up a firm and steady seat in a clean place—one that is neither too high nor too low—and cover it with comfortable material like cloth or grass."},{"ref":"6.12","s":"तत्रैकाग्रं मनः कृत्वा यतचित्तेन्द्रियक्रियः ।\nउपविश्यासने युञ्ज्याद्योगमात्मविशुद्धये ॥ १२ ॥","t":"Sitting there, make your mind single-pointed and control your thoughts and senses. Practice this discipline (Yoga) solely to purify your inner self."},{"ref":"6.13","s":"समं कायशिरोग्रीवं धारयन्नचलं स्थिरः ।\nसम्प्रेक्ष्य नासिकाग्रं स्वं दिशश्चानवलोकयन् ॥ १३ ॥","t":"Keep your body, head, and neck in a straight line and stay perfectly still. Fix your gaze on one point (like the tip of your nose) and do not look around in different directions."},{"ref":"6.14","s":"प्रशान्तात्मा विगतभीर्ब्रह्मचारिव्रते स्थितः ।\nमनः संयम्य मच्चित्तो युक्त आसीत मत्परः ॥ १४ ॥","t":"With a peaceful heart, free from fear, and being firm in your self-control, sit with your mind quiet and your thoughts focused on the highest Truth."},{"ref":"6.15","s":"युञ्जन्नेवं सदात्मानं योगी नियतमानसः ।\nशान्तिं निर्वाणपरमां मत्संस्थामधिगच्छति ॥ १५ ॥","t":"By constantly practicing this self-discipline, a person with a controlled mind reaches ultimate peace and a state of total freedom."},{"ref":"6.16","s":"नात्यश्नतस्तु योगोऽस्ति न चैकान्तमनश्नतः ।\nन चातिस्वप्नशीलस्य जाग्रतो नैव चार्जुन ॥ १६ ॥","t":"Arjuna, this discipline is not for someone who eats too much or too little, nor for someone who sleeps too much or stays awake all the time."},{"ref":"6.17","s":"युक्ताहारविहारस्य युक्तचेष्टस्य कर्मसु ।\nयुक्तस्वप्नावबोधस्य योगो भवति दुःखहा ॥ १७ ॥","t":"For someone who is balanced in their eating, recreation, work habits, and sleep, this discipline (Yoga) becomes the destroyer of all sorrow."},{"ref":"6.18","s":"यदा विनियतं चित्तमात्मन्येवावतिष्ठते ।\nनिःस्पृहः सर्वकामेभ्यो युक्त इत्युच्यते तदा ॥ १८ ॥","t":"When your mind is so well-controlled that it stays focused on your true self, and you no longer crave external things, then you are truly disciplined."},{"ref":"6.19","s":"यथा दीपो निवातस्थो नेङ्गते सोपमा स्मृता ।\nयोगिनो यतचित्तस्य युञ्जतो योगमात्मनः ॥ १९ ॥","t":"A mind that is perfectly controlled is like a lamp in a windless place—it stays steady and does not flicker."},{"ref":"6.20","s":"यत्रोपरमते चित्तं निरुद्धं योगसेवया ।\nयत्र चैवात्मनात्मानं पश्यन्नात्मनि तुष्यति ॥ २० ॥","t":"In this state, the mind finds rest through practice. One sees their true nature with their own awareness and finds total satisfaction within themselves."},{"ref":"6.21","s":"सुखमात्यन्तिकं यत्तद्बुद्धिग्राह्यमतीन्द्रियम् ।\nवेत्ति यत्र न चैवायं स्थितश्चलति तत्त्वतः ॥ २१ ॥","t":"Where one experiences ultimate happiness—a joy that the mind can understand but the senses cannot reach—and where, once established, one never wavers from the Truth."},{"ref":"6.22","s":"यं लब्ध्वा चापरं लाभं मन्यते नाधिकं ततः ।\nयस्मिन्स्थितो न दुःखेन गुरुणापि विचाल्यते ॥ २२ ॥","t":"Once you have gained this state, no other gain seems greater. Being established in this, even the heaviest sorrow cannot shake you."},{"ref":"6.23","s":"तं विद्याद्दुःखसंयोगवियोगं योगसंज्ञितम् ।\nस निश्चयेन योक्तव्यो योगोऽनिर्विण्णचेतसा ॥ २३ ॥","t":"Understand that this state—the complete disconnection from sorrow—is what is called Yoga. You should practice this Yoga with firm determination and a heart that does not give up."},{"ref":"6.24","s":"सङ्कल्पप्रभवान्कामांस्त्यक्त्वा सर्वानशेषतः ।\nमनसैवेन्द्रियग्रामं विनियम्य समन्ततः ॥ २४ ॥","t":"Completely let go of all desires that come from selfish planning, and use your mind to pull back all your senses from every direction."},{"ref":"6.25","s":"शनैः शनैरुपरमेद्बुद्ध्या धृतिगृहीतया ।\nआत्मसंस्थं मनः कृत्वा न किञ्चिदपि चिन्तयेत् ॥ २५ ॥","t":"Slowly, step by step, bring the mind to a state of rest using a firm and patient intellect. Once the mind is settled in the self, do not let any other thoughts enter."},{"ref":"6.26","s":"यतो यतो निश्चरति मनश्चञ्चलमस्थिरम् ।\nततस्ततो नियम्यैतदात्मन्येव वशं नयेत् ॥ २६ ॥","t":"No matter where the restless and unsteady mind wanders, you should pull it back and bring it under the control of your true self."},{"ref":"6.27","s":"प्रशान्तमनसं ह्येनं योगिनं सुखमुत्तमम् ।\nउपैति शान्तरजसं ब्रह्मभूतमकल्मषम् ॥ २७ ॥","t":"Ultimate happiness comes to the practitioner whose mind is peaceful, whose restless passions (Rajas) are calmed, who is pure, and who has realized their oneness with the Absolute."},{"ref":"6.28","s":"युञ्जन्नेवं सदात्मानं योगी विगतकल्मषः ।\nसुखेन ब्रह्मसंस्पर्शमत्यन्तं सुखमश्नुते ॥ २८ ॥","t":"By constantly practicing this discipline, the pure Yogi easily enjoys the infinite happiness that comes from being in contact with the Absolute reality."},{"ref":"6.29","s":"सर्वभूतस्थमात्मानं सर्वभूतानि चात्मनि ।\nईक्षते योगयुक्तात्मा सर्वत्र समदर्शनः ॥ २९ ॥","t":"One who is disciplined in Yoga sees their own self in all living beings, and all beings within their own self. They see the same reality everywhere."},{"ref":"6.30","s":"यो मां पश्यति सर्वत्र सर्वं च मयि पश्यति ।\nतस्याहं न प्रणश्यामि स च मे न प्रणश्यति ॥ ३० ॥","t":"For someone who sees Me (the Absolute) in everything and sees everything in Me, I am never lost to them, and they are never lost to Me."},{"ref":"6.31","s":"सर्वभूतस्थितं यो मां भजत्येकत्वमास्थितः ।\nसर्वथा वर्तमानोऽपि स योगी मयि वर्तते ॥ ३१ ॥","t":"One who is established in this sense of unity and recognizes Me dwelling in every living being—that person lives in Me, no matter what their external circumstances are."},{"ref":"6.32","s":"आत्मौपम्येन सर्वत्र समं पश्यति योऽर्जुन ।\nसुखं वा यदि वा दुःखं स योगी परमो मतः ॥ ३२ ॥","t":"Arjuna, the highest Yogi is the one who sees everyone as equal to themselves—recognizing that others feel pleasure and pain just as they do."},{"ref":"6.33","s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nयोऽयं योगस्त्वया प्रोक्तः साम्येन मधुसूदन ।\nएतस्याहं न पश्यामि चञ्चलत्वात्स्थितिं स्थिराम् ॥ ३३ ॥","t":"Arjuna asked: Krishna, you describe this Yoga as a state of perfect balance, but I don't see how it can last, because the mind is so restless."},{"ref":"6.34","s":"चञ्चलं हि मनः कृष्ण प्रमाथि बलवद्दृढम् ।\nतस्याहं निग्रहं मन्ये वायोरिव सुदुष्करम् ॥ ३४ ॥","t":"The mind is restless, turbulent, strong, and stubborn, Krishna. I think controlling it is as difficult as trying to catch and hold the wind."},{"ref":"6.35","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nअसंशयं महाबाहो मनो दुर्निग्रहं चलम् ।\nअभ्यासेन तु कौन्तेय वैराग्येण च गृह्यते ॥ ३५ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: Without a doubt, the mind is restless and hard to control. But it can be mastered through consistent practice (Abhyasa) and the cultivation of detachment (Vairagya)."},{"ref":"6.36","s":"असंयतात्मना योगो दुष्प्राप इति मे मतिः ।\nवश्यात्मना तु यतता शक्योऽवाप्तुमुपायतः ॥ ३६ ॥","t":"In my view, Yoga is very hard to reach for someone who has no self-control. But for someone who is disciplined and uses the right methods, it is definitely achievable."},{"ref":"6.37","s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nअयतिः श्रद्धयोपेतो योगाच्चलितमानसः ।\nअप्राप्य योगसंसिद्धिं कां गतिं कृष्ण गच्छति ॥ ३७ ॥","t":"Arjuna asked: Krishna, what happens to a person who has faith but lacks the discipline to stay on the path? If their mind wanders away before they reach perfection, what is their fate?"},{"ref":"6.38","s":"कच्चिन्नोभयविभ्रष्टश्छिन्नाभ्रमिव नश्यति ।\nअप्रतिष्ठो महाबाहो विमूढो ब्रह्मणः पथि ॥ ३८ ॥","t":"Having lost both worldly success and spiritual progress, and having no solid ground to stand on, do they just disappear like a scattered cloud?"},{"ref":"6.39","s":"एतन्मे संशयं कृष्ण छेत्तुमर्हस्यशेषतः ।\nत्वदन्यः संशयस्यास्य छेत्ता न ह्युपपद्यते ॥ ३९ ॥","t":"Please clear this doubt of mine completely, Krishna. No one else can answer this question as well as you can."},{"ref":"6.40","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nपार्थ नैवेह नामुत्र विनाशस्तस्य विद्यते ।\nन हि कल्याणकृत्कश्चिद्दुर्गतिं तात गच्छति ॥ ४० ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: Arjuna, such a person is never destroyed, neither in this life nor in the next. No one who does good, my dear friend, ever comes to a bad end."},{"ref":"6.41","s":"प्राप्य पुण्यकृतां लोकानुषित्वा शाश्वतीः समाः ।\nशुचीनां श्रीमतां गेहे योगभ्रष्टोऽभिजायते ॥ ४१ ॥","t":"After reaching the destination of the righteous and staying there for a long time, someone who fell from the path of Yoga is born again into a family that is clean and successful."},{"ref":"6.42","s":"अथवा योगिनामेव कुले भवति धीमताम् ।\nएतद्धि दुर्लभतरं लोके जन्म यदीदृशम् ॥ ४२ ॥","t":"Or they might even be born into a family of wise practitioners. This kind of birth is very rare and valuable in this world."},{"ref":"6.43","s":"तत्र तं बुद्धिसंयोगं लभते पौर्वदेहिकम् ।\nयतते च ततो भूयः संसिद्धौ कुरुनन्दन ॥ ४३ ॥","t":"There, they regain the mental clarity and understanding they had in their previous life, and they start striving even harder for perfection, Arjuna."},{"ref":"6.44","s":"पूर्वाभ्यासेन तेनैव ह्रियते ह्यवशोऽपि सः ।\nजिज्ञासुरपि योगस्य शब्दब्रह्मातिवर्तते ॥ ४४ ॥","t":"They are carried forward by their previous practice, almost automatically. Even someone who just *wants* to know about Yoga has already moved beyond mere external rituals."},{"ref":"6.45","s":"प्रयत्नाद्यतमानस्तु योगी संशुद्धकिल्बिषः ।\nअनेकजन्मसंसिद्धस्ततो याति परां गतिम् ॥ ४५ ॥","t":"But the practitioner who strives with great effort, whose heart is cleansed, and who reaches perfection over a long period, finally attains the highest goal."},{"ref":"6.46","s":"तपस्विभ्योऽधिको योगी ज्ञानिभ्योऽपि मतोऽधिकः ।\nकर्मिभ्यश्चाधिको योगी तस्माद्योगी भवार्जुन ॥ ४६ ॥","t":"A Yogi is superior to those who practice physical austerities, superior to those who only have theoretical knowledge, and superior to those who only perform rituals. Therefore, Arjuna, be a Yogi!"},{"ref":"6.47","s":"योगिनामपि सर्वेषां मद्गतेनान्तरात्मना ।\nश्रद्धावान्भजते यो मां स मे युक्ततमो मतः ॥ ४७ ॥","t":"And among all Yogis, the one who is full of trust and whose inner self is completely focused on Me (the Absolute)—that person is considered by Me to be the most disciplined of all."},{"ref":"7.1","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nमय्यासक्तमनाः पार्थ योगं युञ्जन्मदाश्रयः ।\nअसंशयं समग्रं मां यथा ज्ञास्यसि तच्छृणु ॥ १ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: Arjuna, with your mind focused on the Truth, practicing discipline and seeking support in Me (the Absolute), listen to how you can know the full reality completely and without any doubt."},{"ref":"7.2","s":"ज्ञानं तेऽहं सविज्ञानमिदं वक्ष्याम्यशेषतः ।\nयज्ज्ञात्वा नेह भूयोऽन्यज्ज्ञातव्यमवशिष्यते ॥ २ ॥","t":"I will explain both the theory (Jnana) and the direct experience (Vijnana) of this truth to you. Once you understand this, there will be nothing left for you to learn in this world."},{"ref":"7.3","s":"मनुष्याणां सहस्रेषु कश्चिद्यतति सिद्धये ।\nयततामपि सिद्धानां कश्चिन्मां वेत्ति तत्त्वतः ॥ ३ ॥","t":"Out of thousands of people, hardly one strives for perfection. And out of those few who do strive and succeed, hardly one truly knows Me as I am."},{"ref":"7.4","s":"भूमिरापोऽनलो वायुः खं मनो बुद्धिरेव च ।\nअहङ्कार इतीयं मे भिन्ना प्रकृतिरष्टधा ॥ ४ ॥","t":"My material nature is divided into eight parts: earth, water, fire, air, space, mind, intellect, and ego."},{"ref":"7.5","s":"अपरेयमितस्त्वन्यां प्रकृतिं विद्धि मे पराम् ।\nजीवभूतां महाबाहो ययेदं धार्यते जगत् ॥ ५ ॥","t":"This is my lower nature. But you should also know my higher nature, Arjuna—the living life-force that sustains this entire world."},{"ref":"7.6","s":"एतद्योनीनि भूतानि सर्वाणीत्युपधारय ।\nअहं कृत्स्नस्य जगतः प्रभवः प्रलयस्तथा ॥ ६ ॥","t":"Understand that all living beings come from these two natures. I am both the beginning and the end of the entire universe."},{"ref":"7.7","s":"मत्तः परतरं नान्यत्किञ्चिदस्ति धनञ्जय ।\nमयि सर्वमिदं प्रोतं सूत्रे मणिगणा इव ॥ ७ ॥","t":"There is nothing in existence higher than Me, Arjuna. Everything in the universe is strung on Me like pearls on a string."},{"ref":"7.8","s":"रसोऽहमप्सु कौन्तेय प्रभास्मि शशिसूर्ययोः ।\nप्रणवः सर्ववेदेषु शब्दः खे पौरुषं नृषु ॥ ८ ॥","t":"I am the \"wetness\" (taste) in water, the light in the sun and moon, the sacred sound OM in the scriptures, the vibration in the air, and the core talent/strength in humans."},{"ref":"7.9","s":"पुण्यो गन्धः पृथिव्यां च तेजश्चास्मि विभावसौ ।\nजीवनं सर्वभूतेषु तपश्चास्मि तपस्विषु ॥ ९ ॥","t":"I am the sweet scent of the earth and the heat in fire. I am the life-force in all living things and the discipline in those who practice self-control."},{"ref":"7.10","s":"बीजं मां सर्वभूतानां विद्धि पार्थ सनातनम् ।\nबुद्धिर्बुद्धिमतामस्मि तेजस्तेजस्विनामहम् ॥ १० ॥","t":"Arjuna, understand that I am the eternal seed of everything that exists. I am the intelligence of those who are smart, and the greatness of those who are great."},{"ref":"7.11","s":"बलं बलवतां चाहं कामरागविवर्जितम् ।\nधर्माविरुद्धो भूतेषु कामोऽस्मि भरतर्षभ ॥ ११ ॥","t":"I am the strength of those who are strong, provided that strength is free from selfish craving and obsession. In all beings, I am the desire that is aligned with justice and duty (Dharma)."},{"ref":"7.12","s":"ये चैव सात्त्विका भावा राजसास्तामसाश्च ये ।\nमत्त एवेति तान्विद्धि न त्वहं तेषु ते मयि ॥ १२ ॥","t":"Understand that all states of being—whether they are pure (Sattva), active (Rajas), or dull (Tamas)—come from Me alone. I am not controlled by them, but they exist within Me."},{"ref":"7.13","s":"त्रिभिर्गुणमयैर्भावैरेभिः सर्वमिदं जगत् ।\nमोहितं नाभिजानाति मामेभ्यः परमव्ययम् ॥ १३ ॥","t":"Bewildered by these three qualities of nature, the entire world fails to recognize Me, who am higher than these qualities and unchanging."},{"ref":"7.14","s":"दैवी ह्येषा गुणमयी मम माया दुरत्यया ।\nमामेव ये प्रपद्यन्ते मायामेतां तरन्ति ते ॥ १४ ॥","t":"This divine energy of mine, made of the three qualities, is very difficult to cross. Only those who surrender to Me (the Absolute Truth) can cross over this illusion."},{"ref":"7.15","s":"न मां दुष्कृतिनो मूढाः प्रपद्यन्ते नराधमाः ।\nमाययापहृतज्ञाना आसुरं भावमाश्रिताः ॥ १५ ॥","t":"Those who do bad things, who are foolish, and who are the lowest among humans do not seek Me. Their wisdom has been stolen by illusion, and they have taken on a destructive (demonic) nature."},{"ref":"7.16","s":"चतुर्विधा भजन्ते मां जनाः सुकृतिनोऽर्जुन ।\nआर्तो जिज्ञासुरर्थार्थी ज्ञानी च भरतर्षभ ॥ १६ ॥","t":"Four types of good people seek Me, Arjuna: those in distress, those who want knowledge, those who want success/wealth, and those who already have wisdom."},{"ref":"7.17","s":"तेषां ज्ञानी नित्ययुक्त एकभक्तिर्विशिष्यते ।\nप्रियो हि ज्ञानिनोऽत्यर्थमहं स च मम प्रियः ॥ १७ ॥","t":"Among them, the wise person who is always disciplined and devoted to the One Truth is the most outstanding. I am very dear to such a person, and they are very dear to Me."},{"ref":"7.18","s":"उदाराः सर्व एवैते ज्ञानी त्वात्मैव मे मतम् ।\nआस्थितः स हि युक्तात्मा मामेवानुत्तमां गतिम् ॥ १८ ॥","t":"All of these are indeed noble, but I consider the wise person to be My very self. Being disciplined, they are firmly established in Me as their highest goal."},{"ref":"7.19","s":"बहूनां जन्मनामन्ते ज्ञानवान्मां प्रपद्यते ।\nवासुदेवः सर्वमिति स महात्मा सुदुर्लभः ॥ १९ ॥","t":"After many lifetimes of learning, the wise person finally realizes that \"The Absolute (Vasudeva) is everything\" and seeks refuge in Me. Such a great soul is very rare."},{"ref":"7.20","s":"कामैस्तैस्तैर्हृतज्ञानाः प्रपद्यन्तेऽन्यदेवताः ।\nतं तं नियममास्थाय प्रकृत्या नियताः स्वया ॥ २० ॥","t":"Those whose wisdom is stolen by various cravings seek out other \"gods\" (lesser goals), following different rules and restricted by their own limited nature."},{"ref":"7.21","s":"यो यो यां यां तनुं भक्तः श्रद्धयार्चितुमिच्छति ।\nतस्य तस्याचलां श्रद्धां तामेव विदधाम्यहम् ॥ २१ ॥","t":"Whatever form a person chooses to trust and follow with faith, I strengthen that faith and make it steady."},{"ref":"7.22","s":"स तया श्रद्धया युक्तस्तस्याराधनमीहते ।\nलभते च ततः कामान्मयैव विहितान्हि तान् ॥ २२ ॥","t":"Armed with that faith, they work toward their goal and eventually get what they want. But in reality, those results are provided by Me (the laws of the Absolute) alone."},{"ref":"7.23","s":"अन्तवत्तु फलं तेषां तद्भवत्यल्पमेधसाम् ।\nदेवान्देवयजो यान्ति मद्भक्ता यान्ति मामपि ॥ २३ ॥","t":"But the rewards gained by people of small understanding are temporary. Those who seek lesser things get lesser things; but those who seek Me (the Absolute) reach Me."},{"ref":"7.24","s":"अव्यक्तं व्यक्तिमापन्नं मन्यन्ते मामबुद्धयः ।\nपरं भावमजानन्तो ममाव्ययमनुत्तमम् ॥ २४ ॥","t":"Unintelligent people think that I—the invisible and infinite—have just become a visible person. They do not know my higher nature, which is eternal and supreme."},{"ref":"7.25","s":"नाहं प्रकाशः सर्वस्य योगमायासमावृतः ।\nमूढोऽयं नाभिजानाति लोको मामजमव्ययम् ॥ २५ ॥","t":"I am not visible to everyone, as I am hidden by my own creative power. This confused world does not recognize Me as the unborn and unchanging source."},{"ref":"7.26","s":"वेदाहं समतीतानि वर्तमानानि चार्जुन ।\nभविष्याणि च भूतानि मां तु वेद न कश्चन ॥ २६ ॥","t":"I know everything that has happened, everything that is happening now, and everything that will happen in the future, Arjuna. But no one truly knows Me."},{"ref":"7.27","s":"इच्छाद्वेषसमुत्थेन द्वन्द्वमोहेन भारत ।\nसर्वभूतानि सम्मोहं सर्गे यान्ति परन्तप ॥ २७ ॥","t":"From the very moment of birth, all beings are confused by the delusion of opposites (like/dislike) that comes from desire and hatred."},{"ref":"7.28","s":"येषां त्वन्तगतं पापं जनानां पुण्यकर्मणाम् ।\nते द्वन्द्वमोहनिर्मुक्ता भजन्ते मां दृढव्रताः ॥ २८ ॥","t":"But those good people who have stopped doing wrong things and whose negativity has ended are freed from the confusion of opposites. They focus on Me with steady determination."},{"ref":"7.29","s":"जरामरणमोक्षाय मामाश्रित्य यतन्ति ये ।\nते ब्रह्म तद्विदुः कृत्स्नमध्यात्मं कर्म चाखिलम् ॥ २९ ॥","t":"Those who seek freedom from the cycle of decay and death by seeking refuge in Me, come to know the full Truth (Brahman), the nature of the Self, and the complete logic of action (Karma)."},{"ref":"7.30","s":"साधिभूताधिदैवं मां साधियज्ञं च ये विदुः ।\nप्रयाणकालेऽपि च मां ते विदुर्युक्तचेतसः ॥ ३० ॥","t":"Those who recognize Me in the physical world, in the cosmic powers, and in the act of contribution—they stay connected to the Truth even at the moment of death."},{"ref":"8.1","s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nकिं तद्ब्रह्म किमध्यात्मं किं कर्म पुरुषोत्तम ।\nअधिभूतं च किं प्रोक्तमधिदैवं किमुच्यते ॥ १ ॥","t":"Arjuna asked: Krishna, what is that Absolute (Brahman)? What is the nature of the self (Adhyatma)? What is action (Karma)? What is the material world (Adhibhuta), and what are the cosmic powers (Adhidaiva)?"},{"ref":"8.2","s":"अधियज्ञः कथं कोऽत्र देहेऽस्मिन्मधुसूदन ।\nप्रयाणकाले च कथं ज्ञेयोऽसि नियतात्मभिः ॥ २ ॥","t":"Who is the Lord of contribution (Adhiyajña) in this body, and how does he live here, Krishna? And how can those who have mastered themselves know you at the moment of death?"},{"ref":"8.3","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nअक्षरं ब्रह्म परमं स्वभावोऽध्यात्ममुच्यते ।\nभूतभावोद्भवकरो विसर्गः कर्मसंज्ञितः ॥ ३ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: Brahman is the unchanging supreme reality; its inherent nature is called Adhyatma (the Self). The creative energy that brings all beings into existence is called Karma (Action)."},{"ref":"8.4","s":"अधिभूतं क्षरो भावः पुरुषश्चाधिदैवतम् ।\nअधियज्ञोऽहमेवात्र देहे देहभृतां वर ॥ ४ ॥","t":"The material world (Adhibhuta) is everything that changes and perishes. The cosmic spirit (Adhidaiva) is the divine person behind the powers of nature. And I am the Lord of contribution (Adhiyajña) living right here in your body, Arjuna."},{"ref":"8.5","s":"अन्तकाले च मामेव स्मरन्मुक्त्वा कलेवरम् ।\nयः प्रयाति स मद्भावं याति नास्त्यत्र संशयः ॥ ५ ॥","t":"Anyone who remembers Me alone at the time of death, leaves their body and reaches My state of being; there is no doubt about this."},{"ref":"8.6","s":"यं यं वापि स्मरन्भावं त्यजत्यन्ते कलेवरम् ।\nतं तमेवैति कौन्तेय सदा तद्भावभावितः ॥ ६ ॥","t":"Arjuna, whatever state of being a person is focused on when they leave their body, that is the state they will reach, because they have been absorbed in that thought their whole life."},{"ref":"8.7","s":"तस्मात्सर्वेषु कालेषु मामनुस्मर युध्य च ।\nमय्यर्पितमनोबुद्धिर्मामेवैष्यस्यसंशयम् ॥ ७ ॥","t":"Therefore, at all times remember Me and do your work (fight)! With your mind and intellect dedicated to Me, you will undoubtedly reach Me."},{"ref":"8.8","s":"अभ्यासयोगयुक्तेन चेतसा नान्यगामिना ।\nपरमं पुरुषं दिव्यं याति पार्थानुचिन्तयन् ॥ ८ ॥","t":"By practicing constant discipline and not letting the mind wander, one reaches the supreme divine Spirit by always thinking of it."},{"ref":"8.9","s":"कविं पुराणमनुशासितार-\nमणोरणीयांसमनुस्मरेद्यः ।\nसर्वस्य धातारमचिन्त्यरूप-\nमादित्यवर्णं तमसः परस्तात् ॥ ९ ॥","t":"One should remember the all-knowing, the ancient, the ruler of all, who is smaller than an atom and the sustainer of everything, whose form is beyond thought and who shines like the sun beyond all darkness."},{"ref":"8.10","s":"प्रयाणकाले मनसाचलेन\nभक्त्या युक्तो योगबलेन चैव ।\nभ्रुवोर्मध्ये प्राणमावेश्य सम्यक्\nस तं परं पुरुषमुपैति दिव्यम् ॥ १० ॥","t":"At the moment of death, one who has an unmoving mind, who is full of devotion and the power of Yoga, and who has focused their life-energy between the eyebrows, reaches that supreme divine Spirit."},{"ref":"8.11","s":"यदक्षरं वेदविदो वदन्ति\nविशन्ति यद्यतयो वीतरागाः ।\nयदिच्छन्तो ब्रह्मचर्यं चरन्ति\nतत्ते पदं सङ्ग्रहेण प्रवक्ष्ये ॥ ११ ॥","t":"I will briefly describe to you that state which the experts call 'imperishable,' which disciplined seekers enter, and for which they practice self-control."},{"ref":"8.12","s":"सर्वद्वाराणि संयम्य मनो हृदि निरुध्य च ।\nमूर्ध्न्याधायात्मनः प्राणमास्थितो योगधारणाम् ॥ १२ ॥","t":"Close all the gates of the senses, lock the mind in the heart, fix the life-force in the head, and remain steady in deep concentration."},{"ref":"8.13","s":"ओमित्येकाक्षरं ब्रह्म व्याहरन्मामनुस्मरन् ।\nयः प्रयाति त्यजन्देहं स याति परमां गतिम् ॥ १३ ॥","t":"One who leaves the body while chanting the sacred sound OM and remembering Me, reaches the highest destination."},{"ref":"8.14","s":"अनन्यचेताः सततं यो मां स्मरति नित्यशः ।\nतस्याहं सुलभः पार्थ नित्ययुक्तस्य योगिनः ॥ १४ ॥","t":"Arjuna, for the person who constantly remembers Me with an undivided mind every day, I am very easy to reach."},{"ref":"8.15","s":"मामुपेत्य पुनर्जन्म दुःखालयमशाश्वतम् ।\nनाप्नुवन्ति महात्मानः संसिद्धिं परमां गताः ॥ १५ ॥","t":"Once they have reached Me, these great souls are never born again into this temporary world of sorrow, because they have reached the highest perfection."},{"ref":"8.16","s":"आब्रह्मभुवनाल्लोकाः पुनरावर्तिनोऽर्जुन ।\nमामुपेत्य तु कौन्तेय पुनर्जन्म न विद्यते ॥ १६ ॥","t":"Every world in the universe is subject to 'return' (cycles), Arjuna; but once you reach Me, there is no more rebirth into those cycles."},{"ref":"8.17","s":"सहस्रयुगपर्यन्तमहर्यद्ब्रह्मणो विदुः ।\nरात्रिं युगसहस्रान्तां तेऽहोरात्रविदो जनाः ॥ १७ ॥","t":"Those who understand that a day of the Creator (Brahma) lasts for thousands of ages, and his night lasts just as long, truly understand the nature of time."},{"ref":"8.18","s":"अव्यक्ताद्व्यक्तयः सर्वाः प्रभवन्त्यहरागमे ।\nरात्र्यागमे प्रलीयन्ते तत्रैवाव्यक्तसंज्ञके ॥ १८ ॥","t":"At the start of the 'Day,' all visible things come from the invisible; at the start of 'Night,' they all dissolve back into the same invisible source."},{"ref":"8.19","s":"भूतग्रामः स एवायं भूत्वा भूत्वा प्रलीयते ।\nरात्र्यागमेऽवशः पार्थ प्रभवत्यहरागमे ॥ १९ ॥","t":"This same multitude of beings appears over and over again, and dissolves helplessly when 'Night' falls, only to emerge again when 'Day' returns, Arjuna."},{"ref":"8.20","s":"परस्तस्मात्तु भावोऽन्योऽव्यक्तोऽव्यक्तात्सनातनः ।\nयः स सर्वेषु भूतेषु नश्यत्सु न विनश्यति ॥ २० ॥","t":"But beyond that invisible source, there is another eternal and truly invisible state that does not perish even when every other being perishes."},{"ref":"8.21","s":"अव्यक्तोऽक्षर इत्युक्तस्तमाहुः परमां गतिम् ।\nयं प्राप्य न निवर्तन्ते तद्धाम परमं मम ॥ २१ ॥","t":"That unchanging state is called 'imperishable' and is the highest goal. That is my supreme home; those who reach it never have to return to the world of sorrow."},{"ref":"8.22","s":"पुरुषः स परः पार्थ भक्त्या लभ्यस्त्वनन्यया ।\nयस्यान्तःस्थानि भूतानि येन सर्वमिदं ततम् ॥ २२ ॥","t":"That supreme Spirit, Arjuna, can be reached through undivided devotion. All beings live within it, and it spreads through everything."},{"ref":"8.23","s":"यत्र काले त्वनावृत्तिमावृत्तिं चैव योगिनः ।\nप्रयाता यान्ति तं कालं वक्ष्यामि भरतर्षभ ॥ २३ ॥","t":"Now I will tell you about the times when departing practitioners reach a state of no-return, and when they reach a state of return."},{"ref":"8.24","s":"अग्निर्ज्योतिरहः शुक्लः षण्मासा उत्तरायणम् ।\nतत्र प्रयाता गच्छन्ति ब्रह्म ब्रह्मविदो जनाः ॥ २४ ॥","t":"Light, day, the waxing moon, the sun's northern path—those who depart during these times of 'clarity' and know the Absolute, go to the Absolute."},{"ref":"8.25","s":"धूमो रात्रिस्तथा कृष्णः षण्मासा दक्षिणायनम् ।\nतत्र चान्द्रमसं ज्योतिर्योगी प्राप्य निवर्तते ॥ २५ ॥","t":"Smoke, night, the waning moon, the sun's southern path—one who departs during these times of 'shadow' reaches a temporary reward and then returns."},{"ref":"8.26","s":"शुक्लकृष्णे गती ह्येते जगतः शाश्वते मते ।\nएकया यात्यनावृत्तिमन्ययावर्तते पुनः ॥ २६ ॥","t":"These two paths—the path of light and the path of darkness—are considered eternal in this world. One leads to freedom, and the other leads back to the cycle."},{"ref":"8.27","s":"नैते सृती पार्थ जानन्योगी मुह्यति कश्चन ।\nतस्मात्सर्वेषु कालेषु योगयुक्तो भवार्जुन ॥ २७ ॥","t":"Arjuna, no Yogi who truly understands these two paths is ever confused again. Therefore, stay disciplined in Yoga at all times!"},{"ref":"8.28","s":"वेदेषु यज्ञेषु तपःसु चैव\nदानेषु यत्पुण्यफलं प्रदिष्टम् ।\nअत्येति तत्सर्वमिदं विदित्वा\nयोगी परं स्थानमुपैति चाद्यम् ॥ २८ ॥","t":"Whatever rewards are promised for studying scripture, performing rituals, practicing austerity, or giving charity — the yogi who understands this teaching goes beyond all of them and reaches the supreme, original state."},{"ref":"9.1","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nइदं तु ते गुह्यतमं प्रवक्ष्याम्यनसूयवे ।\nज्ञानं विज्ञानसहितं यज्ज्ञात्वा मोक्ष्यसेऽशुभात् ॥ १ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: To you, who do not complain or judge, I will tell the deepest secret: the combination of theoretical knowledge and direct experience. Knowing this will free you from all misfortune."},{"ref":"9.2","s":"राजविद्या राजगुह्यं पवित्रमिदमुत्तमम् ।\nप्रत्यक्षावगमं धर्म्यं सुसुखं कर्तुमव्ययम् ॥ २ ॥","t":"This is the king of sciences, the king of secrets, and the ultimate purifier. It is understood through direct experience, it is aligned with your duty, it is joyful to practice, and its results never fade."},{"ref":"9.3","s":"अश्रद्दधानाः पुरुषा धर्मस्यास्य परन्तप ।\nअप्राप्य मां निवर्तन्ते मृत्युसंसारवर्त्मनि ॥ ३ ॥","t":"Arjuna, those who have no trust in this path fail to reach Me and remain trapped in the repetitive cycle of birth and death."},{"ref":"9.4","s":"मया ततमिदं सर्वं जगदव्यक्तमूर्तिना ।\nमत्स्थानि सर्वभूतानि न चाहं तेष्ववस्थितः ॥ ४ ॥","t":"I spread through this entire universe in my invisible form. All beings exist within Me, but I am not limited or contained by them."},{"ref":"9.5","s":"न च मत्स्थानि भूतानि पश्य मे योगमैश्वरम् ।\nभूतभृन्न च भूतस्थो ममात्मा भूतभावनः ॥ ५ ॥","t":"And yet, in truth, beings do not even exist within Me—look at my divine mystery! I am the sustainer and the creator of all beings, yet My true self is not dependent on them."},{"ref":"9.6","s":"यथाकाशस्थितो नित्यं वायुः सर्वत्रगो महान् ।\nतथा सर्वाणि भूतानि मत्स्थानीत्युपधारय ॥ ६ ॥","t":"Understand that just as the powerful wind always stays within the vastness of space while moving everywhere, so do all living beings exist within Me."},{"ref":"9.7","s":"सर्वभूतानि कौन्तेय प्रकृतिं यान्ति मामिकाम् ।\nकल्पक्षये पुनस्तानि कल्पादौ विसृजाम्यहम् ॥ ७ ॥","t":"Arjuna, at the end of a vast age, all beings dissolve back into my nature; and at the start of a new age, I bring them forth again."},{"ref":"9.8","s":"प्रकृतिं स्वामवष्टभ्य विसृजामि पुनः पुनः ।\nभूतग्राममिमं कृत्स्नमवशं प्रकृतेर्वशात् ॥ ८ ॥","t":"Using my own natural power, I repeatedly create this entire multitude of beings, who are essentially helpless under the laws of nature."},{"ref":"9.9","s":"न च मां तानि कर्माणि निबध्नन्ति धनञ्जय ।\nउदासीनवदासीनमसक्तं तेषु कर्मसु ॥ ९ ॥","t":"Arjuna, these actions do not trap me, because I remain unattached and indifferent to them, like a neutral observer."},{"ref":"9.10","s":"मयाध्यक्षेण प्रकृतिः सूयते सचराचरम् ।\nहेतुनानेन कौन्तेय जगद्विपरिवर्तते ॥ १० ॥","t":"With Me as the supervisor, nature creates everything that moves and everything that stays still. This is why the world keeps turning, Arjuna."},{"ref":"9.11","s":"अवजानन्ति मां मूढा मानुषीं तनुमाश्रितम् ।\nपरं भावमजानन्तो मम भूतमहेश्वरम् ॥ ११ ॥","t":"Confused people look down on Me because I have appeared in a human body; they don't recognize my supreme nature as the Lord of all existence."},{"ref":"9.12","s":"मोघाशा मोघकर्माणो मोघज्ञाना विचेतसः ।\nराक्षसीमासुरीं चैव प्रकृतिं मोहिनीं श्रिताः ॥ १२ ॥","t":"Having useless hopes, doing useless work, and possessing useless knowledge, these people lose their ability to reason and take on a destructive and deluded nature."},{"ref":"9.13","s":"महात्मानस्तु मां पार्थ दैवीं प्रकृतिमाश्रिताः ।\nभजन्त्यनन्यमनसो ज्ञात्वा भूतादिमव्ययम् ॥ १३ ॥","t":"But the great souls, Arjuna, who live in accordance with divine nature, focus on Me with an undivided mind, knowing that I am the eternal source of everything."},{"ref":"9.14","s":"सततं कीर्तयन्तो मां यतन्तश्च दृढव्रताः ।\nनमस्यन्तश्च मां भक्त्या नित्ययुक्ता उपासते ॥ १४ ॥","t":"Always speaking of the Truth, striving with firm determination, and being humble and devoted, they stay constantly connected to Me."},{"ref":"9.15","s":"ज्ञानयज्ञेन चाप्यन्ये यजन्तो मामुपासते ।\nएकत्वेन पृथक्त्वेन बहुधा विश्वतोमुखम् ॥ १५ ॥","t":"Others contribute through the 'sacrifice of knowledge,' seeing Me as the One, as the Many, and as the universal presence that faces in every direction."},{"ref":"9.16","s":"अहं क्रतुरहं यज्ञः स्वधाहमहमौषधम् ।\nमन्त्रोऽहमहमेवाज्यमहमग्निरहं हुतम् ॥ १६ ॥","t":"I am the ritual, I am the sacrifice, I am the offering, I am the herb, I am the mantra, I am the butter, I am the fire, and I am the act of pouring."},{"ref":"9.17","s":"पिताहमस्य जगतो माता धाता पितामहः ।\nवेद्यं पवित्रमोङ्कार ऋक्साम यजुरेव च ॥ १७ ॥","t":"I am the father, mother, sustainer, and ancestor of this world. I am the goal of knowledge, the purifier, the sound OM, and the core of all ancient scriptures."},{"ref":"9.18","s":"गतिर्भर्ता प्रभुः साक्षी निवासः शरणं सुहृत् ।\nप्रभवः प्रलयः स्थानं निधानं बीजमव्ययम् ॥ १८ ॥","t":"I am the goal, the supporter, the master, the witness, the home, the refuge, the friend, the beginning, the end, the foundation, and the eternal seed."},{"ref":"9.19","s":"तपाम्यहमहं वर्षं निगृह्णाम्युत्सृजामि च ।\nअमृतं चैव मृत्युश्च सदसच्चाहमर्जुन ॥ १९ ॥","t":"I provide the heat and the rain; I am immortality and I am death; I am that which exists and that which does not yet exist, Arjuna."},{"ref":"9.20","s":"त्रैविद्या मां सोमपाः पूतपापा\nयज्ञैरिष्ट्वा स्वर्गतिं प्रार्थयन्ते ।\nते पुण्यमासाद्य सुरेन्द्रलोक-\nमश्नन्ति दिव्यान्दिवि देवभोगान् ॥ २० ॥","t":"Those who follow the literal rules of rituals and pray for heaven eventually reach the world of the gods and enjoy temporary divine pleasures."},{"ref":"9.21","s":"ते तं भुक्त्वा स्वर्गलोकं विशालं\nक्षीणे पुण्ये मर्त्यलोकं विशन्ति ।\nएवं त्रयीधर्ममनुप्रपन्ना\nगतागतं कामकामा लभन्ते ॥ २१ ॥","t":"After enjoying that vast heavenly world, once their merit is used up, they fall back into the mortal world. Thus, those who just chase their desires through rituals stay trapped in the cycle of coming and going."},{"ref":"9.22","s":"अनन्याश्चिन्तयन्तो मां ये जनाः पर्युपासते ।\nतेषां नित्याभियुक्तानां योगक्षेमं वहाम्यहम् ॥ २२ ॥","t":"But for those who think of Me alone and focus on Me with undivided attention, I personally ensure they get what they need and protect what they already have."},{"ref":"9.23","s":"येऽप्यन्यदेवताभक्ता यजन्ते श्रद्धयान्विताः ।\nतेऽपि मामेव कौन्तेय यजन्त्यविधिपूर्वकम् ॥ २३ ॥","t":"Even those who worship other powers with faith are actually worshipping Me, Arjuna, though they are doing it without knowing the full rules."},{"ref":"9.24","s":"अहं हि सर्वयज्ञानां भोक्ता च प्रभुरेव च ।\nन तु मामभिजानन्ति तत्त्वेनातश्च्यवन्ति ते ॥ २४ ॥","t":"I am the only true enjoyer and master of all contributions; but those who do not recognize My true nature eventually fail."},{"ref":"9.25","s":"यान्ति देवव्रता देवान्पितॄन्यान्ति पितृव्रताः ।\nभूतानि यान्ति भूतेज्या यान्ति मद्याजिनोऽपि माम् ॥ २५ ॥","t":"Those who focus on lesser powers reach those powers; those who focus on ancestors reach them; but those who focus on Me reach Me."},{"ref":"9.26","s":"पत्रं पुष्पं फलं तोयं यो मे भक्त्या प्रयच्छति ।\nतदहं भक्त्युपहृतमश्नामि प्रयतात्मनः ॥ २६ ॥","t":"If someone offers Me even a leaf, a flower, a fruit, or just water with devotion—I accept that offering from a person of pure heart."},{"ref":"9.27","s":"यत्करोषि यदश्नासि यज्जुहोषि ददासि यत् ।\nयत्तपस्यसि कौन्तेय तत्कुरुष्व मदर्पणम् ॥ २७ ॥","t":"Whatever you do, whatever you eat, whatever you offer, whatever you give, and whatever discipline you practice—do it all as an offering to Me, Arjuna."},{"ref":"9.28","s":"शुभाशुभफलैरेवं मोक्ष्यसे कर्मबन्धनैः ।\nसंन्यासयोगयुक्तात्मा विमुक्तो मामुपैष्यसि ॥ २८ ॥","t":"In this way, you will be freed from the bondage of actions and their good or bad results. Being disciplined in this path of renunciation, you will be liberated and reach Me."},{"ref":"9.29","s":"समोऽहं सर्वभूतेषु न मे द्वेष्योऽस्ति न प्रियः ।\nये भजन्ति तु मां भक्त्या मयि ते तेषु चाप्यहम् ॥ २९ ॥","t":"I am the same to all living beings; I have no enemies and no favorites. But those who worship Me with devotion live within Me, and I live within them."},{"ref":"9.30","s":"अपि चेत्सुदुराचारो भजते मामनन्यभाक् ।\nसाधुरेव स मन्तव्यः सम्यग्व्यवसितो हि सः ॥ ३० ॥","t":"Even if someone of terrible character decides to focus on Me with undivided devotion, they must be considered good, because they have made the right resolution."},{"ref":"9.31","s":"क्षिप्रं भवति धर्मात्मा शश्वच्छान्तिं निगच्छति ।\nकौन्तेय प्रतिजानीहि न मे भक्तः प्रणश्यति ॥ ३१ ॥","t":"Such a person quickly becomes righteous and attains eternal peace. Arjuna, you can be sure of this: my devotee is never lost."},{"ref":"9.32","s":"मां हि पार्थ व्यपाश्रित्य येऽपि स्युः पापयोनयः ।\nस्त्रियो वैश्यास्तथा शूद्रास्तेऽपि यान्ति परां गतिम् ॥ ३२ ॥","t":"Arjuna, anyone who takes refuge in Me—regardless of their social status, gender, or background—can reach the highest goal."},{"ref":"9.33","s":"किं पुनर्ब्राह्मणाः पुण्या भक्ता राजर्षयस्तथा ।\nअनित्यमसुखं लोकमिमं प्राप्य भजस्व माम् ॥ ३३ ॥","t":"How much more certain is the success of holy teachers and devoted leaders! Since you have found yourself in this temporary and joyless world, stay focused on Me."},{"ref":"9.34","s":"मन्मना भव मद्भक्तो मद्याजी मां नमस्कुरु ।\nमामेवैष्यसि युक्त्वैवमात्मानं मत्परायणः ॥ ३४ ॥","t":"Think of Me, be devoted to Me, offer to Me, and bow to Me. By disciplining yourself this way and making Me your highest goal, you will surely reach Me."},{"ref":"10.1","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nभूय एव महाबाहो शृणु मे परमं वचः ।\nयत्तेऽहं प्रीयमाणाय वक्ष्यामि हितकाम्यया ॥ १ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: Once again, Arjuna, listen to my supreme words. Because you are dear to Me, I will speak for your own welfare."},{"ref":"10.2","s":"न मे विदुः सुरगणाः प्रभवं न महर्षयः ।\nअहमादिर्हि देवानां महर्षीणां च सर्वशः ॥ २ ॥","t":"Neither the gods nor the great seers know my origin, because I am the source of all the gods and seers in every way."},{"ref":"10.3","s":"यो मामजमनादिं च वेत्ति लोकमहेश्वरम् ।\nअसम्मूढः स मर्त्येषु सर्वपापैः प्रमुच्यते ॥ ३ ॥","t":"Anyone who knows Me as the unborn, beginningless, and great Lord of all worlds, is freed from all confusion and negativity among mortals."},{"ref":"10.4","s":"बुद्धिर्ज्ञानमसम्मोहः क्षमा सत्यं दमः शमः ।\nसुखं दुःखं भवोऽभावो भयं चाभयमेव च ॥ ४ ॥","t":"Intelligence, knowledge, clarity, patience, truth, self-control, calmness, pleasure and pain, birth and death, fear and fearlessness..."},{"ref":"10.5","s":"अहिंसा समता तुष्टिस्तपो दानं यशोऽयशः ।\nभवन्ति भावा भूतानां मत्त एव पृथग्विधाः ॥ ५ ॥","t":"Non-violence, equality, contentment, discipline, charity, fame and disgrace—all these different states of beings come from Me alone."},{"ref":"10.6","s":"महर्षयः सप्त पूर्वे चत्वारो मनवस्तथा ।\nमद्भावा मानसा जाता येषां लोक इमाः प्रजाः ॥ ६ ॥","t":"The seven great seers of the past and the four ancestors of humanity were born from my mind; all the people in the world today have come from them."},{"ref":"10.7","s":"एतां विभूतिं योगं च मम यो वेत्ति तत्त्वतः ।\nसोऽविकम्पेन योगेन युज्यते नात्र संशयः ॥ ७ ॥","t":"Anyone who truly understands this manifestation and My divine power becomes united with an unshakeable discipline; there is no doubt about this."},{"ref":"10.8","s":"अहं सर्वस्य प्रभवो मत्तः सर्वं प्रवर्तते ।\nइति मत्वा भजन्ते मां बुधा भावसमन्विताः ॥ ८ ॥","t":"I am the source of everything; everything starts from Me. Realizing this, the wise worship Me with deep internal feeling."},{"ref":"10.9","s":"मच्चित्ता मद्गतप्राणा बोधयन्तः परस्परम् ।\nकथयन्तश्च मां नित्यं तुष्यन्ति च रमन्ति च ॥ ९ ॥","t":"With their minds focused on Me and their lives dedicated to Me, they enlighten each other and constantly speak of Me, finding total satisfaction and joy."},{"ref":"10.10","s":"तेषां सततयुक्तानां भजतां प्रीतिपूर्वकम् ।\nददामि बुद्धियोगं तं येन मामुपयान्ति ते ॥ १० ॥","t":"To those who are always disciplined and who seek Me with love, I give the 'Yoga of Discernment' (Buddhi-yoga) by which they can reach Me."},{"ref":"10.11","s":"तेषामेवानुकम्पार्थमहमज्ञानजं तमः ।\nनाशयाम्यात्मभावस्थो ज्ञानदीपेन भास्वता ॥ ११ ॥","t":"Out of pure compassion for them, I—living within their own self—destroy the darkness of ignorance with the bright lamp of knowledge."},{"ref":"10.12","s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nपरं ब्रह्म परं धाम पवित्रं परमं भवान् ।\nपुरुषं शाश्वतं दिव्यमादिदेवमजं विभुम् ॥ १२ ॥","t":"Arjuna said: You are the supreme Absolute, the highest home, and the ultimate purifier. You are the eternal, divine Spirit, the first of all gods, unborn and all-pervading."},{"ref":"10.13","s":"आहुस्त्वामृषयः सर्वे देवर्षिर्नारदस्तथा ।\nअसितो देवलो व्यासः स्वयं चैव ब्रवीषि मे ॥ १३ ॥","t":"All the great seers like Narada, Asita, Devala, and Vyasa say this about you, and now You are telling me the same yourself."},{"ref":"10.14","s":"सर्वमेतदृतं मन्ये यन्मां वदसि केशव ।\nन हि ते भगवन्व्यक्तिं विदुर्देवा न दानवाः ॥ १४ ॥","t":"Krishna, I believe everything You are telling me is true. Neither the gods nor the demons truly understand your manifestation."},{"ref":"10.15","s":"स्वयमेवात्मनात्मानं वेत्थ त्वं पुरुषोत्तम ।\nभूतभावन भूतेश देवदेव जगत्पते ॥ १५ ॥","t":"Only You can know Yourself through your own Self, O Supreme Person! You are the creator, the master of all, the God of gods, and the Lord of the entire universe."},{"ref":"10.16","s":"वक्तुमर्हस्यशेषेण दिव्या ह्यात्मविभूतयः ।\nयाभिर्विभूतिभिर्लोकानिमांस्त्वं व्याप्य तिष्ठसि ॥ १६ ॥","t":"Please tell me in detail about your divine manifestations, through which you exist while spreading through all these worlds."},{"ref":"10.17","s":"कथं विद्यामहं योगिंस्त्वां सदा परिचिन्तयन् ।\nकेषु केषु च भावेषु चिन्त्योऽसि भगवन्मया ॥ १७ ॥","t":"How can I know You, O Yogi, by meditating on You constantly? In what specific things should I think of You, Krishna?"},{"ref":"10.18","s":"विस्तरेणात्मनो योगं विभूतिं च जनार्दन ।\nभूयः कथय तृप्तिर्हि शृण्वतो नास्ति मेऽमृतम् ॥ १८ ॥","t":"Tell me again in detail about your power and your manifestations, Krishna. I can never get enough of hearing this life-giving nectar."},{"ref":"10.19","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nहन्त ते कथयिष्यामि दिव्या ह्यात्मविभूतयः ।\nप्राधान्यतः कुरुश्रेष्ठ नास्त्यन्तो विस्तरस्य मे ॥ १९ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: Yes, I will tell you about my divine manifestations, but only the most important ones, Arjuna, because there is no end to them."},{"ref":"10.20","s":"अहमात्मा गुडाकेश सर्वभूताशयस्थितः ।\nअहमादिश्च मध्यं च भूतानामन्त एव च ॥ २० ॥","t":"I am the Self, Arjuna, living in the heart of every being. I am the beginning, the middle, and the end of all living things."},{"ref":"10.21","s":"आदित्यानामहं विष्णुर्ज्योतिषां रविरंशुमान् ।\nमरीचिर्मरुतामस्मि नक्षत्राणामहं शशी ॥ २१ ॥","t":"Among the gods of light, I am Vishnu; among radiant things, I am the sun. I am the wind-spirit Marichi, and among the stars, I am the moon."},{"ref":"10.22","s":"वेदानां सामवेदोऽस्मि देवानामस्मि वासवः ।\nइन्द्रियाणां मनश्चास्मि भूतानामस्मि चेतना ॥ २२ ॥","t":"Of the scriptures, I am the Samaveda; of the gods, I am Indra. Of the senses, I am the mind; and in all living beings, I am consciousness."},{"ref":"10.23","s":"रुद्राणां शङ्करश्चास्मि वित्तेशो यक्षरक्षसाम् ।\nवसूनां पावकश्चास्मि मेरुः शिखरिणामहम् ॥ २३ ॥","t":"Of the spirits of destruction, I am Shiva; of the spirits of wealth, I am Kubera. Of the elements, I am fire; and of the mountains, I am Meru."},{"ref":"10.24","s":"पुरोधसां च मुख्यं मां विद्धि पार्थ बृहस्पतिम् ।\nसेनानीनामहं स्कन्दः सरसामस्मि सागरः ॥ २४ ॥","t":"Arjuna, know Me as Brihaspati, the chief of priests. Among generals, I am Skanda; and among bodies of water, I am the ocean."},{"ref":"10.25","s":"महर्षीणां भृगुरहं गिरामस्म्येकमक्षरम् ।\nयज्ञानां जपयज्ञोऽस्मि स्थावराणां हिमालयः ॥ २५ ॥","t":"Of the great seers, I am Bhrigu; of words, I am the sound OM. Of sacrifices, I am the silent chanting (Japa); and of steady things, I am the Himalayas."},{"ref":"10.26","s":"अश्वत्थः सर्ववृक्षाणां देवर्षीणां च नारदः ।\nगन्धर्वाणां चित्ररथः सिद्धानां कपिलो मुनिः ॥ २६ ॥","t":"Of all trees, I am the sacred Ashvattha; of divine seers, I am Narada. Of heavenly musicians, I am Chitraratha; and among the perfected, I am the sage Kapila."},{"ref":"10.27","s":"उच्चैःश्रवसमश्वानां विद्धि माममृतोद्भवम् ।\nऐरावतं गजेन्द्राणां नराणां च नराधिपम् ॥ २७ ॥","t":"Among horses, I am the immortal Uccaishravas; among lordly elephants, I am Airavata; and among men, I am the King."},{"ref":"10.28","s":"आयुधानामहं वज्रं धेनूनामस्मि कामधुक् ।\nप्रजनश्चास्मि कन्दर्पः सर्पाणामस्मि वासुकिः ॥ २८ ॥","t":"Of weapons, I am the thunderbolt; of cows, I am the wish-granting Surabhi. I am Kandarpa, the source of procreation; and among serpents, I am Vasuki."},{"ref":"10.29","s":"अनन्तश्चास्मि नागानां वरुणो यादसामहम् ।\nपितॄणामर्यमा चास्मि यमः संयमतामहम् ॥ २९ ॥","t":"Of the multi-headed snakes, I am Ananta; of aquatic beings, I am Varuna. Among ancestors, I am Aryama; and among those who maintain law and order, I am Yama (Death)."},{"ref":"10.30","s":"प्रह्लादश्चास्मि दैत्यानां कालः कलयतामहम् ।\nमृगाणां च मृगेन्द्रोऽहं वैनतेयश्च पक्षिणाम् ॥ ३० ॥","t":"Among the demons, I am the devoted Prahlada; of things that measure, I am Time. Among beasts, I am the lion; and among birds, I am Garuda."},{"ref":"10.31","s":"पवनः पवतामस्मि रामः शस्त्रभृतामहम् ।\nझषाणां मकरश्चास्मि स्रोतसामस्मि जाह्नवी ॥ ३१ ॥","t":"Of purifiers, I am the wind; of warriors, I am Rama. Among fishes, I am the crocodile; and among rivers, I am the Ganges."},{"ref":"10.32","s":"सर्गाणामादिरन्तश्च मध्यं चैवाहमर्जुन ।\nअध्यात्मविद्या विद्यानां वादः प्रवदतामहम् ॥ ३२ ॥","t":"Arjuna, I am the beginning, the end, and also the middle of all creations. Of sciences, I am the science of the Self; and among those who debate, I am the logic (vada)."},{"ref":"10.33","s":"अक्षराणामकारोऽस्मि द्वन्द्वः सामासिकस्य च ।\nअहमेवाक्षयः कालो धाताहं विश्वतोमुखः ॥ ३३ ॥","t":"Of letters, I am the letter A; of grammar, I am the dual compound. I am imperishable Time, and the Creator whose face is in every direction."},{"ref":"10.34","s":"मृत्युः सर्वहरश्चाहमुद्भवश्च भविष्यताम् ।\nकीर्तिः श्रीर्वाक्च नारीणां स्मृतिर्मेधा धृतिः क्षमा ॥ ३४ ॥","t":"I am all-devouring death, and also the source of everything that will exist in the future. Among feminine qualities, I am fame, prosperity, speech, memory, intelligence, firmness, and patience."},{"ref":"10.35","s":"बृहत्साम तथा साम्नां गायत्री छन्दसामहम् ।\nमासानां मार्गशीर्षोऽहमृतूनां कुसुमाकरः ॥ ३५ ॥","t":"Of hymns, I am the Brihat-saman; of meters, I am the Gayatri. Of months, I am Margashirsha (late autumn); and of seasons, I am the flower-bearing spring."},{"ref":"10.36","s":"द्यूतं छलयतामस्मि तेजस्तेजस्विनामहम् ।\nजयोऽस्मि व्यवसायोऽस्मि सत्त्वं सत्त्ववतामहम् ॥ ३६ ॥","t":"I am the gambling of the deceitful and the splendor of the splendid. I am victory, I am resolve, and I am the truth of the truthful."},{"ref":"10.37","s":"वृष्णीनां वासुदेवोऽस्मि पाण्डवानां धनञ्जयः ।\nमुनीनामप्यहं व्यासः कवीनामुशना कविः ॥ ३७ ॥","t":"Of the Vrishni clan, I am Krishna; of the Pandavas, I am Arjuna. Of the sages, I am Vyasa; and of the poets, I am the poet Ushanas."},{"ref":"10.38","s":"दण्डो दमयतामस्मि नीतिरस्मि जिगीषताम् ।\nमौनं चैवास्मि गुह्यानां ज्ञानं ज्ञानवतामहम् ॥ ३८ ॥","t":"I am the rod of those who punish and the strategy of those who seek victory. I am the silence of secrets and the wisdom of those who know."},{"ref":"10.39","s":"यच्चापि सर्वभूतानां बीजं तदहमर्जुन ।\nन तदस्ति विना यत्स्यान्मया भूतं चराचरम् ॥ ३९ ॥","t":"And whatever is the seed of all beings, that am I, Arjuna. No being—whether moving or unmoving—can exist without Me."},{"ref":"10.40","s":"नान्तोऽस्ति मम दिव्यानां विभूतीनां परन्तप ।\nएष तूद्देशतः प्रोक्तो विभूतेर्विस्तरो मया ॥ ४० ॥","t":"There is no end to my divine manifestations, Arjuna. I have told you about them only in brief, using a few examples."},{"ref":"10.41","s":"यद्यद्विभूतिमत्सत्त्वं श्रीमदूर्जितमेव वा ।\nतत्तदेवावगच्छ त्वं मम तेजोंऽशसम्भवम् ॥ ४१ ॥","t":"Whatever you see that is glorious, prosperous, or powerful—understand that it has been born from a mere fraction of My splendor."},{"ref":"10.42","s":"अथवा बहुनैतेन किं ज्ञातेन तवार्जुन ।\nविष्टभ्याहमिदं कृत्स्नमेकांशेन स्थितो जगत् ॥ ४२ ॥","t":"But what is the use of knowing all these details, Arjuna? I sustain this entire universe with just a single small part of Myself."},{"ref":"11.1","s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nमदनुग्रहाय परमं गुह्यमध्यात्मसंज्ञितम् ।\nयत्त्वयोक्तं वचस्तेन मोहोऽयं विगतो मम ॥ १ ॥","t":"Arjuna said: Out of your kindness toward me, You have shared the supreme secret of the Self. After hearing your words, my confusion has completely disappeared."},{"ref":"11.2","s":"भवाप्ययौ हि भूतानां श्रुतौ विस्तरशो मया ।\nत्वत्तः कमलपत्राक्ष माहात्म्यमपि चाव्ययम् ॥ २ ॥","t":"O lotus-eyed Krishna, I have heard from You in great detail about how all beings are created and how they dissolve, as well as Your own eternal greatness."},{"ref":"11.3","s":"एवमेतद्यथात्थ त्वमात्मानं परमेश्वर ।\nद्रष्टुमिच्छामि ते रूपमैश्वरं पुरुषोत्तम ॥ ३ ॥","t":"O Supreme Lord, You are exactly as You say You are. But now, O Supreme Person, I actually want to *see* Your divine, sovereign form."},{"ref":"11.4","s":"मन्यसे यदि तच्छक्यं मया द्रष्टुमिति प्रभो ।\nयोगेश्वर ततो मे त्वं दर्शयात्मानमव्ययम् ॥ ४ ॥","t":"If You think it is possible for me to see it, O Lord of Yoga, then please show me Your eternal and unchanging Self."},{"ref":"11.5","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nपश्य मे पार्थ रूपाणि शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ।\nनानाविधानि दिव्यानि नानावर्णाकृतीनि च ॥ ५ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: Arjuna, look at My hundreds and thousands of different forms—divine, and of every possible color and shape."},{"ref":"11.6","s":"पश्यादित्यान्वसून्रुद्रानश्विनौ मरुतस्तथा ।\nबहून्यदृष्टपूर्वाणि पश्याश्चर्याणि भारत ॥ ६ ॥","t":"Look at the various gods of light, power, and nature. Look at all these wonders that have never been seen before, Arjuna."},{"ref":"11.7","s":"इहैकस्थं जगत्कृत्स्नं पश्याद्य सचराचरम् ।\nमम देहे गुडाकेश यच्चान्यद्द्रष्टुमिच्छसि ॥ ७ ॥","t":"Behold the entire universe—everything that moves and everything that stays still—all existing right here in one place within My body, and whatever else you wish to see."},{"ref":"11.8","s":"न तु मां शक्यसे द्रष्टुमनेनैव स्वचक्षुषा ।\nदिव्यं ददामि ते चक्षुः पश्य मे योगमैश्वरम् ॥ ८ ॥","t":"But you cannot see Me with your normal human eyes. I will give you a 'divine eye'; now behold My supreme power!"},{"ref":"11.9","s":"सञ्जय उवाच ।\nएवमुक्त्वा ततो राजन्महायोगेश्वरो हरिः ।\nदर्शयामास पार्थाय परमं रूपमैश्वरम् ॥ ९ ॥","t":"Sanjaya said: O King, after saying this, Krishna, the great Lord of Yoga, showed Arjuna His supreme, sovereign form."},{"ref":"11.10","s":"अनेकवक्त्रनयनमनेकाद्भुतदर्शनम् ।\nअनेकदिव्याभरणं दिव्यानेकोद्यतायुधम् ॥ १० ॥","t":"He had countless mouths and eyes, showing incredible sights, decorated with many divine ornaments, and holding many powerful weapons."},{"ref":"11.11","s":"दिव्यमाल्याम्बरधरं दिव्यगन्धानुलेपनम् ।\nसर्वाश्चर्यमयं देवमनन्तं विश्वतोमुखम् ॥ ११ ॥","t":"Wearing divine garlands and clothes, scented with celestial perfumes, He was full of all wonders—infinite and facing in every direction."},{"ref":"11.12","s":"दिवि सूर्यसहस्रस्य भवेद्युगपदुत्थिता ।\nयदि भाः सदृशी सा स्याद्भासस्तस्य महात्मनः ॥ १२ ॥","t":"If the light of a thousand suns were to burst forth all at once in the sky, that might give some idea of the splendor of that great Soul."},{"ref":"11.13","s":"तत्रैकस्थं जगत्कृत्स्नं प्रविभक्तमनेकधा ।\nअपश्यद्देवदेवस्य शरीरे पाण्डवस्तदा ॥ १३ ॥","t":"Right there in the body of the God of gods, Arjuna saw the entire universe with all its many divisions, all standing together as one."},{"ref":"11.14","s":"ततः स विस्मयाविष्टो हृष्टरोमा धनञ्जयः ।\nप्रणम्य शिरसा देवं कृताञ्जलिरभाषत ॥ १४ ॥","t":"Filled with amazement and with his hair standing on end, Arjuna bowed his head and spoke with joined palms."},{"ref":"11.15","s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nपश्यामि देवांस्तव देव देहे\nसर्वांस्तथा भूतविशेषसङ्घान् ।\nब्रह्माणमीशं कमलासनस्थ-\nमृषींश्च सर्वानुरगांश्च दिव्यान् ॥ १५ ॥","t":"Arjuna said: O God, I see all the gods and all the different types of beings within Your body. I see the Creator, the seers, and the divine serpents."},{"ref":"11.16","s":"अनेकबाहूदरवक्त्रनेत्रं\nपश्यामि त्वां सर्वतोऽनन्तरूपम् ।\nनान्तं न मध्यं न पुनस्तवादिं\nपश्यामि विश्वेश्वर विश्वरूप ॥ १६ ॥","t":"I see You everywhere with infinite arms, bellies, mouths, and eyes. O Lord of the Universe, I see no end, no middle, and no beginning to Your form."},{"ref":"11.17","s":"किरीटिनं गदिनं चक्रिणं च\nतेजोराशिं सर्वतो दीप्तिमन्तम् ।\nपश्यामि त्वां दुर्निरीक्ष्यं समन्ताद्\nदीप्तानलार्कद्युतिमप्रमेयम् ॥ १७ ॥","t":"I see You with your crown, mace, and discus—a mass of brilliance shining in all directions, as bright as a blazing fire or the sun, and impossible to look at directly."},{"ref":"11.18","s":"त्वमक्षरं परमं वेदितव्यं\nत्वमस्य विश्वस्य परं निधानम् ।\nत्वमव्ययः शाश्वतधर्मगोप्ता\nसनातनस्त्वं पुरुषो मतो मे ॥ १८ ॥","t":"You are the unchanging Absolute, the highest thing to be known. You are the ultimate foundation of this universe, the immortal guardian of eternal Dharma, and the original Spirit."},{"ref":"11.19","s":"अनादिमध्यान्तमनन्तवीर्य-\nमनन्तबाहुं शशिसूर्यनेत्रम् ।\nपश्यामि त्वां दीप्तहुताशवक्त्रं\nस्वतेजसा विश्वमिदं तपन्तम् ॥ १९ ॥","t":"I see You without beginning or end, with infinite power and many arms. The sun and moon are Your eyes, and Your mouth is a blazing fire that heats the whole universe."},{"ref":"11.20","s":"द्यावापृथिव्योरिदमन्तरं हि\nव्याप्तं त्वयैकेन दिशश्च सर्वाः ।\nदृष्ट्वाद्भुतं रूपमिदं तवोग्रं\nलोकत्रयं प्रव्यथितं महात्मन् ॥ २० ॥","t":"You alone fill the entire space between heaven and earth and every direction. Seeing this terrifying and wonderful form, the three worlds are trembling with fear."},{"ref":"11.21","s":"अमी हि त्वां सुरसङ्घा विशन्ति\nकेचिद्भीताः प्राञ्जलयो गृणन्ति ।\nस्वस्तीत्युक्त्वा महर्षिसिद्धसङ्घाः\nस्तुवन्ति त्वां स्तुतिभिः पुष्कलाभिः ॥ २१ ॥","t":"Multitudes of gods are entering You, praising You with joined palms. Seers and perfected beings cry 'May all be well!' while singing your praises."},{"ref":"11.22","s":"रुद्रादित्या वसवो ये च साध्या\nविश्वेऽश्विनौ मरुतश्चोष्मपाश्च ।\nगन्धर्वयक्षासुरसिद्धसङ्घा\nवीक्षन्ते त्वां विस्मिताश्चैव सर्वे ॥ २२ ॥","t":"All the different powers of nature and all the perfected beings are looking at You in absolute amazement."},{"ref":"11.23","s":"रूपं महत्ते बहुवक्त्रनेत्रं\nमहाबाहो बहुबाहूरुपादम् ।\nबहूदरं बहुदंष्ट्राकरालं\nदृष्ट्वा लोकाः प्रव्यथितास्तथाहम् ॥ २३ ॥","t":"Looking at Your massive form with its many mouths, eyes, arms, and terrifying teeth, all the worlds are shaking with fear, and so am I."},{"ref":"11.24","s":"नभःस्पृशं दीप्तमनेकवर्णं\nव्यात्ताननं दीप्तविशालनेत्रम् ।\nदृष्ट्वा हि त्वां प्रव्यथितान्तरात्मा\nधृतिं न विन्दामि शमं च विष्णो ॥ २४ ॥","t":"Seeing You touching the sky, shining with many colors and mouths wide open, I am terrified. I have lost my courage and my peace, Krishna."},{"ref":"11.25","s":"दंष्ट्राकरालानि च ते मुखानि\nदृष्ट्वैव कालानलसन्निभानि ।\nदिशो न जाने न लभे च शर्म\nप्रसीद देवेश जगन्निवास ॥ २५ ॥","t":"Seeing your mouths with their terrifying teeth, like the fires at the end of time, I am confused and find no comfort. Please be kind to me, O Lord of the universe!"},{"ref":"11.26","s":"अमी च त्वां धृतराष्ट्रस्य पुत्राः\nसर्वे सहैवावनिपालसङ्घैः ।\nभीष्मो द्रोणः सूतपुत्रस्तथासौ\nसहास्मदीयैरपि योधमुख्यैः ॥ २६ ॥","t":"All these sons of Dhritarashtra, along with many other kings and our own great warriors like Bhishma, Drona, and Karna..."},{"ref":"11.27","s":"वक्त्राणि ते त्वरमाणा विशन्ति\nदंष्ट्राकरालानि भयानकानि ।\nकेचिद्विलग्ना दशनान्तरेषु\nसन्दृश्यन्ते चूर्णितैरुत्तमाङ्गैः ॥ २७ ॥","t":"...are all rushing into Your terrifying mouths. I see some of them with their heads crushed between Your teeth."},{"ref":"11.28","s":"यथा नदीनां बहवोऽम्बुवेगाः\nसमुद्रमेवाभिमुखा द्रवन्ति ।\nतथा तवामी नरलोकवीरा\nविशन्ति वक्त्राण्यभिविज्वलन्ति ॥ २८ ॥","t":"Just as many rivers flow toward the ocean, all these human heroes are rushing into Your blazing mouths."},{"ref":"11.29","s":"यथा प्रदीप्तं ज्वलनं पतङ्गा\nविशन्ति नाशाय समृद्धवेगाः ।\nतथैव नाशाय विशन्ति लोकास्-\nतवापि वक्त्राणि समृद्धवेगाः ॥ २९ ॥","t":"Just as moths fly into a flame only to be destroyed, these worlds are rushing into Your mouths to their own destruction."},{"ref":"11.30","s":"लेलिह्यसे ग्रसमानः समन्ताल्-\nलोकान्समग्रान्वदनैर्ज्वलद्भिः ।\nतेजोभिरापूर्य जगत्समग्रं\nभासस्तवोग्राः प्रतपन्ति विष्णो ॥ ३० ॥","t":"You are devouring all these worlds from every side with Your blazing mouths. Your intense rays are heating up and scorching the entire universe, Krishna."},{"ref":"11.31","s":"आख्याहि मे को भवानुग्ररूपो\nनमोऽस्तु ते देववर प्रसीद ।\nविज्ञातुमिच्छामि भवन्तमाद्यं\nन हि प्रजानामि तव प्रवृत्तिम् ॥ ३१ ॥","t":"Tell me, who are You in this terrifying form? I bow to You, O best of gods! Please be kind. I want to understand your true nature, because I don't understand what you are doing."},{"ref":"11.32","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nकालोऽस्मि लोकक्षयकृत्प्रवृद्धो\nलोकान्समाहर्तुमिह प्रवृत्तः ।\nऋतेऽपि त्वां न भविष्यन्ति सर्वे\nयेऽवस्थिताः प्रत्यनीकेषु योधाः ॥ ३२ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: I am Time, the destroyer of worlds, now active in wiping out these people. Even without you, all these warriors standing here will cease to exist."},{"ref":"11.33","s":"तस्मात्त्वमुत्तिष्ठ यशो लभस्व\nजित्वा शत्रून्भुङ्क्ष्व राज्यं समृद्धम् ।\nमयैवैते निहताः पूर्वमेव\nनिमित्तमात्रं भव सव्यसाचिन् ॥ ३३ ॥","t":"Therefore, stand up and win glory! Defeat your enemies and enjoy a prosperous kingdom. I have already killed them; you should be just the instrument, Arjuna!"},{"ref":"11.34","s":"द्रोणं च भीष्मं च जयद्रथं च\nकर्णं तथान्यानपि योधवीरान् ।\nमया हतांस्त्वं जहि मा व्यथिष्ठा\nयुध्यस्व जेतासि रणे सपत्नान् ॥ ३४ ॥","t":"Drona, Bhishma, Jayadratha, Karna, and all these other heroes have already been killed by Me. Do not be afraid! Fight, and you will certainly win!"},{"ref":"11.35","s":"सञ्जय उवाच ।\nएतच्छ्रुत्वा वचनं केशवस्य\nकृताञ्जलिर्वेपमानः किरीटी ।\nनमस्कृत्वा भूय एवाह कृष्णं\nसगद्गदं भीतभीतः प्रणम्य ॥ ३५ ॥","t":"Sanjaya said: Hearing these words, Arjuna trembled and bowed down. With a shaking voice and filled with fear, he spoke to Krishna again."},{"ref":"11.36","s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nस्थाने हृषीकेश तव प्रकीर्त्या\nजगत्प्रहृष्यत्यनुरज्यते च ।\nरक्षांसि भीतानि दिशो द्रवन्ति\nसर्वे नमस्यन्ति च सिद्धसङ्घाः ॥ ३६ ॥","t":"Arjuna said: It is only right, Krishna, that the universe rejoices in Your name. Evil forces flee in fear, while perfected beings bow to You."},{"ref":"11.37","s":"कस्माच्च ते न नमेरन्महात्मन्\nगरीयसे ब्रह्मणोऽप्यादिकर्त्रे ।\nअनन्त देवेश जगन्निवास\nत्वमक्षरं सदसत्तत्परं यत् ॥ ३७ ॥","t":"Why wouldn't they bow to You, O Great Soul? You are greater even than the Creator. You are the infinite Lord, the home of the universe, the unchanging truth, and both what exists and what does not."},{"ref":"11.38","s":"त्वमादिदेवः पुरुषः पुराणस्-\nत्वमस्य विश्वस्य परं निधानम् ।\nवेत्तासि वेद्यं च परं च धाम\nत्वया ततं विश्वमनन्तरूप ॥ ३८ ॥","t":"You are the first of gods, the ancient Spirit, and the ultimate resting place of the universe. You are the knower, the object of knowledge, and the highest home. You spread through the entire universe."},{"ref":"11.39","s":"वायुर्यमोऽग्निर्वरुणः शशाङ्कः\nप्रजापतिस्त्वं प्रपितामहश्च ।\nनमो नमस्तेऽस्तु सहस्रकृत्वः\nपुनश्च भूयोऽपि नमो नमस्ते ॥ ३९ ॥","t":"You are the wind, the god of death, the fire, the water, and the moon. You are the Creator and the great-grandfather. I bow to You a thousand times, and again and again!"},{"ref":"11.40","s":"नमः पुरस्तादथ पृष्ठतस्ते\nनमोऽस्तु ते सर्वत एव सर्व ।\nअनन्तवीर्यामितविक्रमस्त्वं\nसर्वं समाप्नोषि ततोऽसि सर्वः ॥ ४० ॥","t":"Salutations to You from the front, from behind, and from every side, O All! You possess infinite power and measureless strength. You fill everything, so You are everything."},{"ref":"11.41","s":"सखेति मत्वा प्रसभं यदुक्तं\nहे कृष्ण हे यादव हे सखेति ।\nअजानता महिमानं तवेदं\nमया प्रमादात्प्रणयेन वापि ॥ ४१ ॥","t":"Thinking of You only as a friend, I have rashly called You 'Kṛṣṇa,' 'Yādava,' and 'Friend,' not knowing Your greatness, either because of my negligence or my affection."},{"ref":"11.42","s":"यच्चावहासार्थमसत्कृतोऽसि\nविहारशय्यासनभोजनेषु ।\nएकोऽथवाप्यच्युत तत्समक्षं\nतत्क्षामये त्वामहमप्रमेयम् ॥ ४२ ॥","t":"I have even joked about You or been disrespectful while we were playing, resting, or eating together. I beg Your forgiveness for all of that, O immeasurable One."},{"ref":"11.43","s":"पितासि लोकस्य चराचरस्य\nत्वमस्य पूज्यश्च गुरुर्गरीयान् ।\nन त्वत्समोऽस्त्यभ्यधिकः कुतोऽन्यो\nलोकत्रयेऽप्यप्रतिमप्रभाव ॥ ४३ ॥","t":"You are the Father of the whole world, the most respected Teacher, and there is no one equal to You. How could anyone be greater than You in all the three worlds?"},{"ref":"11.44","s":"तस्मात्प्रणम्य प्रणिधाय कायं\nप्रसादये त्वामहमीशमीड्यम् ।\nपितेव पुत्रस्य सखेव सख्युः\nप्रियः प्रियायार्हसि देव सोढुम् ॥ ४४ ॥","t":"Therefore, I bow down and prostrate myself, seeking Your grace. As a father forgives a son, a friend a friend, or a lover a beloved—please forgive me and be kind."},{"ref":"11.45","s":"अदृष्टपूर्वं हृषितोऽस्मि दृष्ट्वा\nभयेन च प्रव्यथितं मनो मे ।\nतदेव मे दर्शय देव रूपं\nप्रसीद देवेश जगन्निवास ॥ ४५ ॥","t":"I am thrilled to have seen this vision that no one has ever seen before, but I am also shaking with fear. Please show me Your familiar form again, O Lord!"},{"ref":"11.46","s":"किरीटिनं गदिनं चक्रहस्तम्-\nइच्छामि त्वां द्रष्टुमहं तथैव ।\nतेनैव रूपेण चतुर्भुजेन\nसहस्रबाहो भव विश्वमूर्ते ॥ ४६ ॥","t":"I want to see You as before, with Your crown and mace and discus. Please assume Your gentle, four-armed form again, O thousand-armed Universal Form!"},{"ref":"11.47","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nमया प्रसन्नेन तवार्जुनेदं\nरूपं परं दर्शितमात्मयोगात् ।\nतेजोमयं विश्वमनन्तमाद्यं\nयन्मे त्वदन्येन न दृष्टपूर्वम् ॥ ४७ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: By My grace and through My own power, I have shown you this supreme, universal, and infinite form which no one else has ever seen."},{"ref":"11.48","s":"न वेदयज्ञाध्ययनैर्न दानैर्-\nन च क्रियाभिर्न तपोभिरुग्रैः ।\nएवंरूपः शक्य अहं नृलोके\nद्रष्टुं त्वदन्येन कुरुप्रवीर ॥ ४८ ॥","t":"Arjuna, not through the study of scriptures, nor rituals, nor charity, nor difficult disciplines can I be seen in this form by anyone else in the human world."},{"ref":"11.49","s":"मा ते व्यथा मा च विमूढभावो\nदृष्ट्वा रूपं घोरमीदृङ्ममेदम् ।\nव्यपेतभीः प्रीतमनाः पुनस्त्वं\nतदेव मे रूपमिदं प्रपश्य ॥ ४९ ॥","t":"Do not be afraid or confused by seeing this terrifying form of Mine. Be free from fear, and with a happy heart, look at My familiar form once again."},{"ref":"11.50","s":"सञ्जय उवाच ।\nइत्यर्जुनं वासुदेवस्तथोक्त्वा\nस्वकं रूपं दर्शयामास भूयः ।\nआश्वासयामास च भीतमेनं\nभूत्वा पुनः सौम्यवपुर्महात्मा ॥ ५० ॥","t":"Sanjaya said: After saying this, Krishna showed His own gentle form again, comforting the terrified Arjuna."},{"ref":"11.51","s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nदृष्ट्वेदं मानुषं रूपं तव सौम्यं जनार्दन ।\nइदानीमस्मि संवृत्तः सचेताः प्रकृतिं गतः ॥ ५१ ॥","t":"Arjuna said: Seeing this gentle human form of Yours, I have now become calm and restored to my normal nature."},{"ref":"11.52","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nसुदुर्दर्शमिदं रूपं दृष्टवानसि यन्मम ।\nदेवा अप्यस्य रूपस्य नित्यं दर्शनकाङ्क्षिणः ॥ ५२ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: The form you have just seen is very difficult to see. Even the gods are always longing for a glimpse of it."},{"ref":"11.53","s":"नाहं वेदैर्न तपसा न दानेन न चेज्यया ।\nशक्य एवंविधो द्रष्टुं दृष्टवानसि मां यथा ॥ ५३ ॥","t":"Neither by the scriptures, nor by self-discipline, nor by charity, nor by ritual can I be seen in the way you have just seen Me."},{"ref":"11.54","s":"भक्त्या त्वनन्यया शक्य अहमेवंविधोऽर्जुन ।\nज्ञातुं द्रष्टुं च तत्त्वेन प्रवेष्टुं च परन्तप ॥ ५४ ॥","t":"But through undivided devotion (Bhakti), Arjuna, I can be truly known, seen, and entered into."},{"ref":"11.55","s":"मत्कर्मकृन्मत्परमो मद्भक्तः सङ्गवर्जितः ।\nनिर्वैरः सर्वभूतेषु यः स मामेति पाण्डव ॥ ५५ ॥","t":"The one who works for Me, considers Me the highest, is devoted to Me, is free from attachment, and holds no hatred toward any living being — that person reaches Me, Arjuna."},{"ref":"12.1","s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nएवं सततयुक्ता ये भक्तास्त्वां पर्युपासते ।\nये चाप्यक्षरमव्यक्तं तेषां के योगवित्तमाः ॥ १ ॥","t":"Arjuna asked: Some devotees focus on You as a person, while others focus on the invisible and unchanging Absolute. Which of these two paths is the best for mastering Yoga?"},{"ref":"12.2","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nमय्यावेश्य मनो ये मां नित्ययुक्ता उपासते ।\nश्रद्धया परयोपेतास्ते मे युक्ततमा मताः ॥ २ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: Those who fix their minds on Me and worship Me with constant discipline and supreme faith—I consider them the most fully disciplined of all."},{"ref":"12.3","s":"ये त्वक्षरमनिर्देश्यमव्यक्तं पर्युपासते ।\nसर्वत्रगमचिन्त्यं च कूटस्थमचलं ध्रुवम् ॥ ३ ॥","t":"But those who focus on the unchanging, invisible, and everywhere-present Absolute—the unthinkable, unmoving, and eternal Truth..."},{"ref":"12.4","s":"सन्नियम्येन्द्रियग्रामं सर्वत्र समबुद्धयः ।\nते प्राप्नुवन्ति मामेव सर्वभूतहिते रताः ॥ ४ ॥","t":"...by controlling their senses and having an equal mind toward everyone, while delighting in helping all living beings—they too reach Me."},{"ref":"12.5","s":"क्लेशोऽधिकतरस्तेषामव्यक्तासक्तचेतसाम् ।\nअव्यक्ता हि गतिर्दुःखं देहवद्भिरवाप्यते ॥ ५ ॥","t":"However, the struggle is much greater for those focused on the invisible Absolute. It is very hard for a person living in a physical body to reach an invisible goal."},{"ref":"12.6","s":"ये तु सर्वाणि कर्माणि मयि संन्यस्य मत्पराः ।\nअनन्येनैव योगेन मां ध्यायन्त उपासते ॥ ६ ॥","t":"But for those who surrender all their actions to Me, holding Me as their highest goal, and who meditate on Me with undivided focus..."},{"ref":"12.7","s":"तेषामहं समुद्धर्ता मृत्युसंसारसागरात् ।\nभवामि नचिरात्पार्थ मय्यावेशितचेतसाम् ॥ ७ ॥","t":"For those whose minds are fixed on Me, I quickly become the one who saves them from the ocean of repetitive death and rebirth."},{"ref":"12.8","s":"मय्येव मन आधत्स्व मयि बुद्धिं निवेशय ।\nनिवसिष्यसि मय्येव अत ऊर्ध्वं न संशयः ॥ ८ ॥","t":"Just fix your mind on Me alone and let your intellect live in Me. If you do this, you will undoubtedly live in Me forever."},{"ref":"12.9","s":"अथ चित्तं समाधातुं न शक्नोषि मयि स्थिरम् ।\nअभ्यासयोगेन ततो मामिच्छाप्तुं धनञ्जय ॥ ९ ॥","t":"If you are not able to keep your mind steady on Me right away, then try to reach Me through the 'Yoga of Practice' (Abhyasa-yoga), Arjuna."},{"ref":"12.10","s":"अभ्यासेऽप्यसमर्थोऽसि मत्कर्मपरमो भव ।\nमदर्थमपि कर्माणि कुर्वन्सिद्धिमवाप्स्यसि ॥ १० ॥","t":"If you are unable even to practice, then dedicate all your work to Me. Even by performing your daily actions for My sake, you will reach perfection."},{"ref":"12.11","s":"अथैतदप्यशक्तोऽसि कर्तुं मद्योगमाश्रितः ।\nसर्वकर्मफलत्यागं ततः कुरु यतात्मवान् ॥ ११ ॥","t":"If you find even this too hard, then simply take refuge in My discipline and learn to give up the obsession with the results of your actions."},{"ref":"12.12","s":"श्रेयो हि ज्ञानमभ्यासाज्ज्ञानाद्ध्यानं विशिष्यते ।\nध्यानात्कर्मफलत्यागस्त्यागाच्छान्तिरनन्तरम् ॥ १२ ॥","t":"Wisdom is better than blind practice; meditation is better than mere wisdom; but letting go of the results of action is better than meditation, because it brings peace immediately."},{"ref":"12.13","s":"अद्वेष्टा सर्वभूतानां मैत्रः करुण एव च ।\nनिर्ममो निरहङ्कारः समदुःखसुखः क्षमी ॥ १३ ॥","t":"One who hates no one, who is friendly and kind to all, who doesn't say 'this is mine' or 'I am great,' who stays steady in both pain and pleasure, and who is patient..."},{"ref":"12.14","s":"सन्तुष्टः सततं योगी यतात्मा दृढनिश्चयः ।\nमय्यर्पितमनोबुद्धिर्यो मद्भक्तः स मे प्रियः ॥ १४ ॥","t":"...who is always content, disciplined, firm in their resolve, and whose mind and intellect are dedicated to Me—that devotee is very dear to Me."},{"ref":"12.15","s":"यस्मान्नोद्विजते लोको लोकान्नोद्विजते च यः ।\nहर्षामर्षभयोद्वेगैर्मुक्तो यः स च मे प्रियः ॥ १५ ॥","t":"A person who does not disturb the world, and who is not disturbed *by* the world, and who is free from over-excitement, anger, fear, and anxiety—that person is dear to Me."},{"ref":"12.16","s":"अनपेक्षः शुचिर्दक्ष उदासीनो गतव्यथः ।\nसर्वारम्भपरित्यागी यो मद्भक्तः स मे प्रियः ॥ १६ ॥","t":"One who has no selfish expectations, who is pure, capable, neutral, and free from worry—and who has given up all selfish projects—that person is dear to Me."},{"ref":"12.17","s":"यो न हृष्यति न द्वेष्टि न शोचति न काङ्क्षति ।\nशुभाशुभपरित्यागी भक्तिमान्यः स मे प्रियः ॥ १७ ॥","t":"One who neither celebrates nor hates, who neither grieves nor craves, who has risen above both 'good' and 'bad' luck, and who is full of devotion—that person is dear to Me."},{"ref":"12.18","s":"समः शत्रौ च मित्रे च तथा मानापमानयोः ।\nशीतोष्णसुखदुःखेषु समः सङ्गविवर्जितः ॥ १८ ॥","t":"One who treats enemies and friends the same, and stays equal in both praise and insult, and remains the same in heat and cold, pleasure and pain, without any attachment..."},{"ref":"12.19","s":"तुल्यनिन्दास्तुतिर्मौनी सन्तुष्टो येन केनचित् ।\nअनिकेतः स्थिरमतिर्भक्तिमान्मे प्रियो नरः ॥ १९ ॥","t":"...who treats criticism and praise as the same, who stays quiet and content with whatever they have, who has no fixed attachment to a home, and whose mind is steady—that person is dear to Me."},{"ref":"12.20","s":"ये तु धर्म्यामृतमिदं यथोक्तं पर्युपासते ।\nश्रद्दधाना मत्परमा भक्तास्तेऽतीव मे प्रियाः ॥ २० ॥","t":"But those devotees who follow this immortal path of Dharma with complete faith and hold Me as their highest goal — they are the ones I love most of all."},{"ref":"13.1","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nइदं शरीरं कौन्तेय क्षेत्रमित्यभिधीयते ।\nएतद्यो वेत्ति तं प्राहुः क्षेत्रज्ञ इति तद्विदः ॥ १ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: Arjuna, this body is known as the 'Field' (Kshetra). Those who understand the truth call the one who observes and knows this body the 'Knower of the Field' (Kshetrajna)."},{"ref":"13.2","s":"क्षेत्रज्ञं चापि मां विद्धि सर्वक्षेत्रेषु भारत ।\nक्षेत्रक्षेत्रज्ञयोर्ज्ञानं यत्तज्ज्ञानं मतं मम ॥ २ ॥","t":"Arjuna, understand that I am the Knower of the Field in all fields. The true understanding of both the Field and the Knower is what I consider real knowledge."},{"ref":"13.3","s":"तत्क्षेत्रं यच्च यादृक्च यद्विकारि यतश्च यत् ।\nस च यो यत्प्रभावश्च तत्समासेन मे शृणु ॥ ३ ॥","t":"Now listen briefly to what this Field is, what its nature is, how it changes, where it comes from, and who the Knower is and what his powers are."},{"ref":"13.4","s":"ऋषिभिर्बहुधा गीतं छन्दोभिर्विविधैः पृथक् ।\nब्रह्मसूत्रपदैश्चैव हेतुमद्भिर्विनिश्चितैः ॥ ४ ॥","t":"This truth has been explained by seers in many ways, in various sacred songs, and in the logical and well-reasoned words of the Brahma-sutras."},{"ref":"13.5","s":"महाभूतान्यहङ्कारो बुद्धिरव्यक्तमेव च ।\nइन्द्रियाणि दशैकं च पञ्च चेन्द्रियगोचराः ॥ ५ ॥","t":"The five great elements, the ego, the intellect, the unmanifest source, the eleven senses (including the mind), and the five objects of the senses..."},{"ref":"13.6","s":"इच्छा द्वेषः सुखं दुःखं सङ्घातश्चेतना धृतिः ।\nएतत्क्षेत्रं समासेन सविकारमुदाहृतम् ॥ ६ ॥","t":"...desire, hatred, pleasure, pain, the physical body, consciousness, and resolve—this, in brief, is what makes up the Field and its changing states."},{"ref":"13.7","s":"अमानित्वमदम्भित्वमहिंसा क्षान्तिरार्जवम् ।\nआचार्योपासनं शौचं स्थैर्यमात्मविनिग्रहः ॥ ७ ॥","t":"Humility, honesty, non-violence, patience, integrity, service to a teacher, purity, steadiness, and self-control..."},{"ref":"13.8","s":"इन्द्रियार्थेषु वैराग्यमनहङ्कार एव च ।\nजन्ममृत्युजराव्याधिदुःखदोषानुदर्शनम् ॥ ८ ॥","t":"...detachment from sensory pleasures, lack of ego, and a clear-eyed look at the suffering inherent in birth, death, old age, and disease..."},{"ref":"13.9","s":"असक्तिरनभिष्वङ्गः पुत्रदारगृहादिषु ।\nनित्यं च समचित्तत्वमिष्टानिष्टोपपत्तिषु ॥ ९ ॥","t":"...non-attachment, not being obsessed with family or home, and maintaining a constant equal mind regardless of whether good or bad things happen..."},{"ref":"13.10","s":"मयि चानन्ययोगेन भक्तिरव्यभिचारिणी ।\nविविक्तदेशसेवित्वमरतिर्जनसंसदि ॥ १० ॥","t":"...unswerving devotion to Me, preferring quiet places, and not seeking the constant company of crowds..."},{"ref":"13.11","s":"अध्यात्मज्ञाननित्यत्वं तत्त्वज्ञानार्थदर्शनम् ।\nएतज्ज्ञानमिति प्रोक्तमज्ञानं यदतोऽन्यथा ॥ ११ ॥","t":"...constant focus on the knowledge of the Self and understanding the purpose of knowing the truth—this is what I call Knowledge. Everything else is ignorance."},{"ref":"13.12","s":"ज्ञेयं यत्तत्प्रवक्ष्यामि यज्ज्ञात्वामृतमश्नुते ।\nअनादिमत्परं ब्रह्म न सत्तन्नासदुच्यते ॥ १२ ॥","t":"I will now tell you what is to be known, which leads to immortality: the beginningless Absolute (Brahman), which is beyond both 'existing' and 'not existing.'"},{"ref":"13.13","s":"सर्वतःपाणिपादं तत्सर्वतोऽक्षिशिरोमुखम् ।\nसर्वतःश्रुतिमल्लोके सर्वमावृत्य तिष्ठति ॥ १३ ॥","t":"That Absolute has hands, feet, eyes, heads, and mouths everywhere. It exists in the world by surrounding and filling everything."},{"ref":"13.14","s":"सर्वेन्द्रियगुणाभासं सर्वेन्द्रियविवर्जितम् ।\nअसक्तं सर्वभृच्चैव निर्गुणं गुणभोक्तृ च ॥ १४ ॥","t":"It seems to have the qualities of all the senses, yet it has no senses. It is unattached, yet it supports everything. It has no qualities, yet it experiences all qualities."},{"ref":"13.15","s":"बहिरन्तश्च भूतानामचरं चरमेव च ।\nसूक्ष्मत्वात्तदविज्ञेयं दूरस्थं चान्तिके च तत् ॥ १५ ॥","t":"It is both outside and inside all beings. It is both unmoving and moving. It is too subtle to be seen. It is far away, yet it is right here."},{"ref":"13.16","s":"अविभक्तं च भूतेषु विभक्तमिव च स्थितम् ।\nभूतभर्तृ च तज्ज्ञेयं ग्रसिष्णु प्रभविष्णु च ॥ १६ ॥","t":"It is undivided, yet it appears divided among all beings. It should be known as the sustainer, the consumer, and the creator of all."},{"ref":"13.17","s":"ज्योतिषामपि तज्ज्योतिस्तमसः परमुच्यते ।\nज्ञानं ज्ञेयं ज्ञानगम्यं हृदि सर्वस्य विष्ठितम् ॥ १७ ॥","t":"It is the Light of all lights, and it is said to be beyond all darkness. It is Knowledge itself, the Object of knowledge, and the Goal of knowledge, living in the hearts of all."},{"ref":"13.18","s":"इति क्षेत्रं तथा ज्ञानं ज्ञेयं चोक्तं समासतः ।\nमद्भक्त एतद्विज्ञाय मद्भावायोपपद्यते ॥ १८ ॥","t":"Thus I have briefly described the Field, Knowledge, and what is to be Known. My devotee, understanding this, becomes fit to reach My state of being."},{"ref":"13.19","s":"प्रकृतिं पुरुषं चैव विद्ध्यनादी उभावपि ।\nविकारांश्च गुणांश्चैव विद्धि प्रकृतिसम्भवान् ॥ १९ ॥","t":"Understand that both Material Nature (Prakriti) and Spirit (Purusha) are without beginning. All changes and qualities are born from Material Nature."},{"ref":"13.20","s":"कार्यकरणकर्तृत्वे हेतुः प्रकृतिरुच्यते ।\nपुरुषः सुखदुःखानां भोक्तृत्वे हेतुरुच्यते ॥ २० ॥","t":"Material Nature is the cause behind all physical actions and instruments. Spirit is the cause behind the experience of pleasure and pain."},{"ref":"13.21","s":"पुरुषः प्रकृतिस्थो हि भुङ्क्ते प्रकृतिजान्गुणान् ।\nकारणं गुणसङ्गोऽस्य सदसद्योनिजन्मसु ॥ २१ ॥","t":"Spirit, when living in Material Nature, experiences the qualities born of that nature. Attachment to these qualities is what causes rebirth in good or bad situations."},{"ref":"13.22","s":"उपद्रष्टानुमन्ता च भर्ता भोक्ता महेश्वरः ।\nपरमात्मेति चाप्युक्तो देहेऽस्मिन्पुरुषः परः ॥ २२ ॥","t":"The Supreme Spirit in this body is also called the Witness, the Consenter, the Sustainer, the Enjoyer, the Great Lord, and the Highest Self."},{"ref":"13.23","s":"य एवं वेत्ति पुरुषं प्रकृतिं च गुणैः सह ।\nसर्वथा वर्तमानोऽपि न स भूयोऽभिजायते ॥ २३ ॥","t":"Anyone who truly understands the Spirit and Material Nature along with its qualities, will not be born again, no matter how they are currently living."},{"ref":"13.24","s":"ध्यानेनात्मनि पश्यन्ति केचिदात्मानमात्मना ।\nअन्ये साङ्ख्येन योगेन कर्मयोगेन चापरे ॥ २४ ॥","t":"Some see the Self through meditation, others through analytical logic (Sankhya), and still others through the Yoga of action."},{"ref":"13.25","s":"अन्ये त्वेवमजानन्तः श्रुत्वान्येभ्य उपासते ।\nतेऽपि चातितरन्त्येव मृत्युं श्रुतिपरायणाः ॥ २५ ॥","t":"Others, even if they don't know these paths, worship after hearing about them from others. They too certainly cross beyond death by being devoted to what they have heard."},{"ref":"13.26","s":"यावत्सञ्जायते किञ्चित्सत्त्वं स्थावरजङ्गमम् ।\nक्षेत्रक्षेत्रज्ञसंयोगात्तद्विद्धि भरतर्षभ ॥ २६ ॥","t":"Arjuna, understand that every single being that is born—whether it moves or stays still—comes from the union of the Field and the Knower of the Field."},{"ref":"13.27","s":"समं सर्वेषु भूतेषु तिष्ठन्तं परमेश्वरम् ।\nविनश्यत्स्वविनश्यन्तं यः पश्यति स पश्यति ॥ २७ ॥","t":"One who sees the Supreme Lord living equally in all beings—never dying even when they die—truly sees the reality."},{"ref":"13.28","s":"समं पश्यन्हि सर्वत्र समवस्थितमीश्वरम् ।\nन हिनस्त्यात्मनात्मानं ततो याति परां गतिम् ॥ २८ ॥","t":"By seeing the Lord established equally everywhere, one does not destroy the self with the self, and thus reaches the highest goal."},{"ref":"13.29","s":"प्रकृत्यैव च कर्माणि क्रियमाणानि सर्वशः ।\nयः पश्यति तथात्मानमकर्तारं स पश्यति ॥ २९ ॥","t":"One who sees that all actions are performed entirely by Material Nature, and that the Self is not the doer, truly sees."},{"ref":"13.30","s":"यदा भूतपृथग्भावमेकस्थमनुपश्यति ।\nतत एव च विस्तारं ब्रह्म सम्पद्यते तदा ॥ ३० ॥","t":"When one sees that the various states of all beings are rooted in the One, and expand from that One, then they attain the Absolute."},{"ref":"13.31","s":"अनादित्वान्निर्गुणत्वात्परमात्मायमव्ययः ।\nशरीरस्थोऽपि कौन्तेय न करोति न लिप्यते ॥ ३१ ॥","t":"Because it is beginningless and free from qualities, this eternal Supreme Self does nothing and is never stained, even while living in the body."},{"ref":"13.32","s":"यथा सर्वगतं सौक्ष्म्यादाकाशं नोपलिप्यते ।\nसर्वत्रावस्थितो देहे तथात्मा नोपलिप्यते ॥ ३२ ॥","t":"Just as space is present everywhere but is never stained because it is so subtle, so is the Self present in the whole body without ever being tainted."},{"ref":"13.33","s":"यथा प्रकाशयत्येकः कृत्स्नं लोकमिमं रविः ।\nक्षेत्रं क्षेत्री तथा कृत्स्नं प्रकाशयति भारत ॥ ३३ ॥","t":"Just as the single sun lights up the entire world, so does the Knower of the Field light up this entire Field, Arjuna."},{"ref":"13.34","s":"क्षेत्रक्षेत्रज्ञयोरेवमन्तरं ज्ञानचक्षुषा ।\nभूतप्रकृतिमोक्षं च ये विदुर्यान्ति ते परम् ॥ ३४ ॥","t":"Those who use the eye of wisdom to see the difference between the Field (matter) and the Knower of the Field (awareness), and who understand how beings are freed from material nature — they reach the supreme goal."},{"ref":"14.1","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nपरं भूयः प्रवक्ष्यामि ज्ञानानां ज्ञानमुत्तमम् ।\nयज्ज्ञात्वा मुनयः सर्वे परां सिद्धिमितो गताः ॥ १ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: I will tell you once more about the supreme knowledge—the best of all wisdom. Knowing this, the sages have reached the highest perfection."},{"ref":"14.2","s":"इदं ज्ञानमुपाश्रित्य मम साधर्म्यमागताः ।\nसर्गेऽपि नोपजायन्ते प्रलये न व्यथन्ति च ॥ २ ॥","t":"By following this knowledge and reaching My same nature, these souls are not born at the start of creation and are not disturbed at the time of dissolution."},{"ref":"14.3","s":"मम योनिर्महद्ब्रह्म तस्मिन्गर्भं दधाम्यहम् ।\nसम्भवः सर्वभूतानां ततो भवति भारत ॥ ३ ॥","t":"The great Nature (Brahman) is My womb, and I place the seed of consciousness within it. From this union, all living beings are born, Arjuna."},{"ref":"14.4","s":"सर्वयोनिषु कौन्तेय मूर्तयः सम्भवन्ति याः ।\nतासां ब्रह्म महद्योनिरहं बीजप्रदः पिता ॥ ४ ॥","t":"Whatever forms are born in any womb, Arjuna, the great Nature is their mother, and I am the father who provides the seed."},{"ref":"14.5","s":"सत्त्वं रजस्तम इति गुणाः प्रकृतिसम्भवाः ।\nनिबध्नन्ति महाबाहो देहे देहिनमव्ययम् ॥ ५ ॥","t":"Goodness (Sattva), Passion (Rajas), and Dullness (Tamas) are the three qualities born of Nature. They bind the eternal soul to the physical body, Arjuna."},{"ref":"14.6","s":"तत्र सत्त्वं निर्मलत्वात्प्रकाशकमनामयम् ।\nसुखसङ्गेन बध्नाति ज्ञानसङ्गेन चानघ ॥ ६ ॥","t":"Among these, Sattva (Goodness) is pure, illuminating, and healthy. But it binds the soul through attachment to happiness and knowledge."},{"ref":"14.7","s":"रजो रागात्मकं विद्धि तृष्णासङ्गसमुद्भवम् ।\nतन्निबध्नाति कौन्तेय कर्मसङ्गेन देहिनम् ॥ ७ ॥","t":"Rajas (Passion) is driven by craving and attachment. It binds the soul, Arjuna, through an obsession with action and work."},{"ref":"14.8","s":"तमस्त्वज्ञानजं विद्धि मोहनं सर्वदेहिनाम् ।\nप्रमादालस्यनिद्राभिस्तन्निबध्नाति भारत ॥ ८ ॥","t":"Tamas (Dullness) is born of ignorance and confuses all living beings. It binds the soul through negligence, laziness, and excessive sleep, Arjuna."},{"ref":"14.9","s":"सत्त्वं सुखे सञ्जयति रजः कर्मणि भारत ।\nज्ञानमावृत्य तु तमः प्रमादे सञ्जयत्युत ॥ ९ ॥","t":"Sattva attaches you to happiness; Rajas attaches you to work; and Tamas, by hiding your knowledge, attaches you to mistakes and negligence."},{"ref":"14.10","s":"रजस्तमश्चाभिभूय सत्त्वं भवति भारत ।\nरजः सत्त्वं तमश्चैव तमः सत्त्वं रजस्तथा ॥ १० ॥","t":"Sometimes Sattva dominates by overcoming Rajas and Tamas. At other times Rajas dominates, and sometimes Tamas prevails."},{"ref":"14.11","s":"सर्वद्वारेषु देहेऽस्मिन्प्रकाश उपजायते ।\nज्ञानं यदा तदा विद्याद्विवृद्धं सत्त्वमित्युत ॥ ११ ॥","t":"When the light of wisdom shines through all the senses of the body, then you can be sure that Sattva is dominating."},{"ref":"14.12","s":"लोभः प्रवृत्तिरारम्भः कर्मणामशमः स्पृहा ।\nरजस्येतानि जायन्ते विवृद्धे भरतर्षभ ॥ १२ ॥","t":"Greed, restless activity, starting too many projects, lack of peace, and intense longing—these are the signs that Rajas is dominating, Arjuna."},{"ref":"14.13","s":"अप्रकाशोऽप्रवृत्तिश्च प्रमादो मोह एव च ।\nतमस्येतानि जायन्ते विवृद्धे कुरुनन्दन ॥ १३ ॥","t":"Mental darkness, inactivity, negligence, and total confusion—these are the signs that Tamas is dominating, Arjuna."},{"ref":"14.14","s":"यदा सत्त्वे प्रवृद्धे तु प्रलयं याति देहभृत् ।\nतदोत्तमविदां लोकानमलान्प्रतिपद्यते ॥ १४ ॥","t":"If a person dies while Sattva is strong, they reach the higher, pure worlds of those who know the Truth."},{"ref":"14.15","s":"रजसि प्रलयं गत्वा कर्मसङ्गिषु जायते ।\nतथा प्रलीनस्तमसि मूढयोनिषु जायते ॥ १५ ॥","t":"If one dies while Rajas is strong, they are born again among those obsessed with work. If one dies in Tamas, they are born into the worlds of the confused."},{"ref":"14.16","s":"कर्मणः सुकृतस्याहुः सात्त्विकं निर्मलं फलम् ।\nरजसस्तु फलं दुःखमज्ञानं तमसः फलम् ॥ १६ ॥","t":"The result of a good action is pure and 'Sattvic.' The result of Rajas is pain, and the result of Tamas is ignorance."},{"ref":"14.17","s":"सत्त्वात्सञ्जायते ज्ञानं रजसो लोभ एव च ।\nप्रमादमोहौ तमसो भवतोऽज्ञानमेव च ॥ १७ ॥","t":"From Sattva comes wisdom; from Rajas comes greed; and from Tamas come negligence, confusion, and ignorance."},{"ref":"14.18","s":"ऊर्ध्वं गच्छन्ति सत्त्वस्था मध्ये तिष्ठन्ति राजसाः ।\nजघन्यगुणवृत्तिस्था अधो गच्छन्ति तामसाः ॥ १८ ॥","t":"Those in Sattva move upward; those in Rajas stay in the middle; and those in Tamas sink downward."},{"ref":"14.19","s":"नान्यं गुणेभ्यः कर्तारं यदा द्रष्टानुपश्यति ।\nगुणेभ्यश्च परं वेत्ति मद्भावं सोऽधिगच्छति ॥ १९ ॥","t":"When an observer sees that only these three qualities are acting, and knows what is beyond them, they reach My state of being."},{"ref":"14.20","s":"गुणानेतानतीत्य त्रीन्देही देहसमुद्भवान् ।\nजन्ममृत्युजरादुःखैर्विमुक्तोऽमृतमश्नुते ॥ २० ॥","t":"Having risen above these three qualities that create the body, the soul is freed from birth, death, old age, and sorrow, and tastes immortality."},{"ref":"14.21","s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nकैर्लिङ्गैस्त्रीन्गुणानेतानतीतो भवति प्रभो ।\nकिमाचारः कथं चैतांस्त्रीन्गुणानतिवर्तते ॥ २१ ॥","t":"Arjuna asked: What are the signs of a person who has risen above these three qualities, Krishna? How do they behave, and how did they get past these forces?"},{"ref":"14.22","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nप्रकाशं च प्रवृत्तिं च मोहमेव च पाण्डव ।\nन द्वेष्टि सम्प्रवृत्तानि न निवृत्तानि काङ्क्षति ॥ २२ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: One who does not hate clarity, activity, or confusion when they arise, and doesn't crave them when they are gone..."},{"ref":"14.23","s":"उदासीनवदासीनो गुणैर्यो न विचाल्यते ।\nगुणा वर्तन्त इत्येव योऽवतिष्ठति नेङ्गते ॥ २३ ॥","t":"...one who sits like a neutral observer and is not moved by the qualities, knowing that 'it is just the qualities acting,' and stays steady..."},{"ref":"14.24","s":"समदुःखसुखः स्वस्थः समलोष्टाश्मकाञ्चनः ।\nतुल्यप्रियाप्रियो धीरस्तुल्यनिन्दात्मसंस्तुतिः ॥ २४ ॥","t":"...to whom pain and pleasure are the same, who is self-contained, to whom dirt, stone, and gold are equal, and who remains the same in both praise and criticism..."},{"ref":"14.25","s":"मानापमानयोस्तुल्यस्तुल्यो मित्रारिपक्षयोः ।\nसर्वारम्भपरित्यागी गुणातीतः स उच्यते ॥ २५ ॥","t":"...who is equal in honor and disgrace, who treats friend and enemy the same, and who has given up all selfish projects—that person is said to have risen above the qualities."},{"ref":"14.26","s":"मां च योऽव्यभिचारेण भक्तियोगेन सेवते ।\nस गुणान्समतीत्यैतान्ब्रह्मभूयाय कल्पते ॥ २६ ॥","t":"And one who serves Me with unswerving devotion rises above these three qualities and becomes fit to be the Absolute."},{"ref":"14.27","s":"ब्रह्मणो हि प्रतिष्ठाहममृतस्याव्ययस्य च ।\nशाश्वतस्य च धर्मस्य सुखस्यैकान्तिकस्य च ॥ २७ ॥","t":"For I am the foundation of the Absolute, the source of immortality and eternal Dharma, and the home of absolute happiness."},{"ref":"15.1","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nऊर्ध्वमूलमधःशाखमश्वत्थं प्राहुरव्ययम् ।\nछन्दांसि यस्य पर्णानि यस्तं वेद स वेदवित् ॥ १ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: They speak of an eternal Ashvattha (fig) tree with its roots above and its branches below. Its leaves are the ancient songs of wisdom. One who truly understands this tree knows the essence of all knowledge."},{"ref":"15.2","s":"अधश्चोर्ध्वं प्रसृतास्तस्य शाखा\nगुणप्रवृद्धा विषयप्रवालाः ।\nअधश्च मूलान्यनुसन्ततानि\nकर्मानुबन्धीनि मनुष्यलोके ॥ २ ॥","t":"Its branches spread upward and downward, nourished by the qualities of nature. Sensory objects are its new shoots. Its roots also grow downward, binding people to their actions in the human world."},{"ref":"15.3","s":"न रूपमस्येह तथोपलभ्यते\nनान्तो न चादिर्न च सम्प्रतिष्ठा ।\nअश्वत्थमेनं सुविरूढमूल-\nमसङ्गशस्त्रेण दृढेन छित्त्वा ॥ ३ ॥","t":"Its true form is not perceived here—neither its end, nor its beginning, nor its foundation. One must cut down this firm-rooted tree with the strong sword of non-attachment."},{"ref":"15.4","s":"ततः पदं तत्परिमार्गितव्यं\nयस्मिन्गता न निवर्तन्ति भूयः ।\nतमेव चाद्यं पुरुषं प्रपद्ये\nयतः प्रवृत्तिः प्रसृता पुराणी ॥ ४ ॥","t":"Then one should seek that state from which there is no return, saying: 'I take refuge in that original Spirit from which this ancient cosmic activity first began.'"},{"ref":"15.5","s":"निर्मानमोहा जितसङ्गदोषा\nअध्यात्मनित्या विनिवृत्तकामाः ।\nद्वन्द्वैर्विमुक्ताः सुखदुःखसंज्ञैर्-\nगच्छन्त्यमूढाः पदमव्ययं तत् ॥ ५ ॥","t":"Free from pride and delusion, having conquered the flaw of attachment, always focused on the Self, with desires gone, and free from the dualities of pleasure and pain—the wise reach that unchanging goal."},{"ref":"15.6","s":"न तद्भासयते सूर्यो न शशाङ्को न पावकः ।\nयद्गत्वा न निवर्तन्ते तद्धाम परमं मम ॥ ६ ॥","t":"Neither the sun, nor the moon, nor fire lights up that state. Once you reach it, you never return; that is My supreme home."},{"ref":"15.7","s":"ममैवांशो जीवलोके जीवभूतः सनातनः ।\nमनःषष्ठानीन्द्रियाणि प्रकृतिस्थानि कर्षति ॥ ७ ॥","t":"A small part of Myself becomes the eternal living soul in the world. It draws to itself the five senses and the mind, which are rooted in nature."},{"ref":"15.8","s":"शरीरं यदवाप्नोति यच्चाप्युत्क्रामतीश्वरः ।\nगृहीत्वैतानि संयाति वायुर्गन्धानिवाशयात् ॥ ८ ॥","t":"When the soul (the master) takes a body, or when it leaves it, it carries these senses and the mind along with it, just as the wind carries a scent from its source."},{"ref":"15.9","s":"श्रोत्रं चक्षुः स्पर्शनं च रसनं घ्राणमेव च ।\nअधिष्ठाय मनश्चायं विषयानुपसेवते ॥ ९ ॥","t":"The soul uses the ears, eyes, skin, tongue, and nose, along with the mind, to experience the objects of the world."},{"ref":"15.10","s":"उत्क्रामन्तं स्थितं वापि भुञ्जानं वा गुणान्वितम् ।\nविमूढा नानुपश्यन्ति पश्यन्ति ज्ञानचक्षुषः ॥ १० ॥","t":"The confused do not see the soul as it lives, leaves, or experiences life through the qualities of nature. But those who have the 'eye of knowledge' can see it clearly."},{"ref":"15.11","s":"यतन्तो योगिनश्चैनं पश्यन्त्यात्मन्यवस्थितम् ।\nयतन्तोऽप्यकृतात्मानो नैनं पश्यन्त्यचेतसः ॥ ११ ॥","t":"Disciplined practitioners can see the Self living within them. But those who are not disciplined and lack awareness cannot see it, no matter how hard they try."},{"ref":"15.12","s":"यदादित्यगतं तेजो जगद्भासयतेऽखिलम् ।\nयच्चन्द्रमसि यच्चाग्नौ तत्तेजो विद्धि मामकम् ॥ १२ ॥","t":"Understand that the brilliance in the sun that lights up the world, the light in the moon, and the heat in fire—all that power comes from Me."},{"ref":"15.13","s":"गामाविश्य च भूतानि धारयाम्यहमोजसा ।\nपुष्णामि चौषधीः सर्वाः सोमो भूत्वा रसात्मकः ॥ १३ ॥","t":"I enter the earth and support all beings with My vital energy. As the moon, I provide the life-giving sap that nourishes all plants."},{"ref":"15.14","s":"अहं वैश्वानरो भूत्वा प्राणिनां देहमाश्रितः ।\nप्राणापानसमायुक्तः पचाम्यन्नं चतुर्विधम् ॥ १४ ॥","t":"I become the fire of digestion in the bodies of all living beings. Working with the breath, I digest the four types of food."},{"ref":"15.15","s":"सर्वस्य चाहं हृदि सन्निविष्टो\nमत्तः स्मृतिर्ज्ञानमपोहनं च ।\nवेदैश्च सर्वैरहमेव वेद्यो\nवेदान्तकृद्वेदविदेव चाहम् ॥ १५ ॥","t":"I live in the hearts of everyone. From Me come memory, knowledge, and even forgetfulness. I am the goal of all the Vedas, the creator of the final truth, and the only one who truly knows the scriptures."},{"ref":"15.16","s":"द्वाविमौ पुरुषौ लोके क्षरश्चाक्षर एव च ।\nक्षरः सर्वाणि भूतानि कूटस्थोऽक्षर उच्यते ॥ १६ ॥","t":"There are two types of spirits in this world: the Perishable and the Imperishable. All physical beings are Perishable; the unchanging core is the Imperishable."},{"ref":"15.17","s":"उत्तमः पुरुषस्त्वन्यः परमात्मेत्युदाहृतः ।\nयो लोकत्रयमाविश्य बिभर्त्यव्यय ईश्वरः ॥ १७ ॥","t":"But there is a third, the Supreme Person (Purushottama), known as the Highest Self. He enters the three worlds and supports them as the eternal Lord."},{"ref":"15.18","s":"यस्मात्क्षरमतीतोऽहमक्षरादपि चोत्तमः ।\nअतोऽस्मि लोके वेदे च प्रथितः पुरुषोत्तमः ॥ १८ ॥","t":"Because I am beyond the Perishable and higher than the Imperishable, I am known in the world and in the scriptures as the Supreme Person (Purushottama)."},{"ref":"15.19","s":"यो मामेवमसम्मूढो जानाति पुरुषोत्तमम् ।\nस सर्वविद्भजति मां सर्वभावेन भारत ॥ १९ ॥","t":"Arjuna, anyone who truly knows Me as this Supreme Person is free from confusion. That person knows everything and worships Me with their whole heart."},{"ref":"15.20","s":"इति गुह्यतमं शास्त्रमिदमुक्तं मयानघ ।\nएतद्बुद्ध्वा बुद्धिमान्स्यात्कृतकृत्यश्च भारत ॥ २० ॥","t":"This is the most secret teaching I have given you, Arjuna. Anyone who truly understands it becomes wise and has fulfilled all that needs to be done."},{"ref":"16.1","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nअभयं सत्त्वसंशुद्धिर्ज्ञानयोगव्यवस्थितिः ।\nदानं दमश्च यज्ञश्च स्वाध्यायस्तप आर्जवम् ॥ १ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: Fearlessness, purity of heart, steadfastness in knowledge, charity, self-control, sacrifice, study, discipline, and honesty..."},{"ref":"16.2","s":"अहिंसा सत्यमक्रोधस्त्यागः शान्तिरपैशुनम् ।\nदया भूतेष्वलोलुप्त्वं मार्दवं ह्रीरचापलम् ॥ २ ॥","t":"...non-violence, truth, freedom from anger, renunciation, peace, aversion to gossip, compassion, lack of greed, gentleness, modesty, and stability..."},{"ref":"16.3","s":"तेजः क्षमा धृतिः शौचमद्रोहो नातिमानिता ।\nभवन्ति सम्पदं दैवीमभिजातस्य भारत ॥ ३ ॥","t":"...vigor, forgiveness, firmness, purity, lack of malice, and no excessive pride—these belong to those born with a divine nature, Arjuna."},{"ref":"16.4","s":"दम्भो दर्पोऽभिमानश्च क्रोधः पारुष्यमेव च ।\nअज्ञानं चाभिजातस्य पार्थ सम्पदमासुरीम् ॥ ४ ॥","t":"Hypocrisy, arrogance, pride, anger, harshness, and ignorance belong to those born with a demonic nature, Arjuna."},{"ref":"16.5","s":"दैवी सम्पद्विमोक्षाय निबन्धायासुरी मता ।\nमा शुचः सम्पदं दैवीमभिजातोऽसि पाण्डव ॥ ५ ॥","t":"The divine nature leads to freedom, while the demonic nature leads to bondage. Do not worry, Arjuna; you are born with the divine nature."},{"ref":"16.6","s":"द्वौ भूतसर्गौ लोकेऽस्मिन्दैव आसुर एव च ।\nदैवो विस्तरशः प्रोक्त आसुरं पार्थ मे शृणु ॥ ६ ॥","t":"There are two types of beings in this world: the divine and the demonic. I have described the divine at length; now hear about the demonic, Arjuna."},{"ref":"16.7","s":"प्रवृत्तिं च निवृत्तिं च जना न विदुरासुराः ।\nन शौचं नापि चाचारो न सत्यं तेषु विद्यते ॥ ७ ॥","t":"Demonic people do not know what is right to do or what is right to avoid. They have no purity, no integrity, and no truth within them."},{"ref":"16.8","s":"असत्यमप्रतिष्ठं ते जगदाहुरनीश्वरम् ।\nअपरस्परसम्भूतं किमन्यत्कामहैतुकम् ॥ ८ ॥","t":"They say the universe has no truth, no moral foundation, and no Lord—that it is just a product of lust and chance, with no other purpose."},{"ref":"16.9","s":"एतां दृष्टिमवष्टभ्य नष्टात्मानोऽल्पबुद्धयः ।\nप्रभवन्त्युग्रकर्माणः क्षयाय जगतोऽहिताः ॥ ९ ॥","t":"Holding this view, these ruined souls with little intelligence do terrible things and become enemies of the world, working for its destruction."},{"ref":"16.10","s":"काममाश्रित्य दुष्पूरं दम्भमानमदान्विताः ।\nमोहाद्गृहीत्वासद्ग्राहान्प्रवर्तन्तेऽशुचिव्रताः ॥ १० ॥","t":"Driven by insatiable desire, full of hypocrisy and arrogance, they hold false views and act with impure motives."},{"ref":"16.11","s":"चिन्तामपरिमेयां च प्रलयान्तामुपाश्रिताः ।\nकामोपभोगपरमा एतावदिति निश्चिताः ॥ ११ ॥","t":"Filled with endless worries that only end at death, they think that satisfying their desires is the only goal of life."},{"ref":"16.12","s":"आशापाशशतैर्बद्धाः कामक्रोधपरायणाः ।\nईहन्ते कामभोगार्थमन्यायेनार्थसञ्चयान् ॥ १२ ॥","t":"Bound by hundreds of hopes, driven by desire and anger, they try to pile up wealth by any means necessary just to satisfy their cravings."},{"ref":"16.13","s":"इदमद्य मया लब्धमिमं प्राप्स्ये मनोरथम् ।\nइदमस्तीदमपि मे भविष्यति पुनर्धनम् ॥ १३ ॥","t":"'I gained this today; I will get that tomorrow. This wealth is mine now, and I will have even more in the future.'"},{"ref":"16.14","s":"असौ मया हतः शत्रुर्हनिष्ये चापरानपि ।\nईश्वरोऽहमहं भोगी सिद्धोऽहं बलवान्सुखी ॥ १४ ॥","t":"'I killed that enemy, and I will kill the others too. I am the lord, I am the enjoyer, I am successful, powerful, and happy.'"},{"ref":"16.15","s":"आढ्योऽभिजनवानस्मि कोऽन्योऽस्ति सदृशो मया ।\nयक्ष्ये दास्यामि मोदिष्य इत्यज्ञानविमोहिताः ॥ १५ ॥","t":"'I am rich and well-born; who is equal to me? I will perform rituals, I will give charity, and I will celebrate.' They are blinded by their own ignorance."},{"ref":"16.16","s":"अनेकचित्तविभ्रान्ता मोहजालसमावृताः ।\nप्रसक्ताः कामभोगेषु पतन्ति नरकेऽशुचौ ॥ १६ ॥","t":"Confused by many thoughts and caught in the net of delusion, they are addicted to sensory pleasures and fall into a foul state of suffering."},{"ref":"16.17","s":"आत्मसम्भाविताः स्तब्धा धनमानमदान्विताः ।\nयजन्ते नामयज्ञैस्ते दम्भेनाविधिपूर्वकम् ॥ १७ ॥","t":"Arrogant, stubborn, and drunk on their wealth, they perform rituals only for show, with no regard for the real rules or spirit of the act."},{"ref":"16.18","s":"अहङ्कारं बलं दर्पं कामं क्रोधं च संश्रिताः ।\nमामात्मपरदेहेषु प्रद्विषन्तोऽभ्यसूयकाः ॥ १८ ॥","t":"Obsessed with ego, power, pride, desire, and anger, these people hate Me—the life-force living in their own bodies and in the bodies of others."},{"ref":"16.19","s":"तानहं द्विषतः क्रूरान्संसारेषु नराधमान् ।\nक्षिपाम्यजस्रमशुभानासुरीष्वेव योनिषु ॥ १९ ॥","t":"I throw these hateful and cruel people, who are the lowest of humans, back into the repetitive and difficult cycles of existence."},{"ref":"16.20","s":"आसुरीं योनिमापन्ना मूढा जन्मनि जन्मनि ।\nमामप्राप्यैव कौन्तेय ततो यान्त्यधमां गतिम् ॥ २० ॥","t":"Entering these difficult paths birth after birth, these confused souls never reach Me and continue to fall into lower states."},{"ref":"16.21","s":"त्रिविधं नरकस्येदं द्वारं नाशनमात्मनः ।\nकामः क्रोधस्तथा लोभस्तस्मादेतत्त्रयं त्यजेत् ॥ २१ ॥","t":"There are three gates to this internal hell that destroy the soul: Desire, Anger, and Greed. Therefore, you must give up these three."},{"ref":"16.22","s":"एतैर्विमुक्तः कौन्तेय तमोद्वारैस्त्रिभिर्नरः ।\nआचरत्यात्मनः श्रेयस्ततो याति परां गतिम् ॥ २२ ॥","t":"Arjuna, a person who is freed from these three gates of darkness does what is best for their own self and eventually reaches the highest goal."},{"ref":"16.23","s":"यः शास्त्रविधिमुत्सृज्य वर्तते कामकारतः ।\nन स सिद्धिमवाप्नोति न सुखं न परां गतिम् ॥ २३ ॥","t":"Anyone who ignores the proven rules of life and acts only on their temporary impulses will never reach perfection, happiness, or the supreme goal."},{"ref":"16.24","s":"तस्माच्छास्त्रं प्रमाणं ते कार्याकार्यव्यवस्थितौ ।\nज्ञात्वा शास्त्रविधानोक्तं कर्म कर्तुमिहार्हसि ॥ २४ ॥","t":"Therefore, let the First Principles (Shastra) be your guide in deciding what to do and what to avoid. Knowing these rules, you should perform your work in this world."},{"ref":"17.1","s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nये शास्त्रविधिमुत्सृज्य यजन्ते श्रद्धयान्विताः ।\nतेषां निष्ठा तु का कृष्ण सत्त्वमाहो रजस्तमः ॥ १ ॥","t":"Arjuna asked: Krishna, what is the state of those who ignore the formal rules of scriptures but still perform their work with faith? Is their nature pure (Sattva), passionate (Rajas), or dull (Tamas)?"},{"ref":"17.2","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nत्रिविधा भवति श्रद्धा देहिनां सा स्वभावजा ।\nसात्त्विकी राजसी चैव तामसी चेति तां शृणु ॥ २ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: The faith of living beings is of three kinds, depending on their own inherent nature: it can be pure (Sattvic), passionate (Rajasic), or dull (Tamasic). Listen to the details."},{"ref":"17.3","s":"सत्त्वानुरूपा सर्वस्य श्रद्धा भवति भारत ।\nश्रद्धामयोऽयं पुरुषो यो यच्छ्रद्धः स एव सः ॥ ३ ॥","t":"Everyone's faith matches their own inner nature, Arjuna. A person is essentially what their faith is; as their faith is, so are they."},{"ref":"17.4","s":"यजन्ते सात्त्विका देवान्यक्षरक्षांसि राजसाः ।\nप्रेतान्भूतगणांश्चान्ये यजन्ते तामसा जनाः ॥ ४ ॥","t":"Pure (Sattvic) people focus on the divine powers; passionate (Rajasic) people focus on power and wealth; and dull (Tamasic) people focus on ghosts and lower spirits."},{"ref":"17.5","s":"अशास्त्रविहितं घोरं तप्यन्ते ये तपो जनाः ।\nदम्भाहङ्कारसंयुक्ताः कामरागबलान्विताः ॥ ५ ॥","t":"Some people perform severe and ego-driven austerities that are not recommended by wisdom, driven by hypocrisy, pride, desire, and attachment."},{"ref":"17.6","s":"कर्शयन्तः शरीरस्थं भूतग्राममचेतसः ।\nमां चैवान्तःशरीरस्थं तान्विद्ध्यासुरनिश्चयान् ॥ ६ ॥","t":"They senselessly torture their own bodies and the life-force within them—and even Me, who lives within. Know that their resolutions are destructive."},{"ref":"17.7","s":"आहारस्त्वपि सर्वस्य त्रिविधो भवति प्रियः ।\nयज्ञस्तपस्तथा दानं तेषां भेदमिमं शृणु ॥ ७ ॥","t":"Even the food people prefer, and their ways of contributing, practicing discipline, and giving, are of three kinds. Listen to the difference between them."},{"ref":"17.8","s":"आयुःसत्त्वबलारोग्यसुखप्रीतिविवर्धनाः ।\nरस्याः स्निग्धाः स्थिरा हृद्या आहाराः सात्त्विकप्रियाः ॥ ८ ॥","t":"Foods that increase life, energy, strength, health, happiness, and joy—foods that are juicy, smooth, substantial, and pleasant—are loved by the pure (Sattvic)."},{"ref":"17.9","s":"कट्वम्ललवणात्युष्णतीक्ष्णरूक्षविदाहिनः ।\nआहारा राजसस्येष्टा दुःखशोकामयप्रदाः ॥ ९ ॥","t":"Foods that are too bitter, sour, salty, hot, pungent, dry, or burning—which cause pain, grief, and disease—are preferred by the passionate (Rajasic)."},{"ref":"17.10","s":"यातयामं गतरसं पूति पर्युषितं च यत् ।\nउच्छिष्टमपि चामेध्यं भोजनं तामसप्रियम् ॥ १० ॥","t":"Food that is stale, tasteless, smelly, left overnight, or impure, is what the dull (Tamasic) people love."},{"ref":"17.11","s":"अफलाकाङ्क्षिभिर्यज्ञो विधिदृष्टो य इज्यते ।\nयष्टव्यमेवेति मनः समाधाय स सात्त्विकः ॥ ११ ॥","t":"Work (sacrifice) that is done because it is a duty, without wanting any reward and with a focused mind, is pure (Sattvic)."},{"ref":"17.12","s":"अभिसन्धाय तु फलं दम्भार्थमपि चैव यत् ।\nइज्यते भरतश्रेष्ठ तं यज्ञं विद्धि राजसम् ॥ १२ ॥","t":"But work that is done only for show or with an eye on the reward, Arjuna, know that to be passionate (Rajasic)."},{"ref":"17.13","s":"विधिहीनमसृष्टान्नं मन्त्रहीनमदक्षिणम् ।\nश्रद्धाविरहितं यज्ञं तामसं परिचक्षते ॥ १३ ॥","t":"Work that ignores rules, shares nothing with others, has no wisdom, no integrity, and no faith, is called dull (Tamasic)."},{"ref":"17.14","s":"देवद्विजगुरुप्राज्ञपूजनं शौचमार्जवम् ।\nब्रह्मचर्यमहिंसा च शारीरं तप उच्यते ॥ १४ ॥","t":"Respecting the wise and the teachers, being pure, honest, self-controlled, and non-violent—this is called the discipline (tapas) of the body."},{"ref":"17.15","s":"अनुद्वेगकरं वाक्यं सत्यं प्रियहितं च यत् ।\nस्वाध्यायाभ्यसनं चैव वाङ्मयं तप उच्यते ॥ १५ ॥","t":"Speaking words that don't cause stress, that are true, pleasant, and helpful—and the regular study of wisdom—is called the discipline of speech."},{"ref":"17.16","s":"मनःप्रसादः सौम्यत्वं मौनमात्मविनिग्रहः ।\nभावसंशुद्धिरित्येतत्तपो मानसमुच्यते ॥ १६ ॥","t":"Mental peace, gentleness, silence, self-restraint, and purity of intent—this is called the discipline of the mind."},{"ref":"17.17","s":"श्रद्धया परया तप्तं तपस्तत्त्रिविधं नरैः ।\nअफलाकाङ्क्षिभिर्युक्तैः सात्त्विकं परिचक्षते ॥ १७ ॥","t":"This threefold discipline (body, speech, mind), when practiced with total trust by people who don't want rewards, is called pure (Sattvic)."},{"ref":"17.18","s":"सत्कारमानपूजार्थं तपो दम्भेन चैव यत् ।\nक्रियते तदिह प्रोक्तं राजसं चलमध्रुवम् ॥ १८ ॥","t":"Discipline that is done just to get respect, honor, or praise—and is done with hypocrisy—is passionate (Rajasic). It is unstable and doesn't last."},{"ref":"17.19","s":"मूढग्राहेणात्मनो यत्पीडया क्रियते तपः ।\nपरस्योत्सादनार्थं वा तत्तामसमुदाहृतम् ॥ १९ ॥","t":"Discipline done with a foolish intent, by hurting oneself or trying to destroy others, is called dull (Tamasic)."},{"ref":"17.20","s":"दातव्यमिति यद्दानं दीयतेऽनुपकारिणे ।\nदेशे काले च पात्रे च तद्दानं सात्त्विकं स्मृतम् ॥ २० ॥","t":"A gift given because 'it is right to give,' at the right time and place, to a worthy person who can do nothing in return, is a pure (Sattvic) gift."},{"ref":"17.21","s":"यत्तु प्रत्युपकारार्थं फलमुद्दिश्य वा पुनः ।\nदीयते च परिक्लिष्टं तद्दानं राजसं स्मृतम् ॥ २१ ॥","t":"But a gift given with the hope of getting something back, or for a specific result, or given with a heavy heart, is a passionate (Rajasic) gift."},{"ref":"17.22","s":"अदेशकाले यद्दानमपात्रेभ्यश्च दीयते ।\nअसत्कृतमवज्ञातं तत्तामसमुदाहृतम् ॥ २२ ॥","t":"A gift given at the wrong time or place, to an unworthy person, or given with disrespect and contempt, is a dull (Tamasic) gift."},{"ref":"17.23","s":"ॐ तत्सदिति निर्देशो ब्रह्मणस्त्रिविधः स्मृतः ।\nब्राह्मणास्तेन वेदाश्च यज्ञाश्च विहिताः पुरा ॥ २३ ॥","t":"'OM TAT SAT' is the threefold name of the Absolute. Since ancient times, it has been used to validate teachers, wisdom, and selfless work."},{"ref":"17.24","s":"तस्मादोमित्युदाहृत्य यज्ञदानतपःक्रियाः ।\nप्रवर्तन्ते विधानोक्ताः सततं ब्रह्मवादिनाम् ॥ २४ ॥","t":"Therefore, seekers of the Absolute always start their work, charity, and discipline by saying 'OM' as the rules recommend."},{"ref":"17.25","s":"तदित्यनभिसन्धाय फलं यज्ञतपःक्रियाः ।\nदानक्रियाश्च विविधाः क्रियन्ते मोक्षकाङ्क्षिभिः ॥ २५ ॥","t":"By saying 'TAT' (That), those who want freedom perform their work, discipline, and charity without wanting any personal reward."},{"ref":"17.26","s":"सद्भावे साधुभावे च सदित्येतत्प्रयुज्यते ।\nप्रशस्ते कर्मणि तथा सच्छब्दः पार्थ युज्यते ॥ २६ ॥","t":"The word 'SAT' is used to mean 'Existence' and 'Goodness.' Arjuna, it is also used to describe an excellent and auspicious action."},{"ref":"17.27","s":"यज्ञे तपसि दाने च स्थितिः सदिति चोच्यते ।\nकर्म चैव तदर्थीयं सदित्येवाभिधीयते ॥ २७ ॥","t":"Steadiness in work, discipline, and charity is also called 'SAT.' And any action done for that ultimate purpose is also called 'SAT.'"},{"ref":"17.28","s":"अश्रद्धया हुतं दत्तं तपस्तप्तं कृतं च यत् ।\nअसदित्युच्यते पार्थ न च तत्प्रेत्य नो इह ॥ २८ ॥","t":"Whatever is offered, given, or practiced without faith is called 'ASAT' (Non-existent), Arjuna. It has no value in this life or the next."},{"ref":"18.1","s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nसंन्यासस्य महाबाहो तत्त्वमिच्छामि वेदितुम् ।\nत्यागस्य च हृषीकेश पृथक्केशिनिषूदन ॥ १ ॥","t":"Arjuna asked: Krishna, I want to understand the true nature of renunciation (Sannyasa) and abandonment (Tyaga) individually. Please explain the difference between them."},{"ref":"18.2","s":"श्रीभगवानुवाच ।\nकाम्यानां कर्मणां न्यासं संन्यासं कवयो विदुः ।\nसर्वकर्मफलत्यागं प्राहुस्त्यागं विचक्षणाः ॥ २ ॥","t":"The Blessed Lord said: Sages call renunciation (Sannyasa) the giving up of selfishly motivated actions. The wise call abandonment (Tyaga) the giving up of the results of all actions."},{"ref":"18.3","s":"त्याज्यं दोषवदित्येके कर्म प्राहुर्मनीषिणः ।\nयज्ञदानतपःकर्म न त्याज्यमिति चापरे ॥ ३ ॥","t":"Some thinkers say all action should be given up as flawed; others say that sacrifice, charity, and discipline should never be abandoned."},{"ref":"18.4","s":"निश्चयं शृणु मे तत्र त्यागे भरतसत्तम ।\nत्यागो हि पुरुषव्याघ्र त्रिविधः सम्प्रकीर्तितः ॥ ४ ॥","t":"Listen to my final decision about abandonment, Arjuna. Abandonment has been declared to be of three kinds."},{"ref":"18.5","s":"यज्ञदानतपःकर्म न त्याज्यं कार्यमेव तत् ।\nयज्ञो दानं तपश्चैव पावनानि मनीषिणाम् ॥ ५ ॥","t":"Acts of contribution, charity, and discipline should not be given up; they must be performed. These actions are the purifiers of the wise."},{"ref":"18.6","s":"एतान्यपि तु कर्माणि सङ्गं त्यक्त्वा फलानि च ।\nकर्तव्यानीति मे पार्थ निश्चितं मतमुत्तमम् ॥ ६ ॥","t":"But even these actions must be done without attachment and without wanting rewards. This is my final and supreme conviction, Arjuna."},{"ref":"18.7","s":"नियतस्य तु संन्यासः कर्मणो नोपपद्यते ।\nमोहात्तस्य परित्यागस्तामसः परिकीर्तितः ॥ ७ ॥","t":"Giving up your necessary duties out of confusion is called dull (Tamasic) abandonment."},{"ref":"18.8","s":"दुःखमित्येव यत्कर्म कायक्लेशभयात्त्यजेत् ।\nस कृत्वा राजसं त्यागं नैव त्यागफलं लभेत् ॥ ८ ॥","t":"Giving up an action because it is difficult or because you fear physical pain is called passionate (Rajasic) abandonment. This doesn't lead to any real benefit."},{"ref":"18.9","s":"कार्यमित्येव यत्कर्म नियतं क्रियतेऽर्जुन ।\nसङ्गं त्यक्त्वा फलं चैव स त्यागः सात्त्विको मतः ॥ ९ ॥","t":"When a necessary duty is performed simply because 'it ought to be done,' and attachment to the result is given up—that is called pure (Sattvic) abandonment."},{"ref":"18.10","s":"न द्वेष्ट्यकुशलं कर्म कुशले नानुषज्जते ।\nत्यागी सत्त्वसमाविष्टो मेधावी छिन्नसंशयः ॥ १० ॥","t":"A person who is truly detached and wise neither hates unpleasant work nor is addicted to pleasant work. Their doubts are gone."},{"ref":"18.11","s":"न हि देहभृता शक्यं त्यक्तुं कर्माण्यशेषतः ।\nयस्तु कर्मफलत्यागी स त्यागीत्यभिधीयते ॥ ११ ॥","t":"It is impossible for a living being to give up all actions entirely. Therefore, the one who gives up the rewards of action is the true renouncer."},{"ref":"18.12","s":"अनिष्टमिष्टं मिश्रं च त्रिविधं कर्मणः फलम् ।\nभवत्यत्यागिनां प्रेत्य न तु संन्यासिनां क्वचित् ॥ १२ ॥","t":"The results of action are of three kinds: unpleasant, pleasant, and mixed. These results affect those who stay attached, but never those who have truly renounced their ego."},{"ref":"18.13","s":"पञ्चैतानि महाबाहो कारणानि निबोध मे ।\nसाङ्ख्ये कृतान्ते प्रोक्तानि सिद्धये सर्वकर्मणाम् ॥ १३ ॥","t":"Learn from Me, Arjuna, the five factors that are necessary for any action to be successful, according to the final analysis of action."},{"ref":"18.14","s":"अधिष्ठानं तथा कर्ता करणं च पृथग्विधम् ।\nविविधाश्च पृथक्चेष्टा दैवं चैवात्र पञ्चमम् ॥ १४ ॥","t":"The body (the base), the actor (the ego), the various tools (senses), the different efforts, and fifthly, destiny (the unknown variables)."},{"ref":"18.15","s":"शरीरवाङ्मनोभिर्यत्कर्म प्रारभते नरः ।\nन्याय्यं वा विपरीतं वा पञ्चैते तस्य हेतवः ॥ १५ ॥","t":"Whatever action a person starts with their body, speech, or mind—whether it is right or wrong—these five are always the causes."},{"ref":"18.16","s":"तत्रैवं सति कर्तारमात्मानं केवलं तु यः ।\nपश्यत्यकृतबुद्धित्वान्न स पश्यति दुर्मतिः ॥ १६ ॥","t":"Knowing this, if someone thinks that their 'Self' alone is the only doer, they are foolish and cannot see the truth."},{"ref":"18.17","s":"यस्य नाहङ्कृतो भावो बुद्धिर्यस्य न लिप्यते ।\nहत्वापि स इमाँल्लोकान्न हन्ति न निबध्यते ॥ १७ ॥","t":"One whose nature is free from ego and whose intellect is not tainted—even if they have to perform a violent act like killing, they do not truly kill and are not bound by it."},{"ref":"18.18","s":"ज्ञानं ज्ञेयं परिज्ञाता त्रिविधा कर्मचोदना ।\nकरणं कर्म कर्तेति त्रिविधः कर्मसङ्ग्रहः ॥ १८ ॥","t":"The knowledge, the object of knowledge, and the knower are the three things that trigger an action. The tool, the act, and the actor are the three things that make up the action."},{"ref":"18.19","s":"ज्ञानं कर्म च कर्ता च त्रिधैव गुणभेदतः ।\nप्रोच्यते गुणसङ्ख्याने यथावच्छृणु तान्यपि ॥ १९ ॥","t":"Knowledge, action, and the actor are also of three kinds, depending on the three qualities of nature. Listen to their differences."},{"ref":"18.20","s":"सर्वभूतेषु येनैकं भावमव्ययमीक्षते ।\nअविभक्तं विभक्तेषु तज्ज्ञानं विद्धि सात्त्विकम् ॥ २० ॥","t":"Knowledge that sees a single, unchanging reality in all living beings—undivided among the divided—is pure (Sattvic) knowledge."},{"ref":"18.21","s":"पृथक्त्वेन तु यज्ज्ञानं नानाभावान्पृथग्विधान् ।\nवेत्ति सर्वेषु भूतेषु तज्ज्ञानं विद्धि राजसम् ॥ २१ ॥","t":"Knowledge that sees all living beings as separate, different entities—judging them based on their outward variety—is passionate (Rajasic) knowledge."},{"ref":"18.22","s":"यत्तु कृत्स्नवदेकस्मिन्कार्ये सक्तमहैतुकम् ।\nअतत्त्वार्थवदल्पं च तत्तामसमुदाहृतम् ॥ २२ ॥","t":"Knowledge that clings to a single, small result as if it were the whole truth—without any logic or understanding—is dull (Tamasic) knowledge."},{"ref":"18.23","s":"नियतं सङ्गरहितमरागद्वेषतः कृतम् ।\nअफलप्रेप्सुना कर्म यत्तत्सात्त्विकमुच्यते ॥ २३ ॥","t":"Action that is necessary, performed without attachment, and without like or dislike by someone who doesn't want a reward, is pure (Sattvic)."},{"ref":"18.24","s":"यत्तु कामेप्सुना कर्म साहङ्कारेण वा पुनः ।\nक्रियते बहुलायासं तद्राजसमुदाहृतम् ॥ २४ ॥","t":"Action that is done with great effort, driven by selfish desire and ego, is called passionate (Rajasic)."},{"ref":"18.25","s":"अनुबन्धं क्षयं हिंसामनपेक्ष्य च पौरुषम् ।\nमोहादारभ्यते कर्म यत्तत्तामसमुच्यते ॥ २५ ॥","t":"Action undertaken out of confusion, ignoring the consequences, the potential for loss, harm to others, and one's own capability, is called dull (Tamasic)."},{"ref":"18.26","s":"मुक्तसङ्गोऽनहंवादी धृत्युत्साहसमन्वितः ।\nसिद्ध्यसिद्ध्योर्निर्विकारः कर्ता सात्त्विक उच्यते ॥ २६ ॥","t":"An actor who is free from attachment, who doesn't say 'I am great,' who is firm and enthusiastic, and remains the same in success or failure, is pure (Sattvic)."},{"ref":"18.27","s":"रागी कर्मफलप्रेप्सुर्लुब्धो हिंसात्मकोऽशुचिः ।\nहर्षशोकान्वितः कर्ता राजसः परिकीर्तितः ॥ २७ ॥","t":"An actor who is passionate, greedy for results, violent, impure, and easily moved by joy or sorrow, is called passionate (Rajasic)."},{"ref":"18.28","s":"अयुक्तः प्राकृतः स्तब्धः शठो नैष्कृतिकोऽलसः ।\nविषादी दीर्घसूत्री च कर्ता तामस उच्यते ॥ २८ ॥","t":"An actor who is undisciplined, vulgar, stubborn, deceitful, malicious, lazy, depressed, and slow to act, is called dull (Tamasic)."},{"ref":"18.29","s":"बुद्धेर्भेदं धृतेश्चैव गुणतस्त्रिविधं शृणु ।\nप्रोच्यमानमशेषेण पृथक्त्वेन धनञ्जय ॥ २९ ॥","t":"Now listen to the three kinds of discernment (Buddhi) and firmness (Dhriti), Arjuna, explained entirely according to the three qualities."},{"ref":"18.30","s":"प्रवृत्तिं च निवृत्तिं च कार्याकार्ये भयाभये ।\nबन्धं मोक्षं च या वेत्ति बुद्धिः सा पार्थ सात्त्विकी ॥ ३० ॥","t":"Logic that knows when to act and when to stop, what is duty and what is not, what to fear and what not to fear, and what is bondage and what is freedom—that is pure (Sattvic) logic."},{"ref":"18.31","s":"यया धर्ममधर्मं च कार्यं चाकार्यमेव च ।\nअयथावत्प्रजानाति बुद्धिः सा पार्थ राजसी ॥ ३१ ॥","t":"Logic that has a confused understanding of duty and injustice, and of what should be done or avoided—that is passionate (Rajasic) logic."},{"ref":"18.32","s":"अधर्मं धर्ममिति या मन्यते तमसावृता ।\nसर्वार्थान्विपरीतांश्च बुद्धिः सा पार्थ तामसी ॥ ३२ ॥","t":"Logic that is covered in darkness and thinks injustice is justice, and sees everything in a backward way—that is dull (Tamasic) logic."},{"ref":"18.33","s":"धृत्या यया धारयते मनःप्राणेन्द्रियक्रियाः ।\nयोगेनाव्यभिचारिण्या धृतिः सा पार्थ सात्त्विकी ॥ ३३ ॥","t":"The unswerving firmness by which one controls the mind, life-force, and senses through Yoga is pure (Sattvic) firmness."},{"ref":"18.34","s":"यया तु धर्मकामार्थान्धृत्या धारयतेऽर्जुन ।\nप्रसङ्गेन फलाकाङ्क्षी धृतिः सा पार्थ राजसी ॥ ३४ ॥","t":"But the firmness by which one holds onto duty, desire, and wealth out of attachment and greed for results—that is passionate (Rajasic) firmness."},{"ref":"18.35","s":"यया स्वप्नं भयं शोकं विषादं मदमेव च ।\nन विमुञ्चति दुर्मेधा धृतिः सा पार्थ तामसी ॥ ३५ ॥","t":"The firmness by which a fool refuses to give up sleep, fear, grief, depression, and arrogance—that is dull (Tamasic) firmness."},{"ref":"18.36","s":"सुखं त्विदानीं त्रिविधं शृणु मे भरतर्षभ ।\nअभ्यासाद्रमते यत्र दुःखान्तं च निगच्छति ॥ ३६ ॥","t":"Now listen to the three kinds of happiness, Arjuna. Through practice, one finds joy in this and reaches the end of all sorrow."},{"ref":"18.37","s":"यत्तदग्रे विषमिव परिणामेऽमृतोपमम् ।\nतत्सुखं सात्त्विकं प्रोक्तमात्मबुद्धिप्रसादजम् ॥ ३७ ॥","t":"Happiness that feels like poison at first but ends like nectar—born from the clarity of one's own intellect—is called pure (Sattvic)."},{"ref":"18.38","s":"विषयेन्द्रियसंयोगाद्यत्तदग्रेऽमृतोपमम् ।\nपरिणामे विषमिव तत्सुखं राजसं स्मृतम् ॥ ३८ ॥","t":"Happiness that comes from the senses meeting their objects—which feels like nectar at first but ends like poison—is called passionate (Rajasic)."},{"ref":"18.39","s":"यदग्रे चानुबन्धे च सुखं मोहनमात्मनः ।\nनिद्रालस्यप्रमादोत्थं तत्तामसमुदाहृतम् ॥ ३९ ॥","t":"Happiness that confuses the soul from start to finish—arising from sleep, laziness, and negligence—is called dull (Tamasic)."},{"ref":"18.40","s":"न तदस्ति पृथिव्यां वा दिवि देवेषु वा पुनः ।\nसत्त्वं प्रकृतिजैर्मुक्तं यदेभिः स्यात्त्रिभिर्गुणैः ॥ ४० ॥","t":"There is no being on earth or even among the gods in heaven who is free from these three qualities born of nature."},{"ref":"18.41","s":"ब्राह्मणक्षत्रियविशां शूद्राणां च परन्तप ।\nकर्माणि प्रविभक्तानि स्वभावप्रभवैर्गुणैः ॥ ४१ ॥","t":"The duties of thinkers, leaders, providers, and service-workers are distributed based on the qualities (Gunas) born of their own inherent nature, Arjuna."},{"ref":"18.42","s":"शमो दमस्तपः शौचं क्षान्तिरार्जवमेव च ।\nज्ञानं विज्ञानमास्तिक्यं ब्रह्मकर्म स्वभावजम् ॥ ४२ ॥","t":"Mental peace, self-control, discipline, purity, patience, honesty, knowledge, realization, and trust—these are the natural duties of a thinker (Brahmin)."},{"ref":"18.43","s":"शौर्यं तेजो धृतिर्दाक्ष्यं युद्धे चाप्यपलायनम् ।\nदानमीश्वरभावश्च क्षात्रं कर्म स्वभावजम् ॥ ४३ ॥","t":"Bravery, vigor, firmness, skill, not running away from battle, generosity, and a natural sense of leadership—these are the duties of a leader (Kshatriya)."},{"ref":"18.44","s":"कृषिगौरक्ष्यवाणिज्यं वैश्यकर्म स्वभावजम् ।\nपरिचर्यात्मकं कर्म शूद्रस्यापि स्वभावजम् ॥ ४४ ॥","t":"Agriculture, trade, and business are the duties of a provider (Vaishya). Work that consists of support and service is the duty of a worker (Shudra)."},{"ref":"18.45","s":"स्वे स्वे कर्मण्यभिरतः संसिद्धिं लभते नरः ।\nस्वकर्मनिरतः सिद्धिं यथा विन्दति तच्छृणु ॥ ४५ ॥","t":"By being dedicated to their own specific duty, a person reaches perfection. Listen to how one reaches perfection through their own work."},{"ref":"18.46","s":"यतः प्रवृत्तिर्भूतानां येन सर्वमिदं ततम् ।\nस्वकर्मणा तमभ्यर्च्य सिद्धिं विन्दति मानवः ॥ ४६ ॥","t":"By worshipping the Source of all beings—who spreads through everything—through the performance of one's own duty, a person finds perfection."},{"ref":"18.47","s":"श्रेयान्स्वधर्मो विगुणः परधर्मात्स्वनुष्ठितात् ।\nस्वभावनियतं कर्म कुर्वन्नाप्नोति किल्बिषम् ॥ ४७ ॥","t":"It is better to do your own duty, even if you do it imperfectly, than to do someone else's duty perfectly. By doing the work that matches your nature, you incur no negativity."},{"ref":"18.48","s":"सहजं कर्म कौन्तेय सदोषमपि न त्यजेत् ।\nसर्वारम्भा हि दोषेण धूमेनाग्निरिवावृताः ॥ ४८ ॥","t":"One should not give up the work born of their own nature, even if it has flaws. All actions are surrounded by flaws, just as fire is surrounded by smoke."},{"ref":"18.49","s":"असक्तबुद्धिः सर्वत्र जितात्मा विगतस्पृहः ।\nनैष्कर्म्यसिद्धिं परमां संन्यासेनाधिगच्छति ॥ ४९ ॥","t":"With an unattached intellect everywhere, having mastered the self and with desires gone, one reaches the supreme perfection of 'Actionlessness' through renunciation."},{"ref":"18.50","s":"सिद्धिं प्राप्तो यथा ब्रह्म तथाप्नोति निबोध मे ।\nसमासेनैव कौन्तेय निष्ठा ज्ञानस्य या परा ॥ ५० ॥","t":"Learn from Me briefly, Arjuna, how one who has reached this perfection also reaches the Absolute—which is the highest peak of knowledge."},{"ref":"18.51","s":"बुद्ध्या विशुद्धया युक्तो धृत्यात्मानं नियम्य च ।\nशब्दादीन्विषयांस्त्यक्त्वा रागद्वेषौ व्युदस्य च ॥ ५१ ॥","t":"Possessing a purified intellect, controlling the self with firmness, letting go of sensory noise, and casting aside both like and dislike..."},{"ref":"18.52","s":"विविक्तसेवी लघ्वाशी यतवाक्कायमानसः ।\nध्यानयोगपरो नित्यं वैराग्यं समुपाश्रितः ॥ ५२ ॥","t":"Seeking solitude, eating lightly, with speech, body, and mind under control, constantly practicing meditation and grounded in detachment..."},{"ref":"18.53","s":"अहङ्कारं बलं दर्पं कामं क्रोधं परिग्रहम् ।\nविमुच्य निर्ममः शान्तो ब्रह्मभूयाय कल्पते ॥ ५३ ॥","t":"Having given up ego, power, arrogance, desire, anger, and the need to own things—free from 'mine' and peaceful—one is fit to be the Absolute."},{"ref":"18.54","s":"ब्रह्मभूतः प्रसन्नात्मा न शोचति न काङ्क्षति ।\nसमः सर्वेषु भूतेषु मद्भक्तिं लभते परामम् ॥ ५४ ॥","t":"Having become the Absolute, with a peaceful self, one neither grieves nor craves. Being equal toward all living beings, one reaches supreme devotion to Me."},{"ref":"18.55","s":"भक्त्या मामभिजानाति यावान्यश्चास्मि तत्त्वतः ।\nततो मां तत्त्वतो ज्ञात्वा विशते तदनन्तरम् ॥ ५५ ॥","t":"Through devotion, one truly understands Me—how great I am and who I am in truth. Then, knowing Me in truth, they immediately enter into Me."},{"ref":"18.56","s":"सर्वकर्माण्यपि सदा कुर्वाणो मद्व्यपाश्रयः ।\nमत्प्रसादादवाप्नोति शाश्वतं पदमव्ययम् ॥ ५६ ॥","t":"Even while constantly performing all types of actions, if a person takes refuge in Me, they reach the eternal and unchanging state by My grace."},{"ref":"18.57","s":"चेतसा सर्वकर्माणि मयि संन्यस्य मत्परः ।\nबुद्धियोगमुपाश्रित्य मच्चित्तः सततं भव ॥ ५७ ॥","t":"Mentally surrendering all actions to Me, holding Me as the highest goal, and using the Yoga of discernment, fix your mind constantly on Me."},{"ref":"18.58","s":"मच्चित्तः सर्वदुर्गाणि मत्प्रसादात्तरिष्यसि ।\nअथ चेत्त्वमहङ्कारान्न श्रोष्यसि विनङ्क्ष्यसि ॥ ५८ ॥","t":"With your mind fixed on Me, you will overcome all obstacles by My grace. But if you refuse to listen because of your ego, you will be lost."},{"ref":"18.59","s":"यदहङ्कारमाश्रित्य न योत्स्य इति मन्यसे ।\nमिथ्यैष व्यवसायस्ते प्रकृतिस्त्वां नियोक्ष्यति ॥ ५९ ॥","t":"If, out of ego, you think 'I will not fight,' your resolution is useless. Your own nature will force you to act."},{"ref":"18.60","s":"स्वभावजेन कौन्तेय निबद्धः स्वेन कर्मणा ।\nकर्तुं नेच्छसि यन्मोहात्करिष्यस्यवशोऽपि तत् ॥ ६० ॥","t":"Bound by your own past actions born of your nature, you will end up doing the very thing you are trying to avoid out of confusion."},{"ref":"18.61","s":"ईश्वरः सर्वभूतानां हृद्देशेऽर्जुन तिष्ठति ।\nभ्रामयन्सर्वभूतानि यन्त्रारूढानि मायया ॥ ६१ ॥","t":"The Lord lives in the heart of every being, Arjuna, causing all beings to turn around by His mysterious power, as if they were mounted on a machine."},{"ref":"18.62","s":"तमेव शरणं गच्छ सर्वभावेन भारत ।\nतत्प्रसादात्परां शान्तिं स्थानं प्राप्स्यसि शाश्वतम् ॥ ६२ ॥","t":"Seek refuge in Him alone with your whole being, Arjuna. By His grace, you will find supreme peace and an eternal home."},{"ref":"18.63","s":"इति ते ज्ञानमाख्यातं गुह्याद्गुह्यतरं मया ।\nविमृश्यैतदशेषेण यथेच्छसि तथा कुरु ॥ ६३ ॥","t":"Thus, I have shared with you the most secret of all knowledge. Reflect on it deeply and completely, and then do whatever you wish."},{"ref":"18.64","s":"सर्वगुह्यतमं भूयः शृणु मे परमं वचः ।\nइष्टोऽसि मे दृढमिति ततो वक्ष्यामि ते हितम् ॥ ६४ ॥","t":"Hear again my supreme word—the deepest secret of all. Because you are so dear to Me, I am telling you this for your own good."},{"ref":"18.65","s":"मन्मना भव मद्भक्तो मद्याजी मां नमस्कुरु ।\nमामेवैष्यसि सत्यं ते प्रतिजाने प्रियोऽसि मे ॥ ६५ ॥","t":"Fix your mind on Me, be devoted to Me, work for Me, and bow down to Me. You will certainly come to Me; I promise you this, because you are dear to Me."},{"ref":"18.66","s":"सर्वधर्मान्परित्यज्य मामेकं शरणं व्रज ।\nअहं त्वां सर्वपापेभ्यो मोक्षयिष्यामि मा शुचः ॥ ६६ ॥","t":"Give up all other 'Dharmas' (rules/paths) and take refuge in Me alone. I will liberate you from all mistakes and negativity; do not grieve."},{"ref":"18.67","s":"इदं ते नातपस्काय नाभक्ताय कदाचन ।\nन चाशुश्रूषवे वाच्यं न च मां योऽभ्यसूयति ॥ ६७ ॥","t":"This secret should never be shared with someone who lacks discipline, who is not devoted, who doesn't want to learn, or who speaks ill of Me."},{"ref":"18.68","s":"य इमं परमं गुह्यं मद्भक्तेष्वभिधास्यति ।\nभक्तिं मयि परां कृत्वा मामेवैष्यत्यसंशयः ॥ ६८ ॥","t":"Anyone who shares this supreme secret among My devotees, showing pure devotion to Me, will undoubtedly reach Me."},{"ref":"18.69","s":"न च तस्मान्मनुष्येषु कश्चिन्मे प्रियकृत्तमः ।\nभविता न च मे तस्मादन्यः प्रियतरो भुवि ॥ ६९ ॥","t":"Among all humans, there is no one who does a more pleasing service to Me than this, and no one on earth will be dearer to Me."},{"ref":"18.70","s":"अध्येष्यते च य इमं धर्म्यं संवादमावयोः ।\nज्ञानयज्ञेन तेनाहमिष्टः स्यामिति मे मतिः ॥ ७० ॥","t":"And anyone who studies this sacred dialogue between us—I consider that person to have worshipped Me through the 'Sacrifice of Knowledge.'"},{"ref":"18.71","s":"श्रद्धावाननसूयश्च शृणुयादपि यो नरः ।\nसोऽपि मुक्तः शुभाँल्लोकान्प्राप्नुयात्पुण्यकर्मणाम् ॥ ७१ ॥","t":"Even a person who simply listens to this with faith and without judgment will be freed and reach the happy worlds of the righteous."},{"ref":"18.72","s":"कच्चिदेतच्छ्रुतं पार्थ त्वयैकाग्रेण चेतसा ।\nकच्चिदज्ञानसम्मोहः प्रनष्टस्ते धनञ्जय ॥ ७२ ॥","t":"Have you heard this with a one-pointed mind, Arjuna? Has your confusion born of ignorance been destroyed?"},{"ref":"18.73","s":"अर्जुन उवाच ।\nनष्टो मोहः स्मृतिर्लब्धा त्वत्प्रसादान्मयाच्युत ।\nस्थितोऽस्मि गतसन्देहः करिष्ये वचनं तव ॥ ७३ ॥","t":"Arjuna said: My confusion is gone! I have regained my clarity through Your grace. I stand firm, my doubts are destroyed, and I will act according to Your word."},{"ref":"18.74","s":"सञ्जय उवाच ।\nइत्यहं वासुदेवस्य पार्थस्य च महात्मनः ।\nसंवादमिममश्रौषमद्भुतं रोमहर्षणम् ॥ ७४ ॥","t":"Sanjaya said: Thus I have heard this wonderful and hair-raising dialogue between Krishna and the great-souled Arjuna."},{"ref":"18.75","s":"व्यासप्रसादाच्छ्रुतवानेतद्गुह्यमहं परम् ।\nयोगं योगेश्वरात्कृष्णात्साक्षात्कथयतः स्वयम् ॥ ७५ ॥","t":"By the grace of the sage Vyasa, I have heard this supreme secret of Yoga directly from Krishna, the Lord of Yoga, as He spoke it Himself."},{"ref":"18.76","s":"राजन्संस्मृत्य संस्मृत्य संवादमिममद्भुतम् ।\nकेशवार्जुनयोः पुण्यं हृष्यामि च मुहुर्मुहुः ॥ ७६ ॥","t":"O King, as I remember this wonderful and holy dialogue over and over again, I rejoice again and again."},{"ref":"18.77","s":"तच्च संस्मृत्य संस्मृत्य रूपमत्यद्भुतं हरेः ।\nविस्मयो मे महान्राजन्हृष्यामि च पुनः पुनः ॥ ७७ ॥","t":"And as I remember that exceedingly wonderful form of Krishna, my amazement is great and I rejoice over and over."},{"ref":"18.78","s":"यत्र योगेश्वरः कृष्णो यत्र पार्थो धनुर्धरः ।\nतत्र श्रीर्विजयो भूतिर्ध्रुवा नीतिर्मतिर्मम ॥ ७८ ॥","t":"Wherever Krishna, the master of Yoga, and Arjuna, the great archer, are together — there you will find prosperity, victory, abundance, and unwavering justice. This is my firm conviction."}];
